Cambodia and Singapore continue to strengthen and expand cooperation in the fields of politics, economy, trade and security (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Singapore have announced to continue to strengthen and expand cooperation in the fields of politics, economy, trade, defense and security. Energy and tourism.
In the political sphere, the two leaders noted the importance and benefits of reorganizing political dialogue and agreed to push for a second political dialogue between Cambodia and Singapore in the near future.
In the fields of trade and economy, the two leaders agreed to promote better relations, encouraging cooperation between relevant ministries and institutions of the two countries to implement initiatives and plans. Specific actions.
The two leaders also agreed to boost defense and security cooperation, which contributes to the fight against cybercrime, online gambling and other laws.
Regarding energy security, the Prime Minister informed the Prime Minister of Singapore that during the meeting with the Prime Minister of Malaysia on 27 February, the Malaysian side recently agreed and supported the connection of the submarine power grid. Network for connecting electricity from Laos to Singapore via Cambodia.
Regarding tourism cooperation, the Prime Minister informed the Prime Minister of Singapore that Cambodia has recently launched a program to visit Siem Reap 2024, the launch of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport and the establishment of a promotion mechanism. Tourism in Cambodia with the participation of the private sector.
