The Maldives Defense Ministry announced that it had signed an agreement with Beijing on Monday night on Chinese military assistance. According to a statement from the Maldives Defense Ministry, the signing of the military agreement aims to strengthen bilateral ties, but did not provide further details.
(Kampong Chhnang): General Prof. Ek Monosen, President of the Police Academy of Cambodia, on behalf of His Excellency Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on the afternoon of March 4, 2024, closed the training course for the ninth generation of administrative police officers. National Police, Zone 6, Kampong Chhnang Province, with the participation of the leaders of the National Police School, Deputy Commissioners from 5 provinces, and many trainees as police officers.
Major General Tong An, Director of the National Police School, Zone 6, Kampong Chhnang Province, said that 137 administrative police officers who studied in this training course were from Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Speu, Kandal, Kampong Thom and Phnom Penh.
During the study stay, all police students participated in the proper observance of the school's discipline, working hard to learn the skills with good results that will be able to be applied at their local level better.
The General instructed the administrative police officers who have received this training to apply their new knowledge, experience and skills for the benefit of the unit and the society and to provide public services to the local people with values and virtues.
On that occasion, General Prof. Ek Monosen also honored to present the education certificates to the police officers of the Administration Post who won the study. More than 100 leaders and members of the Candlelight Party from Pursat protested at the headquarters. Acting Chairman of Pursat Provincial Party, arbitrarily and without reason
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Tuesday, March 5, 2024, more than 100 leaders and members of the Candlelight Party in Pursat province came to Phnom Penh to protest in front of the candlelight party headquarters. The protest came after party leaders decided to remove Pol Vanrith from the acting chairman of the Pursat Candlelight Party for no reason.
Protesters include Pol Vannrith, currently the second deputy chief of Pursat's Roleap commune, from the Candlelight Party, as well as a commune / sangkat councilor in Pursat province, a senior member of the Candlelight Party. By commune / sangkat. Apart from that, they are all active members of the Candlelight Party in Pursat province.
The leaders as well as the members of the Candlelight Party from Pursat province expressed their anger and dissatisfaction with the decision of the candlelight party leaders. Protesters allege that the leaders of the Candlelight Party nominate themselves as respecters and promoters of democracy, but that the party's internal affairs are not democratic, meaning that they want to withdraw or arbitrarily place them without giving party members a chance. Hear nothing.
Mr. Pol Vanrith expressed his regret over the decision of the leaders of the Candlelight Party because he had sacrificed his physical strength, mental strength and wealth to help the party for many years. Finally, the party leadership resigned without giving any reason. The NEC decided to officially recognize the candidates elected as senators in all eight regions in the 5th legislative election.
It should be noted that this morning, March 5, 2024, the NEC announced the official results of the 5th Senate election, which was held on February 25, 2024, in which the Cambodian People's Party. The incumbent succeeded in controlling almost all the seats in the Senate.
In the 5th legislative election, four political parties competed, with the CPP winning 55 seats and the Khmer Will party winning three. Separately, FUNCINPEC and the National Forces Party, which also contested, did not win seats.
The Senate for the fifth term has 62 members, two of whom are nominated by the King, two are elected by the National Assembly by a majority vote, and 58 are elected by universal suffrage. Commune / Sangkat Councilors and National Assembly members in office. Ministry of Culture: Cambodia wants to have an MOU with Britain on preventing the illegal movement of artifacts
(Phnom Penh): In order to strengthen cooperation and cultural relations, the Royal Government of Cambodia has requested the British Government to consider the possibility of signing a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) on the prevention of the illegal movement of antiquities. A spokesman for the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts told Fresh News.
On that occasion, the two senior leaders met to discuss additional work, focusing on some important points such as:
* 1: Examine the possibility of signing a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) on preventing the illegal movement of antiquities.
* 2: Facilitate the sending of experts to help preserve gold collections and provide advice on how to properly organize such collections in accordance with technical standards, namely to prevent corrosion and damage from moisture. During the exhibition
Sum Mab, spokesman for the Ministry of Culture, stated that "this memorandum is just a request from the Cambodian side to the British side to examine the possibility of further bilateral signing in the future." This work will take a long time, so if any more positive news, the Ministry will continue to inform the public.
Since 1996, the museum has received 154 artifacts, including 136 pieces of jewelry. This is according to Mr. Chhay Visoth, director of the museum department and a member of the spokesperson of the Ministry of Culture.
