Siem Reap Provincial Administration Announces Car Fire in Front of Angkor Wat
(Phnom Penh): The Siem Reap Provincial Administration issued a press release on the case of a house fire on a 45-seat tourist car at the parking lot in front of Angkor Wat temple on the morning of March 5, 2024 at 05:50.
The accident did not cause any injuries to the tourists, damaging three vehicles, including two 45-seater cars and one 24-seater car, and injuring two people.
The provincial administration urges the national and international media and the people to refrain from disseminating information based on any conclusions or personal opinions that have no clear basis or intention to incite harm to security, order and socio-economy leading to accountability. Before the law.
(Preah Sihanouk): Residents of Veal Meas Village, Veal Renh Commune, Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province will receive the achievement of 650 meters of reinforced concrete road, 2024 commune fund project, which opened in the afternoon of March 4. 2024 at Veal Rinh Commune Hall.
The bidding meeting was chaired by Mr. Kheang Phearum, Director of Planning and Investment of Sihanoukville Provincial Hall, Mr. Khov Thav Nith, Veal Rinh Commune Chief, and was attended by the Provincial Technical Working Group, Commune Procurement Committee, Construction Company and For many journalists, the bidding meeting went smoothly, procedurally and transparently.
After opening a transparent bid, the result is as follows:
Two concrete roads, 650 meters long, 5 meters wide, 0.15 meters high, 1 sign, estimated value 339,767,800 Riels, after submitting the project bid to Sorn Nget, including 8 companies participated in the bidding. Fees.
After the opening ceremony, the Director of the Provincial Investment Planning Office said that in order to solve the difficulties for the local people, the Commune / Sangkat Development Fund Project 2024 has launched a series of bids in communes throughout Sihanoukville. Completed the project and achieved many concrete roads in the past.
Mr. Kheang Phearum emphasized that after receiving the successful bid, he instructed all companies to build the road according to the design standards to be good and durable for the people and ask the local authorities. Sangkats need to address the impacts of the people peacefully so that the process of road construction can run smoothly and quickly so that the people can use it in a timely manner.
Veal Rinh commune chief said that in Veal Rinh commune, compared to 2023, in 2024, the concrete road will be longer than before, which is up to 650 meters long, and there are many companies that participated in the bidding. The price this afternoon will be transparent and he hopes that the company that received the project will comply with the technical contract of the team.
He said that, of course, when the project starts, it will inevitably affect the interests of the people, but as the head of the commune procurement team, he will explain to the people the impact not to be offended to get. The road is clean and easy to navigate, of course, we have to sacrifice a few crops, stone pillars, fences and all the impacts that are affected.
(Phnom Penh): Addressing the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting (ADMM) and related meetings in 2024 in Laos, Deputy Prime Minister Gen. Tea Seiha said that geopolitical divisions are contributing factors. Global insecurity triggers new conflicts and makes finding solutions more difficult.
The ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting 2024 was held under the theme "ASEAN Together for Peace, Security and Resilience."
"Rising geopolitical tensions will also affect our joint ability to respond jointly to the major challenges we may face," said Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha. "In this regard, we need to strengthen joint efforts to find multilateral solutions and address the geopolitical dilemma."
In addition, the Deputy Prime Minister expressed his belief that ASEAN is suitable as a bridge to help on that issue. In particular, the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting (ADMM-Plus) is the only forum where the major powers join military cooperation and practical cooperation together to address common challenges.
At the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting, the ASEAN Defense Ministers exchanged views on ASEAN's external relations with external partners, consideration for strengthening ASEAN unity and centralization, and strengthening Effective cooperation under the existing mechanism of the ASEAN Defense Ministers 'Meeting (ADMM) and the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting Plus (ADMM-Plus).
At the same time, the ASEAN Defense Ministers exchanged views on regional and international issues of common interest and concern.
A number of external partners have continued to apply for observers from the ADMM-Plus Working Group due to the success of this observation program in the past round. And some countries have even applied for full ADMM-Plus membership.
Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha emphasized: "This growing interest is a testament to the ADMM and ADMM plus an effective platform for joint efforts to promote strategic trust building and defense cooperation for peace, security and stability." "Local resilience."
As Co-Chair of the IT Security Expert Working Group, Cambodia will work with Australia and all ADMM-Plus countries to promote information security cooperation, incorporating the Agenda for Women, Peace and Security and Climate Change. In the work program of the expert team.
The Minister of Defense of Cambodia expressed the hope that there will be an opportunity to organize joint exercises with any professional team to increase the efficiency of inter-operational capabilities and to raise awareness of information technology security among our troops.
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, said that due to the confidence of investors in the leadership of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has increased investment projects in Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol added, "This increase shows the confidence of investors in the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Investors believe in peace, order, security, and political stability." "Macroeconomic stability If there is no political stability, macroeconomic stability, peace and order, then Cambodia can not attract investment."
The Deputy Prime Minister continued that the investors really expressed their confidence in the leadership of Samdech Hun Manet, as in Japan, Cambodia held a seminar in Japan to promote investment in Cambodia with the participation of more than a dozen companies. The 100 participating companies, including 25 Japanese companies, have expressed interest in investing in Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol added that the interest of foreign investors due to peace, macroeconomic stability and political stability, another factor is Cambodia in the middle of the Mekong sub-region. In that, the investment law in Cambodia also has a lot of good incentives for investors who want to meet the Royal Government or members of the Royal Government is easy just by phone or use many other communication systems.
Another factor is that Cambodia has established 15 technical working groups with co-chairs from the private sector and the Royal Government to solve the problems that the private sector has in case we can not solve this problem, we will go to the forum of the Royal Government and the private sector. Led by President Hun Manet, these are the factors that make investors see that Cambodia can solve investors' problems if any problems occur.
Cambodia congratulates Greece on making positive progress towards achieving the goals of Article 4 of the Convention on Mine Action
(Switzerland): On March 4, 2024, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, President of the 2024 Ottawa Convention, met with Ioannis GHIKAS, Representative of the Permanent Mission of Greece to the United Nations and other international organizations in Geneva to discuss About the current situation and progress of demining in Greece stockpiles in accordance with the mandate of the Convention and the zoning for further cooperation and support.
Dr. Ly Thuch congratulated Ioannis GHIKAS on his appointment as the new Permanent Representative of Greece to the United Nations in Geneva and congratulated Greece on its positive progress. Objectives under Article 4 of the Convention on the Destruction of Mine Action.
Greece has declared its political will to destroy all mines in accordance with Article 4 of the Convention, but that destruction must go through a procedure and take time. Greece hired a Croatian company to transport its stockpiles of mines to Croatia and destroy them there.
Since Greece became a party to the Ottawa Convention in 2004, Greece has no longer been affected by landmines and has destroyed more than 1.2 million stockpiles. More than 343,000 more.
Cambodian Mine Authority meets with representatives of the Permanent Mission of Ukraine to the United Nations and other international organizations in Geneva
The meeting was attended by representatives of the member countries of the Compliance Commission, including Cambodia, Germany, Norway and Peru, as well as the Ottawa Convention Implementation Support Unit (ISU-APMBC).
The meeting continued to promote efforts to support demining in Ukraine by strengthening cooperation, transparency, standards and principles of the Convention to restore the spirit of cooperation under the Convention on Mine Action against Persons. At the same time, Ukraine has shown its commitment to global peace, security and humanity by ratifying many international treaties beyond the Ottawa Convention.
Mr. Khuong Sreng thanked for the dedication of teachers in human resource development to continue to develop the country to grow further
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, thanked the dedication of teachers in accordance with the pentagonal strategy of the Royal Government led by Samdech Mahavor President Hun Manet in developing human resources to continue to develop the country. .
Mr. Khuong Sreng said this at the closing ceremony of the meeting to evaluate the results of education, youth and sports in Phnom Penh for the academic year 2022-2023 and the work direction for the academic year 2023-2024 on the morning of March 5, 2024 at the Department of Education, Youth and Phnom Penh Sports.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that the education sector today is recognized internationally, that is, Cambodia can do it, we have now achieved great success in this field of education, but we must not forget about this success by working together. Make education more successful and make Cambodia achieve its vision of a high middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050.
At the same time, he asked teachers to believe in the leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister, that even our neighbors recognize the progress in all areas of our country.
He also said that it is difficult for private schools to find teachers now because some private teachers have turned to teaching in public schools due to the high salaries of public schools and the ability to teach part-time. He said that the schools in Phnom Penh are clean, the environment is good and the toilets are also good.
He also urged all teachers to participate in the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes. In connection with this case, we have formed a telegram between the authorities, the competent forces and the teachers in the educational institutions, that is, when there is a problem, we solve it immediately.
Mr. Khuong Sreng asked teachers to continue their joint efforts to ensure that there are no drugs in schools, while now there are no drugs in schools in Phnom Penh.
He also asked teachers to dedicate more to the pentagonal strategy of the Royal Government led by His Excellency Hun Manet in the development of human resources, without human resources, we can not develop the country to grow. Currently, the labor market is very competitive, which requires us to have strong human resources.
He also urged the district authorities and the competent forces of the district to participate in saluting the flag in schools, which is held twice a week. Participating in this flag salute allows the authorities as well as our law enforcement forces to promote local development as well as security issues.
