(Preah Vihear): The Department of Health of Preah Vihear Provincial Administration on March 4, 2024 celebrated the 113rd Anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8 under the theme "Women and Girls in the Digital Revolution". In the presence of Dr. Kuong Lo, Advisor of the Ministry of Health and Director of the Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department, as well as the leaders of the civil service of the Department of Health, as well as women in the health sector throughout the province.
On the occasion of the 113rd Anniversary of International Women's Day, March 8, 2024, Mr. Kuong Lo and all male civil servants of Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department would like to congratulate and wish all female civil servants in Provincial health departments, as well as all sisters around the world.
Dr. Kuong Lo also stated that the participation of women at all levels is a value to ensure that every citizen has full rights and opportunities to have the choice of representation and to actively participate in all areas to achieve Achieve priority tasks effectively.
Mr. Kuong Lo also stressed the need for participation in supporting and implementing gender work and empowering women to create a conducive environment and opportunities for women and girls to continue to fully participate in the exercise of their rights and benefits. In a peaceful and prosperous society in the digital age.
At the same time, on the occasion of celebrating the 113rd anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8, Mr. Kuong Lo also encouraged all women in the Health Department of Preah Vihear Provincial Administration to study hard, especially new things to walk. Keep this technology up to date.
He said that today women have the same rights as men, but women also need to strengthen their capacity to get the same opportunities as other men.
In addition to congratulating the female civil servants in the Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department, Mr. Kuong Lo also led a team to congratulate the provincial women leaders and Mrs. Chea, former director of the Provincial Health Department at home.
