Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet has openly welcomed Australian investment with excellent hospitality (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet has openly welcomed Australian investment with excellent hospitality. President Hun Manet made this announcement during a speech at the Australia-Cambodia Business Forum in Melbourne on March 5, 2024.
President Hun Manet said that Cambodia's commitment to sustainable energy presents many lucrative opportunities for Australian investors. With the rich potential of solar and hydropower potential and the ambitious goals set out in the 2022-2040 Energy Development Master Plan, Cambodia is a good market for Australian professionals.
According to Hun Manet, for the past three decades, Australia has always been a major investor in Cambodia. Australia's business interests in Cambodia focus on a wide range of areas, including education, food and beverage services, financial services, mining and resources, hospitality and clothing resources. Australian investment in Cambodia is not just a strategic decision, it is an investment in the future growth of both countries.
"Cambodia's economic growth trajectory, along with our strategic location in the Indo-Pacific region, presents many opportunities for Australian businesses and investors," he said. At the same time, Australian investment in Cambodia has contributed significantly to the country's job creation and sustainable economic growth.
