(Phnom Penh): General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, represented by Mr. Abhisandiband Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, this morning, March 5, 2024, presided over the 113th Anniversary of International Women's Day, March 8, 2024. The song "Women and girls in the digital revolution" with the participation of the female police force under the National Police.
General Sar Thet stated that every year, Cambodia organizes the International Women's Day March 8 campaign to commemorate the struggle for equal rights and freedoms and to reflect on progress, achievements, challenges, commitments and positive measures in promoting Gender equality and empowerment of all women and girls.
Organizing a campaign to celebrate the International Women's Day on March 8, the 113th anniversary in 2024 under the theme "Women and Girls in the Digital Revolution" in order to highlight the potential and necessity of promoting women's participation and representation and Girls in the digital field, effective and secure.
According to General Sar Thet, the theme for this year is designed to respond to the context of social development in the digital age and in line with the vision outlined in the Royal Government of Cambodia's Phase I strategy. Policy framework to promote gender equality and empower women and girls.
He added that promoting the role of women and girls in the digital revolution is necessary and important in accelerating the socio-economic development of the environment. When women and girls have digital knowledge and skills, they can actively and safely participate in the digital economy and society.
The digital revolution will provide new ways for women and girls to exercise their rights, enhance their status, role, access to opportunities and choices in life, as well as improve their socio-economic status and family and access. Broader possibilities for education, professional development, employment and business.
In addition, General Sar Thet instructed and issued some instructions to the female police force, including:
* First, let all women police forces continue to maintain the noble tradition, maintain the honor as a national police force with discipline, morality, virtue and professional conscience, especially to maintain values worthy of the reputation of women as " Mother of the World »
* Second: Propose to continue to work hard to overcome all obstacles, seize the opportunity to develop their knowledge to be worthy of the women of the digital age, full of ability
* Third: Promote excellence as a wife, mother, aunt, sister or exemplary daughter in the family by educating our entire family society to participate in all social movements, respect the law, have good manners, avoid evil. Both become good citizens with honor and dignity, which is an important part in helping to promote virtue, create a warm, safe and harmonious environment in Cambodian society.
On behalf of the National Police Commissioner, the General will continue to pay close attention to the female police force by reducing the gender gap, giving priority to encouraging the promotion of positions in line with achievements and competencies in a transparent and non-discriminatory manner.
