He said that for Cambodia, women's rights have been the focus of the Cambodian government since the liberation on January 7, 1979, until the seventh mandate, in which women played an important role in supporting the economy and development. The society that made Cambodia develop as it is today.
At the same time, the Minister provided some guidelines and recommendations as follows:
1. The leadership must pay more attention to examining the composition of women and provide opportunities for women to get roles and status in each unit under the Ministry of Rural Development.
2. All departments and projects need to increase good cooperation with the gender team to promote gender perspectives and increase the participation of women in the implementation of programs and projects.
3. Gender working groups need to be gender-directed at all levels of leadership to increase awareness of the value of women's participation.
4. Departmental leaders must take care of women who are pregnant and have small children by providing favorable time for maternity leave and good child care.
5. The Gender Working Group must continue to disseminate gender perspectives to the community in order to exchange ideas among rural people, especially women, in order to take advantage of gender dividends and participate in maintaining the achievements provided by the Royal Government through various policies. In force.
6. Every woman must increase and strengthen her capacity in line with the digital revolution to contribute to the maintenance of stability, growth and development of the society.
