Zelensky: The West must have the political will to secure the necessary arms supply
(Kiev) - President Volodymyr Zelensky has called on Ukraine's Western allies to establish a political will to provide Kiev with the necessary military equipment, otherwise the world will face one of the greatest embarrassments of history. This is according to the release by Reuters on Monday, March 4, 2024.
In a fit of rage, Zelensky said in a video message that the world must "react decisively to ensure that war does not look as desperate as Vladimir Putin did." "They have to make it feel like they can guarantee for their partner what they need."
"The important thing is the political will to ensure the level of supply," Zelensky added. If not, it will be the most embarrassing page in history if even the United States or Europe loses to Iran in the form of Shaheds drones or Russian warplanes. "Ukraine is waiting for the necessary materials, especially the US decision on this issue."
Zelensky's comments come amid disagreements in the US Congress over military aid packages and other issues, as Russia is currently on the brink of war for more than two years, but the situation on the front lines is improving. Photo: Reuters Analysis: The General Assembly of China's two parliaments in 2024 will focus on challenges in terms of seeking development through practical implementation.
