The expectation of a ceasefire in Gaza on Monday, March 4, 2024, did not live up to US presidential expectations. Zhou Biden last week said he expected a ceasefire to be reached on Monday, March 4, as Egypt and Qatar actively worked with Israel and Hamas, but obstacles remained. No ceasefire agreement can be reached.
Israeli Prime Minister Netanyahu said last week that a planned infantry strike on Rafah could be postponed if a multi-week ceasefire agreement is agreed.
The failure to clarify the two requirements prompted Israel to boycott its negotiating team to Cairo, Egypt, on Sunday, undermining US President Joe Biden's expectations. The ceasefire on Monday, March 4, became a nonsense.
Why did Hamas not respond to Israel's request?
