Mr Bran Black pointed out that the Australian Business Council currently has working relationships with many countries, including ASEAN countries. In addition, the Executive Director expressed his intention to expand cooperation with Cambodia to strengthen and expand business and trade relations between Australia and Cambodia.
Samdech Hun Manet welcomed the Executive Director of the Australian Business Council and his colleagues for their courtesy and discussion. He stressed that the Royal Government of Cambodia highly values the role of the private sector in contributing to the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
The President also confirmed to the Executive Director that today's meeting is an opportunity that can encourage the private sector of Australia to understand and expand more investment in Cambodia. The Prime Minister warmly welcomed the intention of the Australian Business Council to promote cooperation between the Australian Business Council and Cambodia.
The President of the Royal Government also stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia is open to all businesses and acts as a bridge to facilitate and ensure the investment climate in Cambodia.
During the meeting, Samdech Hun Manet presented the new Cambodian investment policy and law, which encourages the private sector to invest in Cambodia, while Cambodia has linked cooperation in the region as well as other countries in the world. He through free trade agreements at both bilateral and multilateral levels.
The Prime Minister also said that the Royal Government of Cambodia pays close attention to and encourages investment in digital technology, electrical and automotive components, as well as agriculture and tourism to boost Cambodia's economic growth.
