Cintri Gets Solid Waste Collection Rights in Kampong Cham
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Ly Sovann, Governor of Kampong Cham City, on the morning of March 4, 2024, signed an agreement with Cintri Company for 10 years to collect and transport solid waste in the town of Kampong Cham.
The signing ceremony of the contract between the two parties was held as a witness by Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham and Mr. Chay Samith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment.
According to the Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Cintri Company has been well-tested for garbage collection in Kampong Cham City for one year, which is an experience for carrying out this work for a long time. But today, the Kampong Cham municipal administration signed a 10-year contract with Cintri to collect and transport solid waste in Kampong Cham.
The provincial governor confirmed that the company is responsible for collecting and transporting garbage in Kampong Cham city, while the Kampong Cham municipal administration is responsible for collecting the service fee from the back of the house and paying the service fee to the company for 1 ton of garbage worth $ 17.
The provincial governor advised the mayor of Kampong Cham to inspect other locations to collect garbage as much as possible to provide cleanliness to our city to be suitable as a city that has won three romduol flowers.
Mr. Chay Samith said that Kampong Cham is one of the leading provinces in the country in implementing Sub-Decree No. 113, that is, the Kampong Cham Municipality can afford to pay for the garbage collection service without the need for assistance from the provincial administration. And the work of the administration of Kampong Cham can be an experience for dissemination to other cities of other provinces to follow as well.
According to the mayor of Kampong Cham, the results of the work carried out in 2023 show that people throughout the city are happy with the new garbage collection service and pay more than when managed by private companies.
He said that when managed by a private company, there were 3,700 people participating in the service, but now by the end of 2023, there is an increase of 5,804 people to connect to the service. Woman sues Ministry of Justice for court case
(Phnom Penh): After losing the case at the Takeo Provincial Court until the Court of Appeal in Phnom Penh, a woman decided to apply for the intervention of Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, to order the indictment of a person named Heam Cheav Heng in Trapeang Romchek Village, Choam Chao Sangkat Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, for "breach of trust" and "fraud" in the purchase of 22 hectares of land worth more than $ 500,000 in Prey Kabas district, Takeo province.
Srun Bunnary, 59, a resident of Takhmao village, Takhmao commune, Takhmao city, Kandal province, who claimed to be a victim of fraud and breach of trust, described in an application for intervention to Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith in June In 2019, Ham Chiao Heng advised him to buy about 22 hectares of land in Prey Chambok village, Ta Yap commune, Prey Kabas district, Takeo province, saying that it was the people's dry farmland.
After handing over the full amount, he inquired about the time of registration of ownership and asked Ham Cheav Heng to deliver it to the location of the land he had previously purchased, but was denied by Ham Cheav Heng. Raise the time to do it and that it is almost always done and not delivered to the land location.
Because he demanded too much, only on June 5, 2020, Ham Chiao Heng took me to the land location in Prey Chambok village, Taing Yap commune, Prey Kabas district, Takeo province, only to find out that it was not the same place as Ham Chiao Heng. Heng used to recommend buying, not 7 km from the new airport.
It was not until 2021 that a woman named Srun Bunnary researched further and found out that the land that Ham Cheav Heng had bought from the people was state property. After finding such an anomaly, a woman named Srun Bunnary tried to contact Ham Cheav Heng by all means to ask questions and solve problems, but she found an excuse and avoided and even hung up the phone could not be contacted. To date.
Seeing the injustice through the fabricated answers of Ham Cheav Heng, Srun Bunnary decided to file a complaint for intervention from Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith, Minister of Justice.
