Samdech Hun Manet informs Cambodians in Australia and New Zealand that as long as Samdech is the Prime Minister, marijuana cultivation will not be allowed (Video inside) (Australia) Marijuana cultivation is not allowed to the Cambodian people in Australia and New Zealand, stating that as long as the Prime Minister is not allowed to grow marijuana in Cambodia.
The statement was made during a meeting with more than 1,000 Cambodians in Australia and New Zealand on the evening of March 3, 2024 in Melbourne, during a visit to Australia.
On that occasion, Samdech President reminded of the strategy to fight drugs in Cambodia, especially the implementation in the ranks of civil servants, the Armed Forces, the army, which Samdech always compared to wolves in the lake is to have a method to clean the barriers to prevent wolves. Return. Similarly, drug eradication in Cambodia is to begin with civil servants first and will move to other areas.
On the issue of marijuana, the President reiterated his decision not to allow marijuana cultivation in the past, informing Cambodians in Australia and New Zealand, stating that as long as the Prime Minister, he will not allow marijuana cultivation in Cambodia. No.
He said that in some countries, planting is allowed to serve the health sector, but in other countries, after planting, it is no longer possible to control because of the large number. Sometimes there are thieves planting in the forest and fraudulently selling through authorized channels.
The Prime Minister stressed that "even if the Cambodian marijuana business is not poor, Cambodia will only try to grow other crops such as mangoes, bananas for export rather than growing marijuana."
He added that an experience in Singapore found that of the 6,000 drug addicts, 40 per cent were addicted to marijuana under the age of 18 and eventually became addicted. Other types of drugs, so Cambodia absolutely does not allow the cultivation of marijuana.
