Hamas says there could be a ceasefire in the next 24 to 48 hours if Israel accepts the terms
A senior Hamas official told AFP on Sunday that a ceasefire could be reached in the Gaza Strip in the next 24 to 48 hours if Israel El accepts his request in ongoing negotiations.
On Saturday, March 2, a senior US official also said that Israel had agreed to most of the proposals related to the six-week ceasefire in the Gaza war, and now it is up to Hamas to release them. Hostage or not for this ceasefire to take effect.
Negotiators from Egypt, Qatar and the United States have been trying to find a ceasefire for Gaza ahead of Ramadan, the month of Muslim fasting, which could begin on March 10 or 11. Stop the Israeli military's plan to invade Rafah. But Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has warned that any ceasefire could only halt Israeli offensive operations.
