(Kampong Thom): The Kampong Svay District Administration of Kampong Thom Province celebrated the 113rd Anniversary of the International Women's Day on March 8 under the theme "Women and Girls in the Digital Revolution" at Kampong Svay District Hall on March 3, 2024. .
The ceremony was held in the presence of Ms. Khuon Khundy, Senator and Chair of the Kampong Svay District Field Team, and was attended by Ms. Lum Kuntheary, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province and Mr. Uth Vannara, Governor of Kampong Svay District, and women representatives at the district hall and From about 100 communes.
She praised the choice of the theme "Women and Girls in the Digital Revolution" as an important and correct topic in line with the development of society and in line with the strategic plan of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate. Which has decided to focus on digital technology.
She stated that the encouragement of Cambodian women and girls to be connected to digital technology will provide benefits and benefits from the development of digital technology as the core for Cambodia, women's rights have been continued by the Cambodian government since the liberation on January 7, 1979. High attention continues until the seventh mandate, as women have played an important role in supporting the economy and social development that makes Cambodia grow as it is today.
As the chair of the working group, she stressed that the celebration of Women's Rights Day is not a celebration of symbolism, but a show of respect and care for women, who are present more than men in Cambodia. Therefore, all priority activities must take into account women, otherwise any action plan or political program can not reflect the realities for development in Cambodian society.
