(Phnom Penh): Currently, the process of preparing for the Civil Servants Recruitment Examination within the framework of the Anti-Corruption Unit has been under the leadership of the Ministry of Public Function as the Chairman of the Competition Organizing Committee at the Royal University Examination Center in Phnom Penh. .
The current recruitment of officers to join the Anti-Corruption Unit will be 33 places, with a total of more than 2,000 registered candidates passing the examination on subjects related to the Criminal Code, the Criminal Procedure Code, and the Anti-Corruption Law. Corruption and other laws, including crime analysis, general knowledge, foreign languages and computers.
The competition lasts for 120 minutes from 14:00 to 16:00, with the Exam Organizing Committee issuing the exam notification to the candidates on February 20, 2024, stating the legal Ways and regulations to allow all candidates to be ready to take the exam.
