(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sun Chanthol, Deputy Prime Minister and First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, said that Cambodia has established various special economic zones to satisfy investors.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said that on the initiative of Samdech Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, he wanted to create a Cambodian and Japanese economic zone for the convenience of investors.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol stated that the state does not determine where to go as long as investors want to create a special economic zone with a land area of at least 400 hectares, investors and the government will work together to attract Investors to work in the area.
Please be informed that Cambodia Special Economic Zone refers to a special center for the development of the economic sector, which brings together industrial activities and other related activities, and may include general industrial areas and / or export processing areas.
Pursuant to Sub-Decree No. 148 dated December 2005 on the Establishment and Management of Special Economic Zones, each SEZ must have a production center and possibly a free trade center, service center, residential center and tourism center.
Investors are encouraged to choose to invest in special economic zones due to the convenience of labor laws, legal incentives from the Royal Government and the strategic factors of transport infrastructure adjacent to ports, major national roads, expressways, airports and International gates and so on.
The advantages of special economic zone structures and production support services to investors include building management, offices, local administration services, residential areas, sports facilities, roads, treatment facilities, roads, water supply, sewerage, waste disposal, power supply, networks. Internet and telecommunications, fire protection and security systems.
