US says ceasefire for Gaza depends on Hamas decision
Washington: Israel has agreed to accept most of the proposals related to the six-week ceasefire in the Gaza war, and now it is up to Hamas to release the hostages or not, a senior US official has said. No, for this ceasefire to take effect. This is according to a release by the AFP news agency.
"There is a framework for an agreement and Israel has accepted a majority," the senior US official told reporters on Saturday. "So now everything is up to Hamas to decide."
A Hamas delegation is reported to be traveling to Cairo, Egypt, on Saturday to attend a new round of talks. A source close to Hamas also said that the Hamas delegation would provide its answers to a request for a ceasefire plan that was discussed in Paris in February.
