Kampong Cham Provincial Administration Releases Press Release on Progress of Mekong Quarry in Srey Santhor District
(Kampong Cham): The Kampong Cham Provincial Administration has issued a press release outlining the progress of quarrying in the Mekong River area at Prey Toteung village, Russey commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province.
A press release issued by the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration on March 2, 2024 states that after the provincial administration has determined that the landowners to immediately remove the stones from the river surface as of the morning of March 2, 2024, Mr. Un Chanda, Provincial Governor, inspected the site and found that the implementation of this administrative measure has the following results:
The provincial administration continues to closely monitor the implementation of this administrative measure, with Ms. Sopheak, Deputy Governor, leading a team led by the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, the Provincial Department of Environment and other relevant authorities. Evaluate the implementation of this administrative measure until the end.
As for legal measures, the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration has already filed a complaint with the Kampong Cham Provincial Court, and the judiciary is proceeding with legal proceedings.
It should be noted that after receiving the information, the soft person Chai Eang poured stones into the Mekong River at Prey Toteung village, Russey commune, immediately, the provincial administration assigned Ms. Sopheak, Deputy Governor of Kampong Cham province to lead the inspection team to take pictures with Stakeholders will find out that there is indeed an activity of pouring rocks into the river, which has been operating for almost two months, since January 2, 2024.
The rock is poured into a 55-meter-long river and is planned to be 294.6 meters long (currently 130 meters long). The activity of pouring rocks into the river is not allowed.
