Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant Phase 2, with a capacity of nearly 200,000 cubic meters per day, will be put into operation on March 3 tomorrow.
(Phnom Penh): The second phase of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant, with a capacity of 195,000 cubic meters per day and a 2,000 mm pipeline across the Tonle Sap River, was put to trial operation on March 3. 2024 to improve water supply pressure throughout Phnom Penh and Takhmao. This is according to the announcement of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, which was received by Fresh News on March 2, 2024.
Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority (PPWSA) has confirmed that after the completion of construction and quality control of construction equipment, technical equipment, Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant Phase 2 and 2,000 mm water pipeline through the bottom of Tonle Sap River, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority will Launched the test at 12:00 pm on Sunday, March 3, 2024 to increase the water supply pressure throughout Phnom Penh and Takhmao.
The operation of this plant may cause leaks in water distribution pipes in public places or in front of customers' homes and cause water pollution.
Finally, complete peace in Cambodia was discovered on December 29, 1998 by the Khmer "statesman" Techo Sen, using a unique formula called "win-win politics" to turn war into peace. Even the United Nations, which has spent $ 2 billion, has not yet been able to bring complete peace to Cambodia.
This statement was made by Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the dissemination ceremony of the historical achievement "Suon Techo Santepheap" on the afternoon of March 1, 2024 at the Ministry of National Defense.
Samdech Picheay Sena Tea Banh added that due to this historical necessity and need, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also gave permission to build a win-win monument in the style of the Victory Monument in Koh Kong, Anlong Veng, Pailin as evidence and expand publicity. And providing learning about win-win politics, the history of the implementation process in various directions.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh stated that Anlong Veng area, Oddar Meanchey province, was the last area to end the war under the win-win policy, Pailin area is an area that has participated in many operations in the implementation of the win-win policy and the Oral area of the province. Kampong Speu was the starting point for the implementation of win-win politics, and this was the area where Keo Pong's 18th Division was stationed at that time.
One of the main meanings of the construction of the Victory Political Memorial is to commemorate the victory or overthrow of the Khmer Rouge and to bring peace to Cambodia and its people living under the roof of peace.
Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital Holds Spine Surgery Training with Famous Speakers from 4 Countries
(Phnom Penh): The Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital in early March 2024 organized a workshop on endoscopic spine surgery training with well-known specialized speakers from 4 countries to share with teachers. Cambodian doctors. The ceremony took place in the presence of the Director of the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, Professor Ngy Meng.
Prof. Ngy Meng said that the workshop was held to provide an opportunity to share and strengthen scientific and medical knowledge to care for chiropractors, as well as to continue to develop new knowledge and skills for safe and effective treatment. .
"We aim to understand the prevention and treatment of the risk of spinal damage, especially to prevent and reduce the incidence of spinal disease for the people of Cambodia."
He added that the workshop will be a sign of the development and innovation of new procedures for all chiropractors in our country. The highlight of the workshop "is a gathering of good national and international speakers on 12 topics, including speakers from Korea, Japan, the Philippines, Malaysia and 120 doctors from the National Hospital of Cambodia." .
On that occasion, Professor Ngy Meng confirmed that in 2023, 474,205 outpatients visited the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and 61,636 patients were allowed to be treated, so the total number of patients 535,841 people. In 2023, the Department of Neurology received 1,122 patients undergoing IPD surgery, of which 483 were chiropractors.
At the same time, Dr. Sim Sok Chan, Deputy Director of the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and President of the Cambodian Neurosurgery Association, also stated that this spinal disease is an aging disease, mostly due to long-term use of the spine. At some point, both the disc and the bone are weakened, which at some point presses on any nervous system, such as the neck, lumbar spine. After the doctor examines and evaluates, it may sometimes reach the stage of surgery.
