(Phnom Penh): Scientists initially claimed that only Jupiter has the most moons of the eight planets in the solar system, ie Jupiter has between 80-95 moons, but now hypotheses Changed differently than before.
According to astronomers and NASA, 62 new Saturn moons have been discovered, in addition to the 83 previously discovered moons recognized by the International Atomic Energy Agency. IAU) thus bringing the number of Saturn's moons to 145.
These moons are found among the orbits around Saturn, while some of them are extremely dim and difficult to observe, according to astronomers.
Saturn is one of the eight most unique planets in the solar system, as it is the second largest planet after Jupiter, a brightly colored planet. Saturn is far from the sixth sun. Its prominence is due to its multi-layered belt.
Saturn's most famous moon is Titan. Disability Foundation of the Ministry of Social Affairs Donates 2 Houses to People with Disabilities in Kampong Speu and Kandal Provinces
