Kratie Provincial Administration Takes Action to Eradicate Fishing Crimes
(Kratie): The crackdown on fishing crimes can not use the mechanism to sit and blow smoke just to catch illegal fishermen, that is, to find a fire and pour water to extinguish it. Therefore, in order to destroy the roots of illegal fishing using electric devices, the provincial administration, the relevant authorities and the Kratie provincial authorities have taken hot measures by going down to the point of sale and distribution of electric devices.
As a result of the crackdown, the police confiscated exhibits including 22 inverted fish shock inverters imported from China, 15 inverters (hot shock) inverters, and 280 wooden boxes for processing fish inverters.
In addition to confiscating all exhibits, the authorities arrested the owner of the illegal electric shock equipment store to build a file to be sent to the provincial court to proceed with the fisheries law.
Electrocution has been found to be one of the main causes of the loss of fishery resources along the Mekong River. For the geography of Kratie province, the use of equipment also affects dolphins, which are rare in the world's freshwater waters and are present in Kratie province.
The people of Kratie province have expressed their happiness and happiness to the rules to eradicate the crime of fishing using electric devices by the Kratie administration, authorities and law enforcement forces by confiscating electric devices from the point of sale and taking legal action against the sellers.
The people requested the Kratie provincial administration and police to continue to seek shelter, process, sell and distribute illegal fishing gear, especially electric gear from Kratie province.
