3: Use and maintenance of medical equipment and further development investment
4: Human resource management and capacity building, including personnel management and general administration, quality improvement, public relations
5: Inspection, reform, aiming for efficiency, safety and quality, raising all aspects of management and leadership, etc., for the management to continue to maintain the confidence and full satisfaction of the people.
Please be informed that the meeting was attended by the advisor of the Ministry of Secretary of State in charge of improving the quality of hospital services and strengthening professional ethics, as well as the advisor to the directors of the 10 national hospitals and the National Center for Tuberculosis and Lung Sin.
