Ministry of Tourism Holds Training Course on Muslim Tourism Trends and Needs in Preah Sihanouk Province
(Preah Sihanouk): The Ministry of Tourism on March 1, 2024 opened a training course on the trends and needs of Muslim tourism under the chairmanship of Mr. Hor Sarun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism.
On that occasion, Mr. Hor Sarun said that Cambodia is waiting to receive and welcome tourists of all nationalities from around the world, as the slogan "Cambodia welcomes all tourists." In this sense, the Ministry of Tourism always pays attention to understand and meet the different needs of each tourism market source, in which Muslim tourism is also a market source and a tourist that the Ministry of Tourism always considers.
The "Training on Muslim Tourism Trends and Needs" held now is one of the activities that the Ministry of Tourism is focusing on meeting the needs and increasing attractiveness among the Muslim tourism market in response. To the trend as well as the size of the Muslim tourism market, which has been steadily increasing.
Through today's training, tourism service businesses in Sihanoukville will gain more knowledge on how to better organize hospitality, increase attractiveness and ensure another level of satisfaction for Muslim tourists.
With the title of "Green Gold", the tourism sector has contributed to the socio-economic development, which ensures the creation of job opportunities and increased income for the people, boosts exports on the spot, boosts economic growth and increases national income, especially participation. Preservation of culture and protection of the environment, natural resources effectively and responsibly.
The recent opening of Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport and the Techo Takhmao International Airport project are the connecting point between Cambodia and the world, which can attract tourists from faraway countries and increase the number of tourists in the region. Includes tourists from Islamic countries.
In 2024, this is a year that reflects the attention, consideration, and promotion of tourism. The Cambodian and Chinese sides have agreed to launch 2024 as the year of people-to-people exchanges between Cambodia and China in order to encourage Chinese tourists. As a leading market source to visit Cambodia more and more. The official opening ceremony of "Year of Change of People and People of Cambodia-China 2024" was held on January 13, 2024 in Siem Reap.
