At the same time, Dr. Pheung Sakona stated that as a natural condition, women are born with weaker physical strength than men and stronger family responsibilities than men, along with some social norms, which are the main causes leading to Issues that severely affect the space of women's rights, gender discrimination, employment inequality, violence, trafficking, exploitation and social injustice.
Dr. Phoeung Sakona stated, "To this day, despite the concerted efforts of women around the world, the challenges of women in society continue and this annual celebration is a day of celebration. "Remind and encourage women to think more strongly and address these challenges more effectively."
In order to further strengthen the priority work for women in the general framework of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Minister reminded and provided additional advice to the leadership of the Ministry, especially the Women's Committee of the Ministry on some important work as follows:
In fact, in line with the clear political position of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has always given high priority and consideration to women. There are also more numbers at all skill levels.
At the same time, she also asked all women who are working in the framework of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts to continue to be active in their roles and responsibilities, and to take more time to participate in vocational training, both locally and internationally. Overseas for an additional basis for advancement in skills and roles.
100 Nights Team Association calls on social media users to check sources carefully before sharing
(Phnom Penh): The 100 Nights Working Group Association has called on all citizens who use social media to carefully examine sources of information, avoid believing and sharing baseless information, and not fall into the trap of Those anonymous people unknowingly.
The call comes after the 100 Nights Working Group recently observed that the overseas-based extremist group has launched a new campaign: launching a campaign to create false information and search for old videos. Inspired to take advantage of political interests, peace and development in the country by fabricating misleading stories to the Royal Government and causing social unrest.
The 100 Nights Working Group Association also calls on all citizens to participate in eliminating false information or false information to contribute to maintaining peace and order in Cambodian society.
