The registration of political parties and the list of candidates for the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council of the fourth mandate will start tomorrow.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dim Sovannarom, Member and Chairman of the Spokesperson of the National Election Committee (NEC), said that the registration of political parties and the list of candidates for the Capital Council and Provincial Council Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council, 4th Mandate 2024, lasts for 5 days, starting from March 2 and ending on March 6, 2024.
Mr. Dim Sovannarom made this remark when he chaired a meeting with stakeholders on the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council, 4th Mandate 2024 in the morning. March 1, 2024.
At the same time, he continued that to have the right to stand as a candidate, Cambodian citizens of both sexes who wish to stand as candidates for the election of the fourth mandate council must meet the following conditions and qualifications:
- Have Khmer nationality by birth - Be at least 25 years old as of May 26, 2024 - Have the right to vote and meet the conditions set by the NEC - Have exercised the right to vote by voting for The last general election held by the NEC, except in cases where the exercise of the right to vote was not justified. * Separately for ineligibility to stand as a candidate:
Members of the National Assembly, the Senate, the Constitutional Council, the Royal Government and judges
The senior NEC official confirmed that the conditions and procedures for the registration of political parties and the list of candidates:
* The political party must complete two copies of the application for registration of the political party and the list of candidates (T.1008). That political party. * This transfer does not allow the transfer of rights, unless the letter of permission contains the content of the transfer of rights.
The application for registration of a political party and the list of candidates must be accompanied by:
A copy of the certificate of registration of a political party at the Ministry of Interior is a copy of the Prakas on the registration of a political party at the Ministry of Interior, which is certified by the OWSO of the Capital / Provincial Administration or the OWSO. Single entry of the municipal, district and khan administration, 1 copy.
Political parties must send a copy of this proclamation to the NEC for safekeeping. At the Ministry of Interior, the legalization is attached to the application for registration of political parties and the list of candidates for the Council Election (T.008).
Name of political party in full letters, abbreviations and symbols of political parties
Address of the headquarters of the political party and the address of the headquarters of the political party in the capital or province or city or district or Khan
List of candidates for each type of council. This list must have at least twice the number of eligible and reserve candidates for any council seat in which the political party intends to contest.
Confirmation from the Commune / Sangkat Authority about the name on the voter list of any polling station in the commune / sangkat where the candidate is registered to vote
Candidate's statement approving the political party nominating itself to stand for the council election.
