Dr. Yang Saing Koma, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, emphasized this during the 4th Summit on Sustainable Agriculture under the theme "Practice renewable agriculture towards low carbon emissions" today. February 28, 2024.
He stated that by the end of 2024, the Ministry is committed to selecting 10,000 farmers on 15,000 hectares of land in 250 communes. After deploying agricultural officers in all 250 communes, commune agriculture officials will select farmers to participate in the system to link marketing and production.
He added that the Ministry of Agriculture is happy to cooperate and create a system that the Ministry of Agriculture has been working to coordinate this system.
He further explained that the Rumduol and Sen Kraob rice producers' communities will receive agricultural production contracts with the mills, which are members of the Rice Federation, which cooperate in the procurement of Rumduol and Sen Kraom rice, and they will also receive Obtain a special loan to buy Rumduol and Sen Kroom rice on time at a reasonable price, which encourages farmers to continue this rice production.
He said that in setting up the system, commune agriculture officials who have visited all communes will record the number of farmers, the number of areas, the use of agricultural inputs that are allowed and not allowed to be used to provide. Provides transparency, easy accountability to mills for export processing.
He encouraged banks and the private sector to participate in the system to provide credit to farmers for the purchase of fertilizers for production and insurance companies to provide insurance to farmers to ensure sustainability.
