Thailand plans to ban marijuana for recreation before the end of the year
BANGKOK: Thailand will ban the use of marijuana for recreational purposes before the end of this year, but will continue to allow it to be used for medical purposes, the health minister has said. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, February 29, 2024.
After Thailand became the first country in Southeast Asia to allow the use of marijuana for medical purposes in 2018 and later for further entertainment purposes, by 2022 tens of thousands of marijuana shops have sprung up across the country. ASEAN is an industry that is projected to reach $ 1.2 billion by 2025.
