General knowledge: What would happen if there was no February 29?
Although most people are aware of this, there are still some who wonder why it is necessary to have February 29 or every four years. What if there is no leap year, what will happen to human life?
February is usually only 28 days, but almost every four years, February is extended by one day. This is because the solar calendar follows the earth's orbit around the sun.
US, Allies Concerned Over North Korea's Arms Progress
BEIJING (Reuters) - The United States and South Korea say North Korea is one of Russia's leading arms and ammunition destinations for war on Ukrainian soil. The report leaked military intelligence amid the war situation in Ukraine, where Kiev government troops have recovered, but Russia still has a shortage of firearms.
North Korea's weapons factory is reportedly "at full capacity" to produce weapons and ammunition for Russia. The claim was made by the South Korean defense minister as the war in Ukraine enters its third year.
Since August 2023, Pyongyang has shipped 6,700 containers of weapons to Russia with a capacity of more than 3 million 152 mm rounds, or more than 500,000 rounds, according to the South Korean Defense Ministry. Of 122 mm machine guns.
North Korea has shipped 10,000 containers of ammunition or related equipment to Russia since September 2023, according to a report released last Friday.
Russia has more ammunition on the battlefield, while Ukraine lacks countermeasures
**** Concerns over war as North Korea continues to supply Russia
The transfer of weapons from Pyongyang to Moscow was recorded before North Korean leader Kim Jong Un met with his Russian counterpart, President Vladimir Putin, at the September 2023 summit in the east. Of Russia.
After a month-long summit between Russian and North Korean leaders, North Korea in November 2023 launched its previously failed military reconnaissance satellite into orbit. Successfully. Through the satellite, North Korea says it has a clear eye in the sky, where North Korea can detect key US and South Korean military positions through military intelligence satellites.
Then, in December 2023, North Korea successfully tested another of its first supersonic ballistic missiles, which became the fourth test of that type of missile. Also the first of which changed the firing method of the missile faster than the sound. The last test firing in December 2023 came as a shock to countries in the region.
Records show North Korea's technological progress after September summit
South Korea's National Intelligence Service has found that Pyongyang has shipped more than a million shells to Russia in 10 separate shipments since early August 2023 to support To its war in Ukraine. The White House also confirmed last month's findings that North Korean missiles were being used by Russia to fire on Ukrainian cities.
At the moment, the concern is not just about North Korea supplying Russia with ammunition and weapons for the war in Ukraine, but even more so for the United States and its allies. Look at North Korea's evolutionary momentum on more weapons technology.
The United States and its allies believe that in return for North Korea's arms supplies, Russia will provide North Korea with new and sophisticated technology that it will use to pose a threat to the world. .
