(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kha Leng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, said that as of January 2024, the trade volume between Cambodia and China amounted to more than 1154.62 million US dollars. This is an increase of 18.70% compared to the same period in 2023.
A senior official of the Ministry of Commerce said this on February 28, 2024, on the occasion of Ms. Cham Nimmol, Minister of Commerce, opening the seminar on "Updates and Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreements in Regional (RCEP) and Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement ”in Phnom Penh.
In front of national and international guests, especially Chinese, Hong Kong and Macao investors, Ms. Kha Leng stated, "According to Cambodian trade statistics, as of January 2024, the total trade volume between Cambodia and China is more than 1,154. $ 62 million. Of that, the volume exported from Cambodia to China amounted to about 121.73 million US dollars and the volume imported from China to Cambodia amounted to more than 1032.89 million US dollars.
On that occasion, Ms. Kha Leng also praised the Chinese Hong Kong and Macau Foreign Business Association in Cambodia and the Hong Kong Business Association in Cambodia for facilitating the attraction of investors to Cambodia now and organized an important seminar program. This is to promote the potential of trade and investment in Cambodia under the leadership of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate of the National Assembly.
