(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khvay Atiya, spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, has called for an immediate end to the dissemination of content that promotes the destruction of natural resources in Cambodia.
Khvay Atiya's reaction came on Thursday, February 29, 2024, after seeing a post on Yorn Khy's Facebook page that produced content using flowers as a dish to attract the public's attention. .
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment has called for the removal of its social media presence and the cessation of cooking posts made from the world's most endangered wildlife or plants. And protect for future generations.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment added that the Ministry of Environment is currently taking strict action against natural resource crimes, including enforcing the law 100% on natural resource offenders. At the same time, education encourages a change in the attitudes of all people to understand and participate in the conservation of wildlife and biodiversity resources is also an important part of the Ministry has been paying attention.
In addition, Mr. Khvay Atiya said that especially eating wild animals makes the health of consumers more dangerous and sometimes risk of death.
The spokesperson hopes that the creators of social media content will help raise awareness of the importance of biodiversity and encourage people to better protect forests, wildlife and biodiversity. Wildlife and biodiversity are an important part of ensuring ecosystem services that benefit the population and the local economy, especially ensuring the fight against climate change.
