Vietnam has imported brown rice from India for the first time in decades to process and export it as white rice, as Hanoi seeks to take advantage of demand, according to government and business groups. Strong world rice. According to Reuters.
Vietnam, the world's third-largest rice exporter, imported at least 200,000 tonnes of brown rice from India between December and February, the source told Reuters.
Vietnam is receiving large orders for rice exports after India, the world's largest exporter, imposed a 2023 ban on white rice exports. Rice exports from Vietnam will reach 8.3 million tons by 2023
He said that because rice was not available in Vietnam for milling, some traders imported brown rice from India and made good profits by processing and exporting rice. The exporter said he would soon follow suit.
While Indian brown rice costs about US $ 500 per tonne to transport to ports, Vietnamese traders sell white rice for more than $ 600, the source said. Vietnam recently began buying brown rice from India and now buys about 95 percent of India's total brown rice exports, the sources said.
A Vietnamese government official, who asked not to be identified, told Reuters that Hanoi was currently importing about 70,000 tonnes of brown rice a month from India.
