Senior officials of the Ministry of Agriculture open the construction site to expand the cashew processing plant in Kampong Svay district to increase export markets
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Toch Bun Hour, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on the afternoon of February 28, 2024, opened the construction site to expand the cashew processing factory to increase the export market in Trapeang Arak village, Chey district. Kampong Svay, Kampong Thom Province.
Mr. Touch Bun Hour said that Kampong Thom is widely known as the leading cashew producer in Cambodia. In addition, Cambodia's cashew nuts are large and delicious, and have received high ratings from many countries, including Japan.
He said that most of the cashew nuts produced in Cambodia are exported unprocessed due to the lack of space for drying, warehousing and processing, which forced the sale of cashew nuts at low prices immediately. From the harvest.
He added that seeing the potential of cashew products, Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister, instructed the Economic and Financial Policy Committee (NEPC) to lead, prepare and launch the necessary measures to promote. Processing and export of cashew products, including:
* First: Strengthening and expanding the export of cashew nuts, starting from the semi-finished product, that is, focusing on the export of dried cashew nuts, and in the next step, continue to strengthen and expand the processing of cashew nuts in a quantity that can provide capital. .
* Third: Promoting the compilation and establishment of cashew farming communities
* Fourth: Examining the possibility of increasing working capital for the purchase of cashew nuts for processing and increasing investment in infrastructure for the storage and processing of cashew nuts.
At the same time, Kampong Thom province has 145,300 hectares of agricultural land such as cashew crops, a total harvest of 80,000 hectares and an average yield of 1.5 tons / hectare per year, and the province has handicraft enterprises. 7 cashew nuts and 23 dryers.
