(Phnom Penh): Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhara, Deputy Secretary General of the Constitutional Council, said that the Senate is the steering wheel and a compass to guide the path of local democracy.
Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhra said that although the election of senators is a non-universal election, it is very important for the nation.
The Senate is the supreme body enshrined in the Constitution, and the Senate is the legislative body that contributes to the security of the legislature by reviewing and approving laws, especially the Senate is the steering wheel and compass of local democracy.
Based on the Constitution and the election law, the Constitutional Council has the final authority to resolve disputes related to the election of senators. Therefore, it is necessary to strengthen the ownership of its jurisdiction as a staff member of the Constitutional Council in order to maintain the democratic system in Cambodia in accordance with the Constitution and the laws in force.
