Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha commends all levels of civil servants of the Ministry of Interior for their hard work and good results in 2023
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Abhisandibandit Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, in the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the work results of 2023 and the direction of the Ministry of Interior on the morning of February 28, 2024, expressed his appreciation. Leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Interior at all levels who have worked hard to achieve their work and achieve good results in the past.
Dr. Sar Sokha emphasized that the current meeting of the Ministry of Interior is held after the meeting of the Capital-Provincial Administration in order to ensure the annual summary report as well as the results of the discussions in the meeting to collect input. Extensively from sub-national administration.
At the same time, the Ministry of Interior identified key topics for discussion that reflected the realities of the security situation and the provision of local public services, as well as in response to the strategic plan for the promotion of territorial administration, national security and order. Public and Social Security 2024-2028 of the Ministry of Interior.
Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha affirmed that the current meeting is an important opportunity to review and evaluate the work done by the Ministry of Interior and the sub-national administration and the remaining challenges to jointly set the direction for Implement the priority activities set out in the first phase of the Pentagon Strategic Political Program of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly under the leadership of His Excellency Hun Manet.
The Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior also mentioned the main achievements of the Ministry of Interior in 2023, including some principles that the conference should focus on as follows:
Despite the influence of global insecurity, the National Police Force has cooperated with the relevant law enforcement forces to continue to maintain peace, independence, national sovereignty, territorial integrity and ensure political stability, security, public order and social order. And normalization in the management of state institutions.
* Safe village, commune, and sangkat policies, cracking down on criminal offenses, cracking down on illegal drugs, combating human trafficking and all forms of sex trafficking are strictly suppressed, cracking down on gang activities, enforcing traffic laws. Land, firefighting and victim rescue interventions are being strengthened on a regular basis, ensuring social stability in all areas.
* Border Management The Ministry of Interior cooperates with the relevant authorities and institutions to lead, manage, coordinate and control all activities at the border, ensuring the regularity and security of travel and trade. Laws and regulations in force.
At the same time, the provision of administrative services to the people within the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Interior and the sub-national administration has also been strengthened and improved as a step to provide all these services more quickly, easily, transparently, accountable and trusted by the people. Citizens.
It should be informed that the current meeting of the Ministry of Interior will be held for two days, on February 28-29, 2024, with the division of discussion groups according to the main topics. The closing ceremony is scheduled to take place on the afternoon of February 29 tomorrow, presided over by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
