The Ministry of Environment has put in place a number of measures to take immediate action against individuals who incite people to encroach on forest land in protected areas.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has so far found that a small number of opportunistic individuals have been mobilizing people to encroach on community forests, protected areas and forest lands in protected areas. Personal benefit in the form of enjoyable land. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Environment on February 27, 2024.
In this regard, the Ministry of Environment would like to introduce the following measures:
First, the community committee of the protected area must protect the community forest area in accordance with the Prakas of the Ministry of Environment. If necessary, the Community Protected Area Community Committee shall immediately provide information to the relevant Provincial Department of Environment to request guidance and take legal action in a timely manner.
Second: Natural persons or relevant legal entities must immediately stop all activities such as logging, encroachment, encroachment, planting on community lands, protected areas.
Third, the person who encroached on the community forest land in the protected area must return the land unconditionally and reforest the deforested land.
Fourthly, the Provincial Department of Environment shall lead the rangers in cooperation with the sub-national administration, the relevant competent units and the community committee of the protected area to prevent all activities of clearing community forest land in accordance with the law in force.
The Ministry of Environment also urges the competent sub-national administrative departments and provincial provincial environment departments to take legal action to end all encroachment activities on community forests, protected areas within the protected areas effectively.
