The Director of the Department of Industry of Kep Province stated that: Kep province has a total area of 497.87 hectares of salt fields, which are limited to the following types of land: dry land, cultivated land and stream. In the last three years, the province has 7 salt production sites on a total area of 331.5 hectares.
He added that the challenges for salt handicrafts are low salt prices, high costs in the production process, lack of manpower (high labor costs), climate-dependent production, low quality salt, technical standards. Traditionally, there is no modernization and salt handicraft infrastructure is old, dilapidated, lacking additional capital for repair and improvement.
On the occasion of leading professional officers of the Department of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, as well as departments and units around the provinces and districts to inspect the process of salt production and harvesting throughout the province, Dr. Kep Som Piseth, Governor of Kep Province, spoke about the implementation of incentive policies. And stimulate salt production.
The provincial governor also encouraged all salt producers to strive to develop new technical capacity to produce standard quality salt to boost the domestic market and export. At the same time, the provincial governor urged local small and medium enterprises and handicrafts to use more local salt.
