Reuters reports that the latest import quota, in addition to the more than 2 million tonnes previously approved for 2024, comes at a time when harvesting is expected to take place. January to March will be lower than last year due to below-normal rainfall in Java, the country's main rice-growing region.
"Indonesia's rice purchases have been pushing up world prices and this news is further boosting the market," a Singapore-based rice trader told Reuters.
Asian rice prices hit a 16-year high after India, the world's top rice supplier, restricted exports last year. Prices of parboiled rice exported from India hit a record high this week due to limited supply and modest rising demand. Thai and Vietnamese rice prices have risen to near the highest level since 2008.
Indonesia's low yields further threaten supply, pushing up rice prices. Indonesia's rice production in January-March is expected to be 2.82 million tonnes lower than the same period, said Indonesian Commerce Ministry official Arif Sulistiyo during a weekly government meeting. Each other last year.
