MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia's finance minister has been in talks with his Chinese counterpart on the possibility of borrowing in yuan, Russian Finance Minister Anton Siluanov told state media in a speech released on Monday. From the country, but no decision has been made yet.
Mr Siluanov said Moscow was ready to start piloting digital payments with China or the Eurasian countries and would spread the idea with its partners.
He reiterated Russia's position that any action taken on Russian assets abroad would have the same response in Moscow.
