Two youths on a motorcycle hit a buffalo, killing one and seriously injuring another in Koh Kong province
(Koh Kong): A motorbike hit a buffalo, killing one and seriously injuring another, and the buffalo died on the spot. This incident happened at 21:40 pm on February 26, 2024 in Tanon commune, Botum Salor district, Koh Kong province.
The victim was Srey Raksmey, a 22-year-old male motorcyclist (died), residing in Toul Por village, Tanon commune, Botum Sakor district, Koh Kong province, and another named Khat Sok Khim, 25 years old, seriously injured, currently residing in Koh Sdech village, commune Koh Sdech, Kirisakor District, Koh Kong Province. The black Exctor motorcycle does not have a license plate.
Chan Ratha, chief of the Tanon commune administrative police station, said that the driver was driving too fast and was not careful when driving, causing the buffalo to crash and die immediately at the scene.
