The ceremony was accompanied by Mr. Un Bot, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom, Mr. Tan Bunhong, Director of the Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports, representatives of development partners and many government officials.
He said that Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister, has also introduced four key measures to improve the quality of public schools from kindergarten to secondary school. The four key measures include:
* First: Strengthening school governance * Second: Reviewing the curriculum and extracurricular activities in accordance with the need to strengthen the knowledge, discipline, ethics and behavior of students. * Third: Taking care of students' health through child nutrition programs and food quality control in schools. * Fourth: State-community partnership to promote education through caring, encouraging and encouraging the participation of parents and guardians in the community.
He encouraged all participants to strive to improve the school environment to become a green school for students, as the saying goes (clean school, village / commune, no garbage). Pay attention to the work of young people, both inside and outside the school, by providing opportunities for young people to participate in all social activities, especially to promote the Cambodian Children's Council and the Cambodian Youth Council in schools to be active and function well.
He stressed that schools must pay attention to the health and hygiene of students by regularly monitoring the sale of food in schools to comply with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health as well as the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
