Cambodian, Malaysian PMs focus on strengthening political and economic ties and cooperation
(Malaysia): After the official welcoming ceremony with honor and warmth, Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet and Malaysian Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim led senior officials of the two countries to discuss bilateral affairs.
The reception, held at the Government House of Malaysia, was hosted by several Malaysian Malaysian government officials, dignitaries and senior officials with a long red carpet.
After the welcoming ceremony, Samdech Hun Sen and Mr. Anwar Ibrahim led senior officials of the two countries to discuss bilateral issues.
The President will also preside over the Cambodia-Malaysia Business Forum 2024. During the program, the President will deliver a keynote address on "Economic Policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia and Economic Relations between Cambodia and Malaysia." The President will also receive a courtesy call from the Maybank of Malaysia.
Samdech Thipadei will lead a high-level delegation of Cambodia to return home to the Kingdom of Cambodia on the night of February 27, 2024.
It should be noted that Cambodia and Malaysia formally established diplomatic relations on August 31, 1957. Between 1969 and 1975, the diplomatic ties were maintained at the level of the acting charge d'affaires residing in Beijing.
By December 19, 1991, diplomatic ties had been re-established and had been continuously improved and improved to this day.
