NEW YORK (Reuters) - Without new military aid from the United States, his country would not have been able to prevent shipping on the Black Sea, a transit route for tens of thousands of tons of grain from Ukraine, Ukrainian President Vladimir Putin said on Monday. Ukraine to the world market. This is according to the release by Reuters on Tuesday, February 27, 2024.
In an interview with CNN, Zelensky described the construction of the Black Sea corridor as a "huge success", which has so far allowed the export of about 30 million tonnes of grain, along with other agricultural products. But he warned that if Congress did not approve the $ 60 billion security package, the future of transportation would be in doubt.
(Phnom Penh): Stakeholders in the water supply sector from all over Cambodia attended the 12th Annual Meeting of the Cambodian Water Suppliers Association (CWA) in Phnom Penh on 23 February 2024. This program provides a forum to summarize the results achieved and find innovative solutions in the field of water in Cambodia.
The 12th Annual Meeting was chaired by Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and Mr. Justin Wyatt, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia.
There was also the participation of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Water Supply Association and about 384 participants, representatives of ministries and institutions in the Royal Government, water operators, NGOs, development partners, financial institutions and suppliers of water-related materials. .
"Ensuring access to clean water is critical to protecting public health and attracting both domestic and international investment, which is critical to Cambodia's socio-economic development," he said.
"The Ministry encourages private water operators to strengthen their capacity to expand and strengthen water supply services in their licensed areas to ensure compliance with the requirements, especially the four basic conditions: clean water supply," he said. "With quality, safety, sustainability and affordability."
The Minister emphasized the important role of cooperation between the Public Water Supply Authority, private water operators, development partners and relevant ministries and institutions in pushing Cambodia's water sector forward faster as this sector is gaining momentum.
At this annual conference, the Australian Government reaffirmed its commitment to supporting Cambodia to achieve globalization of equitable, safe and affordable drinking water by 2030.
Ambassador Justin Wyatt highlighted Australia's significant contribution through its Economic Development Program, the Cambodia-Australia Partnership for Sustainable Economic Development (CAPRED).
The Ambassador highlighted the program's long-term partnership with Cambodia on water sector development, based on the common belief that access to clean water is a key driver of sustainable development.
"Australia has been partnering with Cambodia for almost a decade to support more than one million Cambodians in rural areas with access to clean water," said Ambassador Justin Wyatt. "The result of this support is a healthier population, more jobs, a stronger local economy."
The Cambodian Water Suppliers Association is a neutral, non-profit, private association for water supply in Cambodia that promotes cooperation, learning and knowledge exchange among national and international stakeholders.
The association has 281 private water operators from 23 provinces and 37 members from companies and financial institutions related to the water sector.
The 12th meeting of this association aims to celebrate the achievements of the Board of Directors of the third mandate from 2020-2023, elect a new board for the mandate of 2024-2027, summarize the work of the association in 2023, and prepare a strategy for 2024 As well as strengthening relationships and sharing knowledge, experience and technology among its members.
Quotes from Malaysian Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim in a statement with President Hun Manet
(Malaysia): In a joint statement with Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet, Malaysian Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim expressed his pleasure at welcoming the President as a friend and continuing the great relationship that Malaysia has with Samdech Hun Sen. Sen for decades.
Mr. Anwar Ibrahim emphasized that in the meeting with the President, there were fruitful discussions on many issues. He added that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding between the National Bank of Cambodia and the Central Bank of Malaysia is very important because it is one of the pillars related to monetary issues.
Mr Anwar emphasized that Malaysia had succeeded in conducting monetary cooperation with China and Thailand. He stressed that this cooperation will reduce the burden of reliance only on the US dollar.
Mr Anwar emphasized that Cambodia and Malaysia had high potential for palm oil and rice trade. The two countries' Ministries of Commerce will use the Technical Committee Forum to address challenges and find solutions to improve trade and tourism. As for investment, Anwar expects more investment in Cambodia and from Cambodia to Malaysia.
Regarding the connection of the transmission network, Mr. Anwar pointed out that the interested ministries and institutions will pay for the construction of a 1,000-kilometer submarine power pipeline that will facilitate the transmission of renewable energy from Cambodia and Laos to Singapore.
The Prime Minister of Malaysia thanked the Prime Minister and the Government of Cambodia for resolving the issue of Malaysians affected by job fraud. Mr. Anwar thanked the Cambodian police and immigration officials for taking care of the issue.
Mr. Anwar also stated that Malaysia and Cambodia will work together with the Islamic community to support vocational training that is needed by Cambodia.
Regarding flights, Mr. Anwar stated that there are currently 47 direct flights per week from Cambodia to Kuala Lumpur and from Kuala Lumpur to Cambodia. Anwar confirmed that he had agreed to consider expanding flights because of the huge potential for both countries.
Mr Anwar also stressed that he and the President acknowledged the fact that ASEAN has noted impressive cooperation in a number of areas, but trade and investment between ASEAN member states remain very low, which should be strengthened to provide Benefits to both countries.
Excerpt from the speech of Samdech Hun Sen in the joint statement with Mr. Anwar Ibrahim, Prime Minister of Malaysia
(Malaysia): During an official visit to Malaysia on February 27, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, and the Prime Minister of Malaysia, Mr. Anwar Ibrahim, made a joint statement expressing the political position of Establish political and economic cooperation between the two countries.
In the statement, Samdech Hun Sen thanked the Prime Minister of Malaysia for the warm welcome and the warm welcome for his first official visit to Malaysia.
This year marks the 67th anniversary of relations between the two countries, and in recent years, relations have reached new heights in terms of high-level economic relations, people-to-people exchanges, and people-to-people exchanges. People and people and strengthening relations in the field of defense.
In that statement, the Prime Minister of Cambodia expressed his deep gratitude to Malaysia for its support and participation in various fields, as well as the care and good coordination of Cambodian workers living in Malaysia.
He stressed that Cambodia has always kept in mind the valuable contribution of the Malaysian peacekeepers to Cambodia during the peace process of the early 1990s. The Prime Minister also mentioned that Mr. Anwar's official visit to Cambodia in March 2023, and his visit today shows the close cooperation between our two countries.
Samdech Hun Manet also said that the working meeting between Samdech and Prime Minister Anwar discussed many issues to improve cooperation between the two countries in all fields.
He also said that during the meeting with the Prime Minister of Malaysia, he noted with satisfaction and positive steps since Anwar's official visit to Cambodia in March 2023.
Samdech Hun Manet emphasized that through this visit and discussion, a new strategy has been set out to strengthen the relationship and cooperation between the two countries in the following necessary areas:
First, on the political side: Samdech Datuk Seri assured Prime Minister Anwar that he would continue Cambodia's positive and constructive approach to the Muslim community. Cambodia welcomes Malaysia's decision to host and launch discussions on the two countries' Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation, which is expected to take place soon before the middle of this year to begin the process of Involvement in other sectors.
Second, on the economic side: Samdech President stated that bilateral trade between the two countries has shown an upward trend and still has untapped potential to further strengthen the economic partnership. He also said that the Prime Minister and the Prime Minister of Malaysia highlighted the important role of the two countries' private sectors in promoting economic cooperation and new development initiatives.
Third, recognizing the importance of improving connectivity: In this regard, the Prime Minister and the Prime Minister discussed the possibility of further cooperation in the field of tourism and the facilitation of additional direct flights, as the Prime Minister. Anwar mentioned earlier, especially for further destinations between the two countries to facilitate travel between the two peoples, as well as tourists from third countries to visit both countries.
The Prime Minister stated in the statement that he and Prime Minister Anwar were optimistic about the future of relations between the two countries. Samdech and the Prime Minister continue to meet and share regularly the aspect of raising the level of relations to a new level.
