Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) announces short-term assistance to people in need of temporary electricity for various festivals
(Phnom Penh): Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has announced the short-term temporary use of electricity for various celebrations. This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News on February 26, 2024.
According to the announcement, in order to facilitate the needs of customers to hold various celebrations at home with short-term power consumption, EDC can provide authorization at the request of customers up to 3ph x 100A or 70kVA (continued from the public distribution line) for temporary use not more than 1 week, requiring customers to cooperate as follows:
1: Customers must apply through EDC App or at EDC branch locations near the required location at least 15 days before the required use, except at funerals can apply immediately. . Details can be contacted via the phone number on the electric bill.
2. The price of electricity used during the celebration must be recorded in the electricity bill based on the monthly electricity price.
3: The cost of installing the meter, meter and other equipment for temporary use during the celebration and the maintenance of the current is the responsibility of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), except for the network cable and electrical equipment under the electricity meter. Cambodia is the burden of customers.
