(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Monday, February 26, 2024, at the Peace Palace, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Hun Manet presided over the award ceremony. Encouragement of the Royal Government to win gold, silver and bronze medals, coaches and assistant coaches from the World Championships, the Southeast Asian Championships, the Asian Championships and the ASEAN University Championships.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that he was pleased to join HE Lok Chumteav, Ladies and Gentlemen to congratulate the athletes in the "Royal Government of Cambodia Award Ceremony" for the winners of the Southeast Asian Championships. Asian Championships, World Championships and 20th Southeast Asian University Games »
Samdech Samdech Hun Sen stated that on this special occasion, he would like to extend his best wishes and greetings from Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister and Chairman of the King's Personal Advisory Council to His Excellency. Lok Chumteav, Mr. Lok Si, coaches, all players.
* Samdech Hun Manet praised and appreciated the efforts of His Excellency, Lok Chumteav, leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the National Sports Federation, especially coaches, athletes who work together. With a sense of responsibility and high commitment to victory and achievement in sports should be proud of the motherland.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that in addition to winning the Games, the hosting of the SEA Games has raised the national prestige and prestige on the international stage, especially the strengthening of diplomatic ties and the strengthening of cooperation. Good relations between friendly countries to promote friendship, strengthen and expand international relations, and promote economic activity through tourism.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that in addition, another great national interest is to make the youth and the people, to increase the spirit of patriotism, to strengthen unity and friendship, which contributes significantly to the strengthening of national unity and peace. Peace in Cambodia.
* President Hun Manet stated that sports play an important role in diplomacy and international relations. Participation in sports reflects the close ties, solidarity, relations and close cooperation between the states and the people of all participating countries.
Samdech Hun Manet stated that sports contribute to maintaining a strong body and promoting good health of human resources, which are important determinants of labor productivity and the strength of the national economy. People who are healthy, live happily, easily grasp new knowledge and technology, have high commitment and hope to increase human capital.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that currently the sports sector has developed significantly and has played an important role in Cambodian society. Samdech President Hun Manet stated that sports have received interest and support from the Cambodian people of all walks of life, regardless of color or political affiliation, as Cambodians play sports for health, both physically and mentally. Slogan: "Sports build people and people build society"
* Hun Manet stated that building human resources in sports takes a long time and requires a lot of investment, while Cambodia has many priorities that need to be taken into account to promote a stronger Cambodian society.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that under the shadow of peace, national unity, political stability and economic growth, the Royal Government continues to pay high attention to the development of sports to strengthen the capacity of Cambodian athletes. Stronger in the competition to win more for the motherland.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been paying high attention to the priority areas of physical education and sports, through the encouragement and provision of all kinds of support, the construction of physical infrastructure to support sports and Equipping sports equipment in public places to inspire people to love sports, love sports and play sports.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government, with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports as its staff, continues to support the sports sector, our athletes and athletes, both spiritually and financially, and calls on all stakeholders to continue to support the development of sports. And sustainable by continuing to strengthen national-international championships and national sports competitions to develop additional capabilities to be better and more successful.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that with the progress and great victory for the motherland, Samdech would like to make some additional recommendations to the relevant institutions and athletes to implement the following:
First. The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, in collaboration with the National Sports Federation, shall establish mechanisms to support, train and encourage athletes at all levels to strengthen their ability to compete in a higher quality manner for the promotion of national sports in the region and the world.
Second. The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the National Sports Federation need to pay more attention to the selection and training of talented young people in sports to improve the quality and ability of sports for future regional and international competitions.
Third. I would like to encourage all coaches and athletes to practice their skills on a regular basis, because building sports skills takes a long time and must be ready to participate. Competitions, both national, regional and global.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet would like to thank the leadership of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the National Sports Federation, relevant officials at all levels, as well as coaches, athletes who have brought brilliant victories in international sports for the motherland. We.
