(Pursat): Nearly 50 Buddhists in Phnom Penh, led by a disciple Seng Kim, on January 25, 2024, marched a magnificent marble statue of the Buddha to be inaugurated on the hill of the ancient temple. Wat Bakan or Prasat Preah Ang Khmao ”which was built from laterite in ancient times and is located in Bakan village, Trapeang Chong commune, Bakan district, Pursat province.
At the same time, the procession of the Buddha statue was dedicated to the patriotic ancestors, especially to Father Seng Khi, mother Mao Heam, brothers and sisters who passed away to heaven.
Hundreds of years ago, a Po tree floated from Mohanakor along the Tonle Sap River, flowing through the Boeung Khnar River, passing through some areas. When moving to Stung Preah Mlou, now called Stung Bakan, the locals brought the boat ashore in order to keep it cool, choosing a hill for worship and a place to plant trees. That Po.
The current location of Bakan district in the past was the location of Pursat province in the Longvek period, under the reign of King Chan Reachea, the administrative position was changed from Bakan to the mouth of the Pursat river until today. Due to the abundance of Chung people living in that area, it has been named Trapeang Chung to this day.
