Preliminary Results of the 5th Mandate Senate Election, February 25, 2024
(Phnom Penh): Japanese observers see that the current election process in Cambodia is much better compared to 2013.
Mr. Harada, a professor from the University of Tokyo, took the time to observe the 5th Senate election on Sunday, February 25, 2024.
Mr. Harada observed the election process and counted ballots at two polling stations, one in Kandal province and one in Phnom Penh. The Japanese observer said he had been monitoring the election process in Cambodia since 2013.
Harada is a Japanese man who loves Cambodia and has learned to speak Khmer well. With careful observation, Harada saw that the Senate election process on Excellence.
Mr. Harada reminded in 2013 that the election process in Cambodia is very complicated because it does not use electoral technology. He said he, along with Japan's JICA, had made a number of recommendations to improve the election procedure and process.
Mr. Harada said that the recommendations were probably accepted by the National Election Committee and that the current electoral system in Cambodia is better. He noted that the voter list is now more efficient because it is integrated into the system to make it easier for voters to find their names. Unlike in 2013, hand-drawn voter lists make it difficult for voters to find them.
He also praised the election procedure in Cambodia, which has confirmed and verified the identity when entering the polling station to make the election process clearer. Cambodian, Mongolian tourism ministers agree to push for direct flights to expand tourism cooperation between the two countries
