NEC Officials Delight in Election Process Demonstrate Stronger and Better Democracy in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The 5th Senate Election Process Held on Sunday 25th This February 2024 has ended well, maintaining good order and security, without any incident disturbing the election process or counting the ballots.
According to the NEC report, 11,730 voters went to the polls, accounting for 99.86 percent of the total, with only 17 abstaining. The election of senators is a non-universal election. The only people who go to the polls are the National Assembly and the Commune / Sangkat Councilors in office.
Mr. Phan Rithipol, Election Management Officer at the 3rd Regional Constituency in Kandal Province, said that both polling stations in the Samdech Techo Hun Sen Regional Pedagogical Center conducted the election peacefully, in good order and without any incidents. . Both the election process and the vote count were attended by representatives of political parties, national and international observers, without any incident.
Mr. Phan Rithipol expressed his happiness and satisfaction with the excellent situation of the election process as well as the vote count. The election official considered this improvement to be a sign of democratic maturity in Cambodian society.
