(Phnom Penh): On Sunday, February 1, 2024, Cambodia will hold the 5th legislative senator election.
Pursuant to the Law on the Election of Senators in 2005, the Senate shall be elected by universal suffrage, elected and appointed for a term of six years. The senators make up half of the members of the National Assembly. Of these, two members are appointed by the King and the other two members are elected by the National Assembly by a simple majority.
According to this law, there are 62 senators for the fifth term. Of these, two members are appointed by the King and the other two members are elected by the National Assembly by a simple majority, and the other 58 members are elected by non-universal suffrage by secret ballot.
Polling stations are organized and divided into eight zones, and seats are divided into the following zones:
According to the National Election Committee, Cambodia's top political figures will go to the polls at the following polling stations:
First, Samdech Techo Hun Sen casts his ballot at polling station 3001, Hun Sen Regional Teacher Training Center, Kandal Province.
Second: Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet Votes at the Office of 1001 Preah Sisowath High School
Third: Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng casts his ballot at the 4002 office of Samdech Ov High School (Battambang City)
Fourth: Samdech Men Sam An Votes at Office 6003, Preah Sihanouk Primary School (Svay Rieng City)
5th: Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh casts his ballot at the polling station 4004 of Angkor High School (Siem Reap City)
Sixth: Samdech Moha National Assembly President Khuon Sodary casts his ballot at Office 3001, Hun Sen Regional Pedagogical Center, Kandal Province.
The following is the history of the Senate for the past 4 terms:
Out of the 61 senators in the first term, there are 10 members.
For the fourth term, a total of 62 senators will increase one seat in the 7th constituency.
