India-Cambodia Joint Business Council inaugurated in New Delhi to boost trade and investment between the two countries
The council was set up with the aim of promoting trade and investment between India and Cambodia through dialogue and cooperation between the two countries' private sectors.
Please be informed that this Joint Business Council has the Department of Industrial Promotion and Internal Trade (DPIIT) as the Secretariat for the Indian side, while the Cambodian Duke Association (COA) will act as the secretariat for the Cambodian side.
The official launch also included trade deals between the two sides, including Cambodian businessmen and Indian businessmen, all of which are major companies investing in key areas such as: skills development; Exploration and mining, health, food processing, construction, research, education and real estate.
"The official inauguration of the Indo-Cambodian Joint Business Council is a step towards a new page in economic cooperation between the two countries," said Duke Ly Yong Phat, president of the Cambodian Duke Association. "This is a platform that will allow us to identify challenges and challenges to create new opportunities for mutual economic benefit."
