Ministry of Environment and Conservation International Cambodia Launch Red Plus Project and Kandal Cardamom Landscape Program
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment and the International Conservation Organization of Cambodia have officially launched the REDD + project and the Central Cardamom Mountain Landscape Program.
This joint initiative is designed to ensure the ecosystem stability of the Central Cardamom landscape and to ensure that local communities are relevant and key players in long-term protection and conservation.
The Central Cardamom Landscape Program has received a 15-year commitment from the Landscape Heritage Fund (LLF), established by the German Ministry of Economic Cooperation and Development.
The Chargé d'Affaires of the German Embassy in Cambodia stated that effective management of protected areas is recognized as the most effective strategy for protecting biodiversity and valuable ecosystem services.
It should be noted that Conservation International has also partnered with USAID-Green Heritage to support the implementation of the Red Cardamom Central Cardamom REDD + project.
