Meak Bochea is an important festival of Buddhism, the state religion in Riel, every year on the 15th day of Meak, in order to commemorate the day when the Buddha declared the founding of Buddhism in the world in India 588 BC. On the 15th day of the month of Meak, just nine months after his enlightenment, it was also a reminder of the age of the Buddha's enlightenment.
