On the orders of Colonel Prohm Yorn, Director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, he directly ordered the fire brigade stationed at all targets to come out and intervene in a timely manner. The fire continued to reach nearby houses.
Colonel Prohm Yorn continued that due to the above location, there are difficulties such as the condition of the road is narrow, it is difficult for the specialized police force to enter to intervene to spray water. However, law enforcement forces use pedestrian rules by dragging water pipes in to intervene to rescue people in time.
In the case of the above fire, a 15-by-8-meter galvanized steel structure caused a fire to burn about 30% of the galvanized iron and wood warehouses, including wood, and caused the fire to spread to a wooden house measuring 7 meters by 25 meters. Completely.
