(Phnom Penh): February 24, 2024, this is the 45th anniversary of the reunion between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his wife, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, and the son of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet (February 24, 1979- February 24, 2024).
On the occasion of the 45th anniversary, Samdech Techo Hun Sen posted a message describing the story that happened on February 24, 1979, the day Samdech met with his wife and son, which he had never shown before.
The following is the full text that Samdech Techo Hun Sen described on the 45th anniversary of the reunion with his wife and son: February 24, 2024 is the 45th anniversary of the reunion between me and my son. My wife and son Manet (February 24, 1979-February 24, 2024).
Since getting married on January 5, 1976, my husband and I have had unfortunate experiences. It is not just for my wife and me, but for Cambodians across the country living under the Pol Pot regime.
How many leaders in the world are suffering like me? After getting married and having their first child separated, the doctor caused her to die without permission to bury her body and take care of his wife after giving birth.
My wife and I shed many tears, which represented pain. Many times my tears flowed into the bowl of porridge. I was separated from my wife and homeland on the night of June 20, 1977, when my wife was more than five months pregnant with the child who is the current Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In this article, I want to tell the story of what happened on February 24, 1979, the day I met my wife and children in Phnom Penh, because in previous writings and in the film there are no details about this.
However, it was time for me to leave home and return home. Arriving home, I saw and met my wife Rany, then met my son, which was a reunion 45 years ago. Reuniting wives and children is fun, but the war between father and son begins.
Manet not only refused to call me father, but he also let me not touch myself. Even farther away is the rivalry between mother and wife between father and child. Manet does not say much and does not have any bad attitude towards me, he politely peeked at my face before dinner.
There is no choice but to surrender, the child is willing to get out of bed and sit down to wait for the child to fall asleep before daring to go back to bed, placing the child in the corner of the bed near the wall. Get up early in the morning, do not let Manet see. This takes about 10 days. This is really a love affair from the time of marriage until Manet agrees to be recognized as a father.
This is the consequence of war and genocide, so we must work together to keep the peace, no matter what the cost.
Meak Bochea is celebrated to commemorate the day when the Buddha declared the founding of Buddhism in the world in India 588 BC on the 15th day of Meak, just nine months after his enlightenment.
The formation of Buddhism as a religious organization took place among 1,250 monks, members of a convention that brought together people from all walks of life.
At that convention, the Buddha proclaimed 11 principles for all members of the convention to adopt as a way of life and to spread the word about Buddhism to others.
On this day of Meakbochea, our Lord Samma Samputa gave the advice of the Supreme Master Ching Hai to the assembly of monks in Veluvan pagoda, which is the first pagoda in Buddhism. On that day, four important events occurred:
1. The 1,250 monks and envoys sent by the Buddha to various places to spread the Dharma returned to him in unison (Svekinasava).
2. All monks are monks who have been directly ordained by the Lord Samma Samputa, who is called a monk (sub-monk).
The above meeting is also called the quadrangle meeting, which is a four-member meeting.
This quadrangular assembly was held at Veluvan pagoda in the royal capital of King Pimpisar after the enlightenment of the Supreme Master Ching Hai nine months ago, 45 years before B.C.
A: 500 students of Uruvela Kassapa
B: 300 students of Preah Nathikasap:
C: 200 students of the Royal Council
D: 250 disciples of Sariputta and Mogullan.
A total of 1,250 monks, excluding Uruvela Kassapa, Nati Kassapa, Kaya Kassapa, Sariputta and Moggallana, added 1,255.
B: The goal of attaining Nirvana is considered to be the highest goal of Buddhism (public interest).
D: There are three principles:
E: The method has 6 points:
The above five points are considered as the policy of Buddhism.
What are the benefits of celebrating Meak Bochea?
The benefits of Meak Bo Day are:
1: Buddhists have correctly understood the importance of this day of worship.
2: Understand the principles and positions of Buddhism.
4: Performed the role of Buddhists on this day of Meak Bochea.
