MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin has said that 95 percent of Russia's strategic nuclear forces have been modernized as the air force has just acquired four new supersonic bombers. This is according to the release by Reuters on February 23, 2024.
Putin made the remarks in a statement on Friday as Russia celebrates its annual National Defense Day, a day after he launched the advanced Tu-160M nuclear strategic bomber. .
The Russian leader praised soldiers fighting in so-called "special military operations" in Ukraine, praising them as heroes who fought for "truth and justice". But most of his speeches focused on the achievements of the Russian military industry.
"Together with our practical combat experience, we will continue to strengthen the armed forces in all possible ways, including ongoing reorganization and modernization efforts," Putin said.
"Today, the percentage of modern weapons and equipment in the strategic nuclear force needs to be modernized to 95 percent, and the navy is almost 100 percent," he said. Official Summary of Election Campaign Events in 14 Days
