Igor Driesmans stated that as the former Cambodian Prime Minister stated in the decision to vote against Russia at the United Nations, Cambodia also values the fundamental principles of sovereignty and territorial integrity of the United Nations Charter. These principles are especially important for smaller countries with larger and stronger neighbors, such as Cambodia.
On March 2, 2022, the United Nations convened an emergency general assembly to vote on a resolution condemning and demanding that Russia withdraw its troops from Ukraine. Of the 141 member states, five voted against the resolution, while 35 voted against.
Cambodia was among the 141 countries that supported the resolution and was also a co-founder of the UN General Assembly emergency resolution on the situation in Ukraine.
