On the afternoon of February 23, 2024, a working group consisting of Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department, doctors, relevant district authorities and Brigade 70 met at Phnom Penh Capital Hall with additional guidance from Mr. Khuong Sreng. Campaign to kill tigers in five districts with the highest risk of dengue fever
On the first day of the campaign, 15 tiger spray guns were used by 26 brigade 70s in collaboration with doctors and relevant 5 district authorities, which are the most challenging districts. For the spread of dengue fever, including: Khan Dangkor, Khan Kambol, Khan Por Senchey, Khan Sen Sok and Khan Meanchey.
On that occasion, Mr. Khuong Sreng instructed the Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department that as a first step, the team had to spray tiger mosquito repellent in all 5 districts within a week and then continue to other districts until all 14 districts. Khans and 105 Sangkats. After completing the work of the 14 districts, the Department of Health must continue to spray mosquito repellent in the canals in Phnom Penh to eradicate dengue fever.
He called on the people of Phnom Penh to participate in eliminating tiger mosquito breeding grounds, such as eliminating clear water as a tiger mosquito shelter (water in car tires, motorcycle tires, cans, bottles, rain gear as a tiger mosquito shelter). Together we are eradicating tiger mosquito nets in our community to help prevent the spread of dengue fever. Tiger mosquitoes are carriers of dengue fever, while husk mosquitoes are not carriers of dengue fever.
