The 14-day Senate election campaign ended smoothly, security, safety and non-violence
(Phnom Penh): The 14-day Senate election campaign ended on the evening of February 23, 2024 with smooth, secure, safe, orderly, non-violent and non-violent events. Notable. This was confirmed in the press conference at the end of the election campaign.
The press conference was held by Mr. Som Sorida, Deputy Secretary General of the National Election Committee at the NEC headquarters on the evening of February 23, 2024.
Mr. Som Soreida stated that the political parties that contested the 5th Senate election in 2024 include: 1st: Cambodian People's Party, 2nd: Khmer Will Party, 3rd: FUNCINPEC Party and 4th: National Forces Party.
According to a senior NEC official, the total number of eligible voters for the Senate is 11,747 in the constituencies of the National Assembly and Commune / Sangkat Councilors. . For this election, the election campaign must be held in each regional constituency. The election campaign lasts for 14 days and all campaign activities must end 24 hours before election day.
Mr. Som Soreida stated, “During the 14 days of the election campaign, the NEC observed that the registered political parties and the list of candidates in each constituency were campaigning. "Finding votes by their own means in an environment of security, safety and good public order does not create any negative image."
Each political party conducts election campaign activities in various ways and to the best of its ability, such as campaign rallies, meetings of party members and supporters, and voters at party and commune offices, distribution of leaflets. Broadcast microphones at party headquarters and mobile broadcasts in villages.
In addition, he pointed out that the NEC observed that, in general, all political parties consistently informed the NEC about the time and place where they should conduct campaigning. Separately, local authorities also strive to facilitate propaganda activities such as: protection of locations, security, safety and public order, especially facilitating traffic on the streets during the campaign march and so on.
Overall, based on the above report, we can conclude that in the past 14 days, the election campaigns of political parties in the provinces and capitals under the region have run smoothly, with understanding, tolerance and cooperation from Stakeholders have improved security, safety, order and order in the provincial capital of each region. General knowledge: Get to know dragons in different cultures of the world (Part 11)
