(Phnom Penh): Illegal gambling games have been rampant throughout Cambodia, a problem that has led to social insecurity and a negative image of tourists. Lucky adventure games are also considered to be evil deeds that will lead to the destruction of the player.
Seeing such negativity, Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on February 14, 2024, issued a voice message ordering the governors of capitals and provinces throughout the country to immediately inspect the gambling place in case it continues to open. Recently, it is necessary to take immediate action to close and report directly to Samdech.
After the order of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, the Capital-Provincial Governor also issued a careful and responsible operation on its jurisdiction. In Kampong Cham province, the implementation of Samdech Thipdey's order has been very effective, as of now, 492 gambling venues in this province have been closed and no more are open.
The provincial governor also instructed the mayors to regularly monitor the situation in their localities and to update it once a month to manage the problem of gambling at closed locations to ensure no theft. Open after closed completely already.
On the afternoon of February 14th and February 15th, the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration closed 406 gambling sites, some of which volunteered to close on their own. Due to the careful implementation of Samdech Thipdey's order, the province has continued to close up to 492 locations as of now.
The effectiveness of the implementation of the order of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet to inspect the gambling place in Kampong Cham province was praised by Dr. Yong Pov, a political and social observer. Dr. even encouraged to stop illegal gambling on a regular basis and not just for a while.
The crackdown on illegal gambling is of great interest to Dr. Prum Tevy, an economic researcher. She observed that some business owners run gambling businesses, using the informal economy as an excuse.
"For example, past incidents like alcohol poisoning and who sells the wine are informal traders," she said. Informal winemakers, if there is a problem, start to get confused. There is death, there is what we have seen, but it must be there, all kinds of things, and we do nothing. "Our government still allows our informal economy to run smoothly so that the less capitalized can make a living."
