Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng outlined the basic principles for commune development set by the CPP in the main principles of the party's political program for the 5th Senate election as follows:
* Commune / Sangkat councils are given the autonomous authority to set policies for the development of their communes and to make arbitrary decisions on the use of funds, the provision of public services and local economic development in the interests of Citizens in accordance with the laws and regulations in force.
* Commune / Sangkat councils have clear functions and responsibilities for directing, managing, administering security, public order, financial resources, personnel, and the provision of necessary and basic public services, as well as local economic development within their jurisdiction. By definition of the law.
* Accelerate the transfer of functions connected with human resources, financial resources and authority from the national level to the sub-national level more and in a timely manner to improve the quality and efficiency of public service delivery and development in all areas at the local level.
Establish a competitive mechanism based on achievements in commune administration to strengthen the capacity of financial resource management and to obtain additional financial resources for local development.
