Cambodian Tonle Sap Project That Changed Lives and Improved Livelihood Receives International Award
(Phnom Penh): Outstanding projects in the development of small-scale agriculture in Cambodia, with high attention and priority in reducing poverty and promoting women's rights, have won the Global Fund's Outstanding Gender Award for International The prestigious IFAD Gender Award represents the Asia-Pacific region through a highly competitive selection process among other projects from 177 countries around the world.
The Tonle Sap Smallholder Poverty Reduction and Smallholder Development (TSSD-AF) Additional Financing Project won the award for its commitment based on strong results on gender equality and the empowerment of rural women in agriculture and forestry. Improving livelihoods and access to finance in its seven target provinces in the Tonle Sap region of Cambodia.
This project has been implemented by the Secretariat of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development (NCDDS) of the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries since 2018.
Ms. Mon Leakena said, "It is an honor for me to represent the women who benefited from the project to go and receive the award." They are enjoying a better life, being able to send their children to higher education and expand their business. As one of the beneficiaries of the project and as a Cambodian, I am very proud of this award. ”
