Senior health officials call on all stakeholders to continue to work together to completely eradicate malaria by 2025
(Siem Reap): Dr. Yok Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, called on all stakeholders, including local authorities, the private sector, development partners and the implementation of the Armed Forces, communities to continue to work together to completely eradicate malaria this year. The coming 2025.
This statement was made by the Minister on the occasion of the High Representative, Prof. Minister Chheang Ra, closing the 2023 Annual Meeting and 2024 work direction of the National Center for Malaria, Parasitology and Bacteriology (NCRC) in This February 23, 2024. The above meeting was held for 3 days on 21-23 February at Angkor Parady Hotel, Siem Reap.
She added that malaria, dengue fever, chickenpox and tapeworms are still a challenge for Cambodia today. These challenges require us to continue our efforts, but compared to some of our neighbors, Cambodia, we have been successful for the next three years, these are all our strengths.
She emphasized that for Cambodia, malaria will be completely eradicated by 2025, a wise initiative and direct adoption by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia until now, His Excellency Hun Manet as Director. Minister on the implementation of the first phase of the Pentagon Strategic Plan, in which the promotion of people's well-being is a priority in order to achieve universal health coverage.
The purpose of this conference is to review the progress of achievements in 2023 and the direction of 2024 on the work of the National Program to Fight Malaria, Dengue Fever and Worm Disease.
