The Ukrainian military command acknowledged that some troops were captured by Russia during its withdrawal from Avdiivka, but tried to say it was not large and that the loss of the city was not strategically important. .
Another senior Ukrainian official said only six Ukrainian soldiers had been arrested during the retreat from Avdiivka. The senior officer said that the captured soldiers were from the 3rd Brigade of the Combat Brigade and that after the ammunition was fired, they were arrested and they lost all contact. With other Ukrainian military groups.
The report blames Ukraine's withdrawal strategy for not being well-planned, withdrawing orders too quickly and the start of withdrawals too late, leading to an immediate worsening of the situation. Withdrawal orders appeared to be swift as some wounded soldiers who could not walk and were not evacuated were killed as Russian troops arrived.
