(Phnom Penh): 126 candidates applied for the Interpretation Competition on "The Role of Buddhism in Promoting Education, Morality and Behavior" to Celebrate the 9th National Reading Day.
Participants include: students, teachers, monks, citizens, journalists and government officials. This is what Dr. Kan Puthy, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, told Fresh News on February 22, 2024.
To celebrate the 9th National Reading Day, which will take place on March 11, 2024 under the theme "Reading is the foundation for all in life", the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has organized a competition to explain the President. "The Role of Buddhism in Promoting Moral and Behavioral Education" will select three winners.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Education, the components that can participate in the competition are education officials, teachers, students, teachers, students and the general public, and the deadline is February 20, 2024 at 17:00. As a constraint.
Dr. Kan Puthy continued that the Royal Government issued a sub-decree on the establishment of National Reading Day in 2015, deciding to choose March 11, the birthday of Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath to celebrate National Reading Day every year. Based on this sub-decree, the Ministry of Education organized the first National Reading Day in 2016.
As for why the Ministry of Education took the topic "The role of Buddhism in promoting education, morality and ethics," a spokesman for the Ministry of Education said that Buddhism is the state religion. In terms of tradition, Buddhism has been deeply rooted in the hearts of the masses, thus making the masses have strong faith from the people to the top leaders.
Buddhism is easy to attract and educate the hearts of the people to our students and children. Seeing this importance, His Excellency Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports has identified all stakeholders. The role of Buddhism in society associated with moral and behavioral education.
Dr. Kan Puthy added, "Science and technology must go hand in hand with morality, ethics and behavior. "If there is science and there is no morality, it will lead to danger, while Buddhism plays a very important role in psychological education."
At the same time, Venerable Nhep Tat, Secretary of Wat Ounalom, said that the selection of the topic "The role of Buddhism in promoting education, morality and behavior" is very good and appropriate to the social context.
Venerable Nhep Tat said that this topic will contribute to:
* 1: For the Cambodian people to contribute to the restoration and promotion of Khmer morality through Buddhist theory * 2: For the Cambodian people to understand and value Buddhism * 3: For the Cambodian people to understand their role to participate in promoting morality in Cambodian society.
Please be informed that in order to celebrate the 9th National Reading Day 2024, which will take place on March 11, 2024, the Ministry of Education will organize:
* 1: The competition program to read essays, poems and compositions to select the winners of the 1st to 3rd Samdech Techo Hun Sen Award under the theme "Reading is the foundation for all in life" by the winners of the competition Cheat takes place from March 9 to 10, 2024 at the Institute of Technology of Cambodia.
* 2: Selection of 3 winners with high ability in interpreting the topic "The role of Buddhism in promoting morality and behavior".
