Israeli airstrikes kill a woman and a child in southern Lebanon
Beirut: Israel on Wednesday launched an offensive in southern Lebanon, killing a woman and a child, a day after Lebanese Hezbollah vowed to pay Israel for killing civilians in Lebanon. Conflict across the Israeli-Lebanese border. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on February 21, 2024.
A woman and a girl were killed in an attack in the village of Majdal Zoun, about six kilometers from the border, according to two security sources and a medical source.
The Iranian-backed Hezbollah movement has been fighting Israel since the attack began on October 7 in a campaign that Hezbollah said was aimed at supporting the Palestinians in the Gaza Strip.
Since October 8, Israeli attacks have killed about 50 civilians in Lebanon, in addition to nearly 200 Hezbollah fighters.
Attacks from Lebanon to Israel have killed 10 Israeli soldiers and five civilians. The violence has displaced tens of thousands of people on both sides of the border.
