According to Ms. Kan Phearum, the head of the O'Phot chicken community in Ang Ta Som commune, in the past for her community there were only about 70 families, but through the development of Skouy chicken, known locally as "chicken". Increasingly popular because of its meat, it tastes delicious and has the ability to produce good eggs, bringing the total number of community members to more than 150 families.
The head of the community said that for this breed of chicken is sold more expensive than normal chicken breed, raising chicken breed allows farmers to get more profit because the chickens are heavy and good quality. For the future, she will be ready to breed more chickens for distribution to the market to double.
