Samdech President Hun Manet said that the state can understand the law but does not know the business strategy like business people.
"Now, our economic policy from six months ago, when we started, was to focus on economic diplomacy, but I went to see the leaders of other countries, they did the same thing, the same economic diplomacy, the leaders went to the place," he said. However, all countries are always facing the private sector. "So the important thing is that we can only open the door to the government, but the people who come in and out are the private sector and call them to us to compete."
In this sense, the engine of the economy is the private sector, in which small and medium enterprises (SMEs) will play an even more important role. Therefore, including the economic sector in the system and outside the system to build the economic base.
Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet said that in 2024, this is the basis for reforming the administrative system and the labor system. If successful, it will be a solid foundation for many years to come.
