(Phnom Penh): The order of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Samdech Hun Manet in the fight against drugs in ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations, and if any officials are found to have narcotics in them will be expelled from the framework without exception. Launched on February 20, 2024, it has been hailed by the public, both at home and abroad.
Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, told Fresh News that as a community worker, people know that people use a lot of drugs in pagodas, corners of school fences, shrubs and stupas. Originally, this also mentions towns, public places and entertainment clubs.
The drug problem is dimming the society and the society seems to be surrounded by drugs, so Dr. announced his strong support for the President's order. Dr. does not want to see only messages of support from all quarters, but to participate in the fight against drugs, especially local authorities must be responsible for their jurisdiction.
