(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathip Hun Manet, has issued 13 recommendations to promote the effective participation of the Royal Government in implementing policies, accountability and ownership.
The President made these 13 recommendations on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting and the 2024 work direction of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation on the afternoon of February 21, 2024.
In addition, the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly has been giving high priority to the promotion of micro, small and medium enterprises, handicrafts, and the informal economy by introducing a number of policy measures in the Pentagon-Phase Strategy. 1, especially the second angle.
In order to promote the effective participation of the Royal Government in implementing policies, responsibilities and ownership, Samdech has made some recommendations to the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation for further implementation as follows:
Third. To lead and promote the movement to increase the production and productivity of local industries, especially the production of raw materials and semi-finished products from local resources to build a supply chain that reduces dependence on imports, create added value High and increase employment for other local producers and processors.
Fifth. Must speed up the preparation of the draft law on technology transfer, the draft sub-decree on the establishment and management of small and medium enterprise concentration areas, the draft sub-decree on the establishment of the Union of Small and Medium Enterprises Associations of Cambodia, and the draft sub-decree on Research and development.
7th. We must continue to pay close attention to strengthening the management and conservation of salt farmland (Kampot-Kep Province), which is inherited from our ancestors, and promote the production of salt, which the Royal Government considers a strategic commodity, in line with the measures. Solve the problem of non-potential salt farmland.
Ninth, continue to promote the development and adoption of new standards on strategic goods for export to international markets, especially markets that are free trade partners with Cambodia. At the same time, the system of certification and inspection must be strengthened in accordance with international standards to prevent disasters to the safety, health of people, animals and plants, property, social security and the environment.
12th. Strengthen the management of state assets and the collection of national budget revenue from the provision of public services within the jurisdiction of the Ministry in accordance with the policies and regulations in force, especially the medium-term revenue collection strategy and the public financial management reform program.
Samdech Mani President Hun Manet said this on the afternoon of February 21, 2024, on the occasion that Samdech presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results in 2023 and the work direction for 2024 of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation. Along with the closing of the conference, the Ministry also organized the inauguration of the "Techo Sen Building".
His Excellency Hun Manet stated, "We must continue to pay close attention to strengthening the management and conservation of salt farmland (Kampot-Kep Province), which is inherited from our ancestors, and promote the production of salt by the Royal Government. "Considered a strategic commodity to go hand in hand with measures to address potential non-salt farmland."
His Excellency Hun Manet also instructed the Ministries, Sub-National Administrative Institutions and stakeholders to cooperate with the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation on the Law on Clean Water Management to ensure the supply of clean water to meet the four basic conditions: quality, safety and Sustainability and affordability.
Samdech Hun Sen also instructed the Ministry of Industry to continue to expand the scope of piped water supply to people in both urban and rural areas, and to encourage investment in large and medium-sized water production to support the region. Faced with a lack of water resources and a lack of financial resources.
