(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, Chairman of the National Committee of the Mekong River of Cambodia and Chairman of the Tonle Sap Authority at the Ministry's office on Wednesday morning, February 21, 2024, chaired a meeting on planning. National Development Strategy 2024-2028 and discuss the organization of the meeting to summarize the work results in 2023 and set the direction for implementation for 2024.
The current meeting was attended by leaders of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, leaders and heads of departments of the National Mekong Committee of Cambodia, leaders and heads of departments of the Tonle Sap Authority and all heads of all departments of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, a total of 80 People.
The Minister said that the preparation of the National Strategic Development Plan 2024-2028 is a necessary and important work to implement the priority policy of the Royal Government to bring Cambodia out of the status of a low-income country to achieve the vision of Cambodia 2050. Make Cambodia a high-income country, a harmonious society with high prestige in the international arena and contribute to achieving sustainable development goals.
At the same time, the Minister also requested the meeting to discuss, analyze, reflect and evaluate in detail the implementation and achievements achieved in the past 5 years 2019-2023 and based on this, determine the main objectives, goals and strategies for Next 5 years 2024-2028.
At the same time, the Minister made recommendations for the development of a strategic development plan based on:
* First: Sub-Decree on the Organization and Functioning of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology * Second: National Policy on Water Resources in the Kingdom of Cambodia * Third: Political Program of the Royal Government and Key Priority Policies on Water Resources Management and Irrigation Development * Fourth: Pentagon Strategy, Phase I of the Royal Government, Seventh Legislature of the National Assembly.
