UK provides $ 3.8 million in additional funding for mine clearance in Cambodia
The new fund follows funding announced last year for projects in Ukraine and Afghanistan and will support more than 50,000 people across 10 countries.
MAG and The HALO Trust expect nearly 17 million square meters to be cleared of mines in 10 countries with UK funding. Liberation of land for agriculture, housing and basic social services such as schools, hospitals, clean water, sanitation, support and promote economic development in communities around the world, restore livelihoods in rural and underprivileged areas, and strengthen local production and food security.
The fund announced today will allow work to continue in some of the world's most heavily mined countries, such as Cambodia and Laos, as well as some of the world's poorest countries, such as South Sudan and Somalia, for up to a month. March 2025. The fund will also support the New Country Program in Ethiopia, where HALO is currently the only active international demining operator.
Continuing demining funding will also create new opportunities for women in countries such as Angola, Cambodia and Laos by increasing employment and career development in demining with ongoing investment in staff training.
"As more demining operations remain in the conflict environment in many countries, the fund will provide significant assistance to countries that are dealing with the aftermath of the conflict and will continue to do so," he said. Continue to claim lives for a long time after the fighting is over. "This is an important step towards a landmine-free world."
