WASHINGTON (Reuters) - A nine-year-old boy in Utah was arrested in connection with the shooting death of a family member in the head, police said on Tuesday. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, February 21, 2024.
Last Friday night, police officers from Tooele rushed to the family home after receiving reports that a man had fainted and was bleeding from his head. Authorities immediately concluded that the 32-year-old man had been shot in the head and was in critical condition. He was rushed to a nearby hospital, but died on arrival.
The investigation led to the arrest of a 9-year-old child who was a member of the victim's family, while police did not specify what the two were supposed to be and did not provide further details. That surrounding the shooting, including whether it is being investigated in the form of a murder case. The 9-year-old has not yet been formally charged.
