(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and National Outstanding Member of the Joint Action Plan of the United Nations Secretary-General for the Health of Women and Children
On the occasion of the National Day of Maternal, Child and Child Health, February 21, 2024, under the theme "Strengthening the quality of maternal, infant and child health care services to achieve global health coverage."
Therefore, on the occasion of the National Day of Maternal, Infant and Child Health 2024, Samdech Kittipritthbandit appealed to his compatriots, especially men and women, parents and young people as follows:
1. Ask pregnant women to get at least four check-ups at regular intervals to get vaccinated against the disease and mother-to-child transmission, especially voluntary blood tests for HIV, syphilis and hepatitis B. Give birth at a health center or hospital with a properly trained doctor.
2: After childbirth, the mother should check the health of the baby to be vaccinated against 11 diseases on time, continue to monitor the health and growth of the baby, breastfeeding only from the moment the baby is born. To infants up to 6 months of age and provide all kinds of nutritious supplements (porridge, all ingredients), along with continued breastfeeding until the child is at least 2 years old.
3. Take the baby to the hospital immediately when you see any danger signs of respiratory disease, diarrhea or other diseases, and take the baby or young child who is thin or does not gain weight at all to consult and receive treatment. At the hospital.
5: Leaders, civil servants, health workers, doctors, midwives and all service providers with high professional ethics and responsibility to support the implementation of the priority policies of the Royal Government to achieve high efficiency. The set goals of the Royal Government.
6: Local authorities at the sub-national level should pay attention to encourage and send women of reproductive age (15 to 49 years old), pregnant women and women with children under 2 years old to receive health care services at health centers or hospitals. Refer to everyone.
7: Officials, staffs, branches, sub-branches and volunteers of the Cambodian Red Cross to work closely with health officials - staff to participate in health education to all target women and help promote women to health centers or hospitals. Time.
