The World Food Program (WFP) said it resumed aid on Sunday after a three-week hiatus, but its convoy "faced complete turmoil and violence due to the collapse of civil order." "
Twenty weeks into the Israeli-led war against Hamas in the Gaza Strip, the United Nations agency has warned that safe food and water are in short supply and that the people's despair is at an all-time high. Before coming.
The Rome-based agency said it planned to send aid by truck every day for seven days. But on Sunday, the convoy fought "several attempts by people to get on our trucks and then face gunfire as soon as we entered Gaza."
The report added: "On Monday, the second convoy to the north also faced unrest and violence due to the collapse of civil order ... Several trucks were hijacked and a truck driver was killed. He was beaten. ”
WFP has said it must temporarily stop shipping "until conditions allow for safe delivery." "This is not an easy decision because it" means that the situation there will get worse and more people will be at risk of dying of starvation, "Reuters reported. Addiction is a smart choice! Nationwide drug crackdown on February 20: 12 cases cracked, 36 arrested
