Minister of Environment: Clean water campaign starts to clean up Tonle Sap as first priority
The Minister added that the surface cleaning campaign is to clean the plastic bags on the surface to prevent the flow of water into the Tonle Sap, which is the main priority. The Ministry of Environment wants fish to be a source of protein for our people, who can sustain about 7 million people in Kong Vong.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth stated that we do not want to lose fish due to pollution by garbage and plastic bags. "When plastic bags in the Tonle Sap damage the environment, when they decompose into fish food, and when people eat fish, it also damages our health."
Thus, the first phase of the clean water campaign begins with a study of the canal system connected to the Tonle Sap and the installation of barriers in those systems to prevent plastic from flowing into the Tonle Sap. Dr. Eang Sophalleth said, "We must first prevent garbage from flowing through the canals and dump into the Tonle Sap, because the Tonle Sap is not a trash can or a plastic bag."
Then, the Ministry of Environment will continue to cooperate with the Tonle Sap Cleanup Partnership by requesting to help build more garbage collection machines on the surface of the water in Cambodia, our Tonle Sap will hope to be a clean paradise, attract tourists and preserve resources. Nature is good for the next generation.
