The move comes after the United States signaled it would veto a draft resolution proposed by Algeria calling for an immediate humanitarian ceasefire in Gaza.
The Security Council requested that in addition to the International Atomic Energy Agency's ongoing inspections in Iran, that it monitor Iran's compliance with "the steps required by the IAEA Board". That also prevents large-scale humanitarian assistance.
Negotiations on a draft US resolution are scheduled to begin this week, but it is unclear when. Under the UN Charter, Member States shall "agree to accept and implement" resolutions adopted by the Security Council, as opposed to decisions made by the UN General Assembly in a non-binding manner.
This is the first time the United States has called for a temporary ceasefire in the Gaza Strip at the United Nations, having previously vetoed the draft when using the term "ceasefire" in the Israeli-Hamas war.
