According to the Ek Phnom District Administration, the Royal Government did not cut the land for the people in 2021. In 2021, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, former Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, led a working group to visit. The site itself has taken legal action against those who encroached on the land for farming and has sent some of the perpetrators to prison.
As a task to be performed in the role of the District Administrative Unity Command, in cooperation with the Provincial Fisheries Administration, it has continued to protect the land in these three areas on a regular basis ever since. By the end of 2023, people in the territory of Banteay Meanchey province came to plow the land because of rice on this prohibited site.
Ek Phnom District Administration appeals to the public from all walks of life to be aware and not to believe the incitement of crooks who still have the ambition to take the three forest areas of the state as their own property, please join together to protect natural resources for the benefit of Of the people and the nation.
