Senior Minister Osman Hassan asks Qatar to help manage donations under Islamic law in Cambodia
(Qatar): Dr. Osman Hassan asks Qatar to provide training and technical assistance on the management of the Zakat budget (donations) in Cambodia under Islamic law, while the Cambodian Islamic community is in need.
He briefed on the situation in Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister and later Samdech Moha Bovarit Hun Manet, the current Prime Minister, which brought peace and harmony to Cambodia. Race and religion The people are taken care of by the Royal Government without any racial discrimination.
At the same time, Dr. Osman Hassan said that Cambodia still lacks in the management of donations and other Islamic teachings, so he asked Qatar to provide views, experiences and laws to Cambodia to establish a fund for management. The problem.
He mentioned 200 poor Cambodian students studying at the University of Fatoni in Thailand, who had just graduated but had no degrees due to a lack of funding. In this regard, the Qatari side has suggested writing a letter of request to the Minister of Education (Awqf) and Islamic Affairs to examine the possibility of assistance in paying school fees.
After checking and seeing that there is a shortage, they will provide the funds we request through the bank, all procedures must be done online.
Qatar to send businessmen to study investment opportunities in key sectors in Cambodia
(Qatar): The Qatari Chamber of Commerce and Industry will send its investors to Cambodia to study investment opportunities in key sectors in Cambodia, such as agriculture, tourism, infrastructure, food production, nutmeg industry and more. Qatar Market While Cambodia is a country rich in raw materials and low labor force.
During the meeting, the Senior Minister informed about the main points of Cambodia, such as the production of rice in excess of 7 million tons per year and cashew nuts can produce 1 million tons and high quality in the world, and HE Senior Minister confirmed that the industry Halal in Cambodia is also developing.
In response, the Qatari side stated that the state of Qatar has good cooperative relations with Cambodia, noting the importance of increasing Qatar investment in the above areas, and promised to arrange visits to Qatari investors. Come to Cambodia to examine the possibility of investing in Cambodia in the above key areas to export from Cambodia to the world market.
Finally, the Qatari side affirmed that the Qatar market welcomes high quality and affordable Cambodian products, indicating that the Chamber of Commerce will enhance existing investment opportunities in Cambodia among the Qatari business community to encourage Qatari investors to invest. Capital in Cambodia.
