He added that in order to contribute to ensuring the effectiveness of the implementation of the ninth anti-drug campaign, which is an important political priority of the Royal Government, as well as to promote trust, efficiency and good governance in state institutions at all levels. At the sub-national level, both in the Armed Forces and in the civil service, it is necessary for the Royal Government to take strict measures through the following strict regulations:
1. All ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations must increase the regular inspection of civil servants, national police officers and soldiers, as well as contracted officers under their supervision on the use of illegal drugs or related drugs. Illegal addiction.
2. All ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations shall take action to terminate their positions and dismiss them without exception for civil servants, national police officers and soldiers, as well as any contracted officials who are found to be using equipment. Illegal drug addiction or involvement in illegal drugs.
3. The application of disciplinary sanctions does not impede the implementation of criminal sanctions in accordance with the laws and regulations in force.
