(Ratanakkiri): The price of cashew nuts in 2024 is lower than last year, considering the same harvest period. For more than 10 days in February 2024, cashew nuts have started to bear fruit, but the price seems to be lower than in 2023.
According to the brokers, this year the cashew yield seems to be lower than in 2023, considering the same period of daily purchases in 2023, they bought from 5 to 7 tons. In particular, at the beginning of 2024, they can only buy 1 to 2 tons per day.
Regarding the cashew harvest in 2024, Mr. Sem Roeun, Director of the Agricultural Productivity Bureau of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the total area under cashew cultivation in Ratanakkiri is 65,695 hectares. 52,550 hectares.
Farmers are now harvesting gradually, and prices are slightly lower than last year compared to the same crop, and yields are lower than last year.
Sources from cashew growers, meanwhile, have expressed serious concern about cashew prices falling at the beginning of the season and declining yields. In terms of economic value, they are at a loss because the demand for pesticides, pesticides and high labor costs is high. In the Commune / Sangkat Fund Auction Process
