Samdech President Hun Manet: In order to eradicate drugs, all people need to participate (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) Drugs need the participation of all citizens through education, dissemination, guidance to relatives not to come into contact with drugs.
This statement was made on the occasion that Samdech Hun Sen presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results of 2023 and set the direction for 2024 of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and disseminating the 9th plan to fight against illegal drugs. In the afternoon of February 20, 2024.
"The fight against drugs is a common issue of ours. The authorities, the Royal Government, and the law enforcement forces have a duty to lead the development of laws to prevent, but it is not possible without the participation," he said. .
At the same time, Samdech President Hun Manet emphasized that the superpower has not yet spent billions to eliminate the drug problem without the participation of the people.
Samdech Hun Manet said that countries that have the death penalty for drug traffickers still have drugs, so it requires the participation of the people through education, guidance and the biggest advice is to advise relatives not to Exposure to drugs.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet said that in the case of drugs, there are legal measures against vendors and producers, but consumers must be considered as victims who need to receive education, guidance and rehabilitation.
Hun Manet stated that the community must work together to eradicate the drug problem, and the role of the Royal Government - authorities at all levels remains the key to solving this problem.
Please be informed that drugs have become a matter of concern in Cambodian society after trafficking and consumption have become more serious.
Samdech President Hun Manet considered the fight against drugs as a necessary task for social security, and Samdech issued a hot order for the relevant authorities to fight effectively. Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on Thailand
(Phnom Penh): The Office of the Spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on February 20, 2024 issued a statement on the case of Cambodian citizens in traffic accidents in Thailand.
The Consulate General of Cambodia in Sa Kaeo province informed on February 19, 2024 that according to preliminary information received from the competent authorities of Thailand in Makham district on February 18, 2024, three Cambodians (2 males) And a woman) were involved in a traffic accident while traveling in a van from Bangkok to the Cambodian-Thai border via Chanthaburi.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Tuesday, February 20, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results of 2023 and Raise the 2024 target of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and disseminate the 9th plan to fight against illegal drugs.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, the opportunity to close the meeting to review the work in 2023 and raise the work direction in 2024 of the National Authority for Combating Drugs:
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that in 2024, as the implementation of the plan to fight against illegal drugs (2017-2023), law enforcement forces launched a total of 55,305 drug crime operations, arresting a number of suspects. 120,307 people seized all kinds of drugs weighing about 27,641 kilograms and about 520,005 kilograms of chemical compounds, including means, materials and other exhibits.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that all procedures for the management of exhibits and assets related to drugs must be expedited, and the operational activities to prevent and suppress drug offenses imported from abroad must be expedited.
Samdech Hun Manet stated that the border authorities, especially the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of National Defense and the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, must strengthen the prevention and suppression of drug imports at the border (land, water, air and mail). ) Especially from the Golden Triangle.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the National Anti-Drug Authority must cooperate with international partners to exchange information on illegal drug trafficking, strengthen the BLO border liaison mechanism with neighboring countries to prevent and cut off drug trafficking from Outsiders come to the country.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that law enforcement officials, especially the Capital and Provincial Unity Command, must take the strictest and most serious measures against drug distribution and use in the community.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that all leaders of ministries, institutions, private companies, factories, enterprises and family members must educate, warn about the effects and destruction of drugs, and take the strictest and strictest measures against drug use. . Must say "no" to drugs!
* Samdech Hun Manet said that the National Authority for Combating Drugs must compile educational content on the effects of drugs and disseminate and disseminate awareness to the people by all means.
* Samdech Hun Manet requested the relevant ministries and institutions, especially the Ministry of Information, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Ministry of Cult and Religion and the Ministry of Tourism to cooperate with the National Authority for Combating Drugs on this important work to integrate Awareness of drug issues and widespread dissemination in schools, pagodas, arts, entertainment, sports and forums.
* President Hun Manet stated that although drugs are a global problem, do not despair of fighting it and let it spread to Cambodian society.
* President Hun Manet stated that the fight against drugs should not be done in a divisive way, but must have a clear plan.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the policy of safe villages and communes of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature has set a goal to prevent and eliminate drugs in Cambodian society.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that in order to participate in the eradication of drugs, the participation of all citizens is needed through education, dissemination and guidance of relatives not to come into contact with drugs.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that Samdech has just issued a new decision, civil servants at both national and sub-national levels found to be involved in drugs will be expelled from the framework.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet plans to take measures to punish any private sector involved in drugs.
* President Hun Manet wants the private sector to take measures to fight drugs without allowing its employees to be involved in drugs. If involved, fired.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that Cambodia will not use weapons to fight drugs in the next 10 to 15 years, but will run out of drugs.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the blacklisting of drug-related officials is not a violation of rights, but a help to the community not to be involved in drugs.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet announces again that marijuana cultivation is not allowed.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet warns those who want to invest in growing marijuana in Cambodia not to spend time flying to Cambodia, Samdech does not allow it.
Avdiivka has been a battleground between Ukraine and Russian troops for nearly a decade. Attacks in the region have intensified since Russia launched a full-scale offensive against Ukraine on February 24, 2022, and a final Russian offensive to retake the site has resumed. About four months ago, after the invasion of Ukraine, the dry season was seen to be ineffective.
Withdrawal orders appeared to be swift as some wounded soldiers who could not walk and were not evacuated were killed as Russian troops arrived. A Ukrainian soldier has been ordered to leave 300 wounded and burn everything else.
Hours after Russian soldiers hoisted their flags over Avdiivka, a shocking story unfolded about several wounded soldiers who could not escape and were killed. Where Russian soldiers arrived at their positions.
Russian leader Vladimir Putin hailed the capture of Avivka as a major victory and congratulated Russian troops. Russia has long attempted to seize the city of Ivory Coast in order to gain full control of the Donbas region, an industrial area in eastern Ukraine.
The loss of Avdiivka has been blamed on a lack of ammunition, as Ukraine's fight against Russia has always relied on military aid from the West, especially from the United States. US military aid has been blocked since late 2023 due to internal political tensions between the ruling Democrats and Republicans.
(Tbong Khmum): Dr. Moeng Makara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Memot District on Monday, February 19, 2024, presided over a meeting with 273 authorities and residents of Memot District. The ceremony took place at Wat Tuol Vihear in Bang Chros village, Choam Kravien commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province.
Dr. Moeng Makara brought greetings and memories from Samdech Hun Sen to all the people present in this program. Dr. Moeng Makara also disseminated the "Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1", a political program of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate for the construction and defense of the motherland of Cambodia.
Dr. Moeng Makara emphasized that the Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1 of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature, under the wise leadership and long-term vision of Samdech Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has identified two main historical missions: :
* First, to maintain and nurture peace, which has been difficult to achieve with priceless sacrifices, and to nurture the momentum of economic growth and overall development.
* Second: Build and strengthen the foundation to accelerate the development of the country by going through the milestones of becoming a high middle income country by 2030 towards achieving the vision of Cambodia 2050 through building The resilience of the five sectors: resilience of the public sector, resilience of the economic sector, resilience of the financial sector, resilience of human capital and society, and resilience of the environment and in response to climate change.
The Pentagon Strategy - The first phase will continue to strengthen and expand the living standards of families, people everywhere across the country, create more jobs and human resources to contribute to ensuring national economic growth. Continuing to help the people proves that the leaders of the Royal Government always pay attention to solve the problems of the people, protect and serve the people in all circumstances.
After the ceremony, Dr. Moeng Makara also led the team to visit Memot District Hall and continue to visit and check the general situation of Pepper community and visit the place of Samdech Thipdey south of Wat Samrong in Samrong village, Treak commune, Memot district. Well.
