(Kampong Speu): Mango candy waste that flows into Stung Prek Tnaot, causing fish to die in the river, has now diverted the waste disposal site in Thpong district, Kampong Speu province, making people very worried about those chemicals.
Around this concern, the people and the village chief are very surprised because these wastes emit a strong chemical pollution around the people's homes.
Many residents reported that the waste was transported from the mango factory, which used to be dumped into Stung Prek Tnaot and poisoned dead fish in the river, and there was a reaction from the authorities, so the waste was diverted by truck. In the above position.
Residents said that the factory owners rented a truck to transport garbage for $ 40, and the truck was dumped at the above location, which affected the health of many families.
Residents stressed that the authorities should take action against the garbage disposal group as strictly as possible, especially the Department of Environment, which is responsible for dealing directly with the company.
Residents said that shortly after the rainy season, the waste could flow into the water, causing the fish to die and other crops to be damaged by the toxins. Handing over the fishing tackle to the authorities and professional officers of the Fisheries Administration
