(Phnom Penh): Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Illegal Drugs, stated that the implementation of the plan to fight against illegal drugs has a big goal is not to make Cambodia a target of crime. Drug abuse and not allowing drugs to cause destructive effects on society.
Remarks by Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun on the occasion of co-chaired by Mr. Abhisandibandit Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior and Deputy Chairman of the Anti-Illegal Drug Campaign Command this morning, February 20, 2024. To disseminate the plan for the 9th anti-drug campaign.
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun affirmed that the past campaign against illegal drugs has achieved remarkable results, and the next goal is to strive to make Cambodia a drug-free country and keep each family as a family. Clean, drug-free from the perspective of "joining together for a drug-free life and community."
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs noted that based on the report summarizing the results of the discussions of the five groups of General Meas Virith, we have accepted many good ideas to be The compass points the way to success on the anti-drug mission, as well as an important input for reporting to the Prime Minister at the closing ceremony this afternoon.
He added that the current drug situation has reached a very worrying stage, which has become a common problem of the whole society, regardless of race, color or color. In this sense, all ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations, the private sector, up to each family must consider the drug problem as a common problem, which requires cooperation, prevention, education, reminder and strict measures.
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun affirmed that seeing these challenges, the Congress selected five topics to be discussed, reflecting on each of the Commissions of the Anti-Drug Campaign Command. Well.
In order for the meeting to receive more input, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun provided some additional guiding recommendations, including:
* 1: Dissemination and education: The National Authority for Combating Drugs in the new mandate considers education as the main method of combating drugs. In this regard, he instructed the General Secretariat and the Committee in charge of outreach to educate the President on how to inspire this drug destruction movement, a national movement in which all sectors must join together: such as education, culture, art, tourism, religion. Sports and so on.
* 2: Drug and Chemical Management: Propose to develop standards for SOP implementation procedures in order to strictly control all chemical compounds that can be processed into drugs. He strongly hopes that this inter-ministerial working group will carry out its duties and responsibilities under the spirit of high responsibility to eliminate cases of illegal drug processing in Cambodia.
He instructed the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs to send the conditions for the location of suspected drug processing to all sub-national authorities to have a basis to inspect any locations suspected of drug smuggling.
