This afternoon, Samdech President Hun Manet closed the meeting to review the work of 2023 and raise the work direction of 2024 of the National Authority for Combating Drugs
(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday afternoon, the 11th day of the month of Meak, the year of the Bronze Age 2567, which is on the 20th of February, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results of 2023 and Raise the 2024 target of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and disseminate the 9th plan to fight against illegal drugs.
Drugs have become a serious problem in Cambodian society after trafficking and consumption became more serious. Samdech Hun Manet considered the fight against drugs as a necessary task for social security, and Samdech issued a hot order for the relevant authorities to fight effectively.
In order to fight the drug effectively, Samdech Hun Manet decided to change the composition of the National Authority for Combating Drugs by appointing four Deputy Prime Ministers as the head of this authority, and leaders from 14 other government ministries and institutions as members. .
Samdech President Hun Manet also announced to take strong action against the Armed Forces, the army and the National Police, by expelling them if they are found to be involved in drugs. A number of military and national police forces were also expelled after being found to be involved in drugs.
According to the report of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, in 2023, the authorities cracked down on a total of 8,063 drug crimes and arrested a total of 20,002 suspects. Nearly 3 tons of drugs were seized. Seized 1 ton and 469 kg of chemical compounds. Burned and neutralized more than 347 tons and 1,207 drugs and related substances.
