The following is a letter from civil society organizations: How important are the 10 key recommendations of Samdech Techo and the 10 recommendations of Samdech Thipdey for the betterment of Cambodian workers?
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results of 2023 and the work direction of 2024 of the Ministry of Labor on February 08, recommended 13 points for the Ministry of Labor to implement successfully.
Out of these 13 recommendations, the third recommendation is that Samdech Thep Dey encourages the Ministry of Labor to implement the 10 key recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, and the 10 recommendations issued by Samdech Thep Dei on August 29, 2012. 2023 ago to be highly effective.
Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and an expert in political science, stated that the 10 recommendations of Samdech Thipdey are important values of the leadership in continuing to pay attention to the well-being of the people, workers, youth and peace. Cambodia's socio-economic development starts from the solid foundation of the health and well-being of the people throughout the country.
Samdech Thipdey's 10 Recommendations Instruct the Ministry of Labor to Discuss Workers' Wages, the Implementation of the Social Security System for Workers in the Informal Economy, 1.5 Million Vocational and Technical Training Programs, Financial support for pregnant women before and after childbirth, create a program to turn an enterprise into a safe community from 2024 onwards.
In addition, the four recommendations that the Ministry of Labor to implement in the next two years are to cooperate with the relevant ministries to establish community nurseries and kindergartens, set up restaurants or canteens in factories, change the means of transporting workers for health and Safety and promotion of skills testing of workers, both domestic and foreign, to obtain a certificate of professional recognition.
As for Samdech Techo's 10 key recommendations, Dr. Yong Pov sees them as invaluable recommendations for workers working in Cambodia. Because there are benefits for workers, especially for pregnant women before and after childbirth, as well as health protection of workers through the implementation of social security.
At the same time, Dr. Yong Pov hoped that the Ministry of Labor and relevant ministries and institutions will continue to implement the 10 key recommendations of Samdech Techo to be stable and sustainable for the benefit of workers to maintain social, economic and political stability in Cambodia. "Workers are the main productive force of the society in the industrial sector," he said.
