Third: National Social Assistance Program: There are two types: Type 1: National Social Assistance Program in the family package: Cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years old, providing scholarships to poor students in primary and secondary education, sponsorship Cash for people with disabilities, cash support for the elderly 60 years and older.
Category 2: Social protection in response to disasters, including natural disasters (hurricanes, floods), public health crises, macroeconomic and financial crises.
Fourth: National Strategy for Informal Economic Development: There are many people engaged in informal economy throughout the country. This work is large, interconnected from the Ministry to the capital-province, which is very busy to organize a practical work system for informal economists.
Fifth: Coordination Mechanism and Financing Program: The Royal Government drops the $ 100 million budget in the beginning and can allocate more if necessary. This mechanism aims to help farmers achieve high incomes, balance production, maintain food security ....
To achieve this goal, the Ministry of Agriculture and Commerce is working together on a number of tasks, including: Establishment of a coordination group between the two ministries, providing guidance to the capital-provincial level to establish a joint working group, monitoring the development of rice prices. In regional and global markets and ready to buy stockpiled rice for food security and price stability.
Sixth: Deployment of Commune / Sangkat Agriculture Officers: In response to this policy, the Ministry of Agriculture, in collaboration with the Ministry of Public Function, has organized the first phase of recruitment of 250 officials and set another 800 communes for the second phase in April.
In addition to the above achievements, Mr. Pen Bona also highlighted some other important achievements in the fields of justice, public functions, land and security.
Civil Service Sector: In this sector, the Ministry of Public Function led by Mr. Hun Many has led many reforms, including two recruitment examinations, including the recruitment of 250 commune agricultural officials and the recruitment of educators. 100 body and sports. Both of these contests are very good, transparent and acclaimed from all walks of life. In general, no abnormalities, no suspicion arises.
The Ministry of Public Function has also been leading many other reforms, such as strengthening institutional capacity, strengthening management and capacity building of civil servants, improving the provision of public services.
