Norway to facilitate transfer of tax funds to Palestinian Authority
(Oslo): The Norwegian government has announced that it will facilitate the transfer of tax funds that Israel has collected and frozen to the Palestinian Authority through a network of pro-Western units. This is according to the release by Reuters on Monday, February 19, 2024.
Under the 1990 Interim Peace Agreement, the Israeli Ministry of Finance collects taxes on behalf of the Palestinian Authority and is subject to a monthly transfer to the Palestinian Authority, but the October 7 attack by Hamas has stalled the process.
Norway says the interim solution will reopen payments and prevent the collapse of the Palestinian Authority by being able to pay salaries and provide essential services such as schools, health care and more. According to Norwegian Prime Minister Jonas Gahr Stoere, "this underscores the need for greater stability in the region and for the Palestinian Authority to be able to protect its people."
Under the settlement agreement, backed by Israeli and Palestinian officials, Norway will work as an intermediary to handle the revenue Israel has been collecting since October 7. Photo by Reuters Ratanakkiri provincial governor has ordered a halt to gambling. Temporary online across the province
(Rattanakiri): Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Rattanakiri Province, on February 18, 2024, ordered all police stations and district police inspectors to stop all online TV gambling (lottery). Temporary.
The provincial governor's order came after the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Manipur Hun Manet, ordered the provincial governor to suspend all licenses to provide additional gambling venues at the local level.
At the same time, Samdech Thipdey instructed the Cambodian Gambling Management Committee under the Ministry of Economy and Finance to chair an urgent meeting with the authorities and all stakeholders to review and reorganize, including the principles and management of gambling. Various across the country.
Samdech has ordered the Capital and Provincial Board of Governors to take immediate action to inspect gambling venues at the local level within its jurisdiction. To revoke the license in the province or across the country.
Chea Touch Noodle Factory in O'Yadao District, Ratanakkiri Province, is busy buying fresh cassava without having to ship it to neighboring countries, but complains of a lack of workers due to the large production line.
She said that every day, the company can buy from brokers from some provinces such as: Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Kratie, Stung Treng and Ratanakkiri.
She said the factory can produce 1,200 tons of fresh cassava into 300 tons of cassava flour in 24 hours. Purchase of fresh cassava to the factory on February 19, the price per kg is 500-520 Riel according to the market in Vietnam, and 21% is deducted according to the actual type of cassava (soil, roots, waste) and skilled workers and ordinary workers. Get a decent salary by providing accommodation, food and shelter.
Ms. Chea Touch added that the plant can produce about 200,000 tons of noodles per year for export, especially to China. However, she complained about the shortage of labor and the high cost of electricity, shipping to China (via Vietnam) was not very profitable, but the rest of the cassava, fertilizer, animal feed sold for some money.
