February 9, 2001 - Elected Prime Minister of Thailand.
February 1, 2003 - He launches a large-scale campaign against drug crimes that kills more than 2,800 people.
February 28, 2008: He returns to Thailand to protest corruption allegations.
August 22, 2023: He is finally repatriated after 15 years in exile and is immediately taken to a prison in Bangkok after a court sentenced him in absentia to eight years in prison for rape. Power and conflict of interest.
August 23, 2023: He is taken to a police hospital in the Thai capital due to health problems.
August 31, 2023: He submits a request for a royal pardon from the King of Thailand.
September 1, 2023: He receives a pardon from the King, reducing his prison term from eight years to one year.
February 13, 2024: The Thai Minister of Justice announces that Thaksin is among 945 prisoners who will be released early.
