Key Remarks by Samdech Mani Hun Manet on the Groundbreaking Ceremony for the Construction of the Bridge over the Bassac River (Chak Angre Krom-Prek Pra) worth More Than 60 Million USD
(Phnom Penh): The construction of roads and bridges for the benefit of the nation and the people is a necessary policy that the Royal Government of Cambodia led by the Cambodian People's Party has adopted since the time of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Coming to the new blood leader, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet also continues to adopt this policy.
On the morning of Monday, February 10, 2024, the bridge over the Bassac River (Chak Angre Krom - Prek Pra), another bridge across the river in Phnom Penh began. The construction process is now official. The groundbreaking ceremony for the bridge was presided over by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, the opportunity to open the construction site of the bridge across the Bassac River (Chak Angre Krom - Prek Pra):
* President Hun Manet stated that in recent years, the increase in traffic has increased rapidly, leading to severe traffic congestion.
* President Hun Manet stated that the main goal of the Royal Government for more than 40 years is to eradicate poverty and improve the living standards of the people by ending the flames of war and promoting development.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the policy of connecting infrastructure helps people to travel more easily, faster and reduce travel time.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government has no plan to set a ceiling for citizens.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen strives to end the war and build peace. Therefore, at all costs, we must work together to maintain peace now and in the future.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the stronger the road, the stronger the hope, the greater the road, the greater the hope.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the goal of infrastructure development in Cambodia has not diminished.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet said that the road is like a blood vessel, so the road to where to help feed the organs there.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that roads are not only used for migration, but also contribute to the promotion of factories and jobs for the people.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that Cambodia currently has 25 bridges across the river. Of these, 19 bridges have been completed, 3 bridges are under construction and 3 bridges are under study.
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet stated that where the road is built, it shows that Nong has a well-developed population.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government has no plans to move the capital from Phnom Penh.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government has no plans to ban people from having children and forbidding people from buying vehicles.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that roads in Phnom Penh can no longer be widened.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet instructed the Phnom Penh Royal Administration to prepare to release vehicles to transport people to visit their hometowns on the occasion of the traditional New Year.
* President Hun Manet stated that Cambodia's ambition is not only to build roads, but also to build their own through the training of engineers.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that so far, China has helped build a total of 16 bridges across the river.
* President Hun Manet stated that China has become the number one country in providing loans, concessions and assistance for the development of Cambodia.
* President Hun Manet requested the Chinese government to continue to support infrastructure projects in Cambodia, such as the "Prek Chik Techo-Funan project, light railways and subways."
* President Hun Manet stated that Cambodia has been striving for more than 20 years to build a peaceful and stable image of Cambodia, only recently through foreign media and a number of issues affecting Cambodia's image of stability.
* President Hun Manet revealed that there were people trying to intervene to help two Taiwanese Chinese who made videos of bad stories from Cambodia, but Samdech refused.
* President Hun Manet stated that those who use Cambodia to produce videos to get more viewers will have to take legal action. After taking legal action, he will be expelled from Cambodia.
* Samdech Mani President Hun Manet warned people with bad intentions towards Cambodia not to dare. Cambodia will take strong action against those with bad intentions.
* President Hun Manet expressed the hope that the year of the Cambodian-Chinese people change in 2024 will be a part of neutralizing the wrong information in the past.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet calls on drivers not to be afraid of police arrests, to have the spirit of respecting the law, not to drive too fast, not to drink alcohol.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that what the Royal Government wants is for drivers to drive with a sense of responsibility, understanding, tolerance and not endanger the lives of others.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on drivers who cause traffic accidents not to try to escape, to take responsibility.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet calls on transporters not to overweight and check the technical specifications.
The March 8 International Day Campaign is a global event declared by the United Nations General Assembly as the 1977 United Nations Day on Women's Rights and World Peace.
Every year, the Kingdom of Cambodia organizes the International Women's Day March 8 campaign to commemorate the struggle for equal rights and freedoms and to reflect on progress, achievements, challenges, commitments and positive measures in promoting gender equality and empowerment. To every woman and girl.
The theme of this year's Cambodia Campaign has been designed to respond to the context of social development in the digital age and in line with the vision outlined in the Royal Government of Cambodia's Phase 1 Strategic Strategy and Policy Framework. Height, gender equality and empowerment of women and girls.
