Interior Ministry Spokesman: Thirty-nine people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on February 18
(Phnom Penh): At least 39 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on February 18, 2024 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on February 19, 2024.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 39 suspects, 28 were arrested in 19 drug cases and 11 were arrested in seven criminal cases.
On the morning of Monday, February 10, 2024, the bridge over the Bassac River (Chak Angre Krom - Prek Pra), another bridge across the river in Phnom Penh, began construction. Officially. The groundbreaking ceremony for the bridge was presided over by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The bridge across the Bassac River (Chak Angre Krom - Prek Pra) is the first bridge construction project for the new Royal Government led by Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet. Through this project, it is clear that the sustainability of the Royal Government's nation-building comes from the Cambodian People's Party, even though the Prime Minister has been changed.
According to the report, the bridge across the Bassac River (Chak Angre Krom - Prek Pra) is a twin concrete bridge with a length of 845.7 meters, starting from the west bank of the Bassac River in Chak Angre Krom, Meanchey district and the end point. Born Tonle Bassac in Sangkat Prek Pra, Khan Chbar Ampov in Phnom Penh.
The road connecting the head of the bridge has a total length of 804.3 meters, connecting from both ends of the bridge to the main boulevards in Phnom Penh. The road connecting the head of the bridge will be built according to the technical specifications, including the road connecting from the west side of the bridge with a length of 379.15 meters and the east side with a length of 425.15 meters will be constructed as a concrete road 9 cm thick, 20 m wide, 27 m wide.
The project also includes the construction of two roundabouts on either side of the bridge and four sidewalks on each side, with a total length of 1,541 meters, paved with reinforced concrete, as well as the construction of two road extensions, including National Road No. 2. 300 meters on the west side and 110 meters on the east side, 110 meters on the east side to connect with the bridge and the arrangement of signs and traffic signs according to the technical standards of the road.
The project will be built by a Shanghai construction company and technically supervised by Guangzhou Wanan Technical Consulting, with a construction period of 42 months to be completed during 2027, with a total budget of $ 60.2 million. The United States, a concessional loan from the Chinese government, together with the Royal Government of Cambodia's contribution to address the impact of demining, unexploded ordnance and other taxes.
The bridge over the Bassac River (Chak Angre Krom - Prek Pra) is an important strategic project to connect and facilitate people's travel. In particular, reduce traffic congestion on the Monivong Bridge.
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, has ordered the revision of Article 10 of the Royal Decree on the Organization and Functioning of the National Council for Sustainable Development.
According to the Royal Decree, Article 10 has been amended to stipulate that the National Council for Sustainable Development has a General Secretariat as its secretariat for day-to-day operations, located within the Ministry of Environment.
The General Secretariat of the National Council for Sustainable Development is headed by one (1) Secretary General, accompanied by a number of Deputy Secretaries General who are appointed by Royal Decree or Sub-Decree.
The organization and functioning of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Sustainable Development shall be determined by sub-decree.
