This statement was made by Samdech President Hun Manet on the morning of February 19, 2024, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a bridge across the Bassac River (Chak Angre Krom - Prek Pra) worth more than $ 60 million. Phnom Penh.
Samdech President Hun Manet said that the main goal of the Royal Government in the seventh mandate and the previous mandate is to promote economic growth and create more jobs. Transforming lakes, forests, rice fields, landless areas into agricultural areas, pushing electricity, factories to the base, which has created jobs for many people.
Samdech Hun Sen also said that if by the end of 1998, the policy of victory of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, Cambodia had just ended the civil war for about 25 years. But under the umbrella of peace throughout the country, the lives of Cambodians have increased rapidly over the past 25 years.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet continued that from 1979 to 1998, Cambodia did not completely end the war because the Khmer Rouge still had its forces in the mountains. And much of the national budget is spent on ammunition and weapons for battle, and much of the national labor force is sent to hire troops to fight on the battlefield.
