Dr. Kin Phea: Education Campaign is really needed to prevent fires in factories and the tourism industry
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results of 2023 and the work direction of 2024 of the Ministry of Labor on February 08, recommended 13 points for the Ministry of Labor to implement better. Moreover, while the recommendations of the President in the past, the Ministry of Labor has successfully implemented.
For the recommendation of the 10th point of the President to the Ministry of Labor to cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions to organize education campaigns and dissemination throughout the country to promote and raise awareness to workers, authorities at all levels and The public on fire education, prevention and control measures in enterprises and businesses in the manufacturing and tourism industries.
Regarding this recommendation, Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, stated that he really appreciates and fully supports the recommendation of the President, because the fire may occur eventually, which requires measures to educate and Prevent clearly.
Dr. Kin Phea said that in order to successfully implement the recommendations of the Ministry of Labor, it is necessary to have clear measures related to education to understand the causes of fires. At the same time, there must be education for workers to understand the first aid when a fire occurs.
The President of the Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia added that the Ministry of Labor must also cooperate with factory owners across the country to set up safe exits, fire hoses and evacuation drills. From fires and so on.
At the same time, the Ministry of Labor must cooperate with other relevant ministries and institutions such as the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Environment and local authorities to promote firefighting in a timely manner to avoid causing serious harm to workers and factory owners.
783 first-year students and second-generation students of Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri University, Ministry of Education, ready to enter the first year
(Kandal): 783 first-generation and second-year students of Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri University took the entrance exam for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports for the academic year 2023-2024 to prepare for the first year.
This exam was held on February 18, 2024 in the presence of Samdech Preah Mongkul Tepachary Vong Aneta, Samdech Preah Sang, Deputy Director of the Judicial Committee of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Rector of Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri University. And Mr. Touch Visal Sok, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Please be informed that Samdech Preah Moha Sangka Reach Bour Kri University was established in the cause of education for the benefit of all generations of Cambodian children to provide opportunities for all Cambodian students to continue their bachelor's degree without charge. No, that is, the university offers students a 100% scholarship from the first year to the fourth year, which is the graduation year.
In addition, Samdech Preah Moha Sangka Reach Bour Kri University also cooperates with many foreign universities to send students to study in the third year at any foreign university as long as they pass the exam, especially English.
Please note that this university has 6 faculties, including: Faculty of Arts, Humanities and Languages, Faculty of Science and Technology, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Engineering and Architecture, Faculty of Development and Tourism, and Faculty of Science. Economics and Business with a total of 32 majors. Senior officials of the Ministry of Health remind pharmacists to abide by the professional standards of pharmacists in order not to face the revocation of licenses.
(Phnom Penh): Pharmacist Ban Botta, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chairman of the National Council of Pharmacists of the Second Mandate, on February 18, 2024, presided over the dissemination ceremony on Pharmacist Professional Standards to Pharmacists. Nearly 1,000 people from Phnom Penh participated.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Ban Botta said that the purpose of today's program is to disseminate to pharmacists in Phnom Penh to understand the standard of justice on behalf of pharmacists should be implemented to improve the well-being of the people.
In addition, Mr. Ban Botta urged pharmacists to adhere to the professional standards of pharmacists in order not to face the revocation of licenses.
Pharmacists claim that when participating in outreach programs, pharmacists gain a lot of knowledge about various legal documents related to the provision of medical services. In addition, they are committed to the proper implementation of the professional standards of pharmacists.
Please be informed that the Pharmacist Professional Standards were established for four main purposes, including:
* First: To introduce the quality, safety, efficiency and professional ethics of medical services to the public.
* Second: To be used as a tool to monitor and evaluate the professional practice of pharmacists in Cambodia.
* Third: To provide input into the preparation of training programs prior to employment, as well as to provide guidance to pharmacists practicing medicine and medical students.
* Fourth: to be used as a basis for professional development, continuous and improve the quality of pharmaceutical services. Pharmacist professional standards have been implemented by the Ministry of Health since 2023.
Cambodian Representative to Attend the First Meeting of the National Report on the Implementation of the International Convention for the Protection of All Persons from Enforced Disappearance in Geneva, Switzerland
(Phnom Penh): A delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia will visit the first national report on the implementation of the International Convention on the Protection of All Persons from Forced Disappearance, which will take place on 19-20 February 2024. In Geneva, Switzerland.
Cambodia is committed to the promotion and protection of human rights through the ratification and accession of eight of the nine major international human rights conventions and conventions, of which Cambodia is the only country. The only one in Southeast Asia that ratified and became a member of the International Convention for the Protection of All Persons from Enforced Disappearance on 27 June 2013.
It should be noted that as a State Party to the International Convention for the Protection of All Persons from Forced Disappearance, Cambodia has the obligation to submit a report to the Committee on Forced Disappearance and to send a delegation to review the report. In front of this committee in the form of constructive dialogue.
