(Phnom Penh): Following the outbreak of Kovid 19 at the end of 2019, sales activity in each market has dropped sharply. So far, although the Kovid 19 outbreak has eased and the economy has begun to show signs of recovery, some traders are still complaining that their sales have not returned to normal.
Ly Sodeth, a senior economist at the World Bank in Cambodia, said that after the outbreak of Kovid 19, the global economic infrastructure has changed, causing sales activity to be unprecedented.
He said that despite the return to normal activity of the 19-Kovid epidemic, market sales could not return to normal and earn less due to changing economic activity. If traders want to improve their sales activities as before, change the method of sales, such as online sales. And at the same time, good business can only be good if money is circulating in the economy.
"The market is not the same as it was before the Kovid outbreak. Despite the economic recovery, sales will not be able to return due to the fragmentation," he explained. . "This has led to some people switching from sitting in the market to selling at home, and some are starting to increase their online sales."
