Minister Hun Many Shows Support for Strict Measures to Crack Down on Two Foreigners Who Produced Incitement Videos in Sihanoukville
(Phnom Penh): Mr. HUN Many, Minister of Public Works, on February 17, 2024, expressed his full support for the Royal Government's strict measures to crack down on two foreigners who produced provocative videos. There is chaos affecting security issues in Cambodia, especially in Sihanoukville itself.
According to Mr. Hun Many, serious measures to crack down on all these crimes as a warning message not to allow such crimes to be committed in the future, regardless of whether committed by foreigners from any country. He sees the production of this provocative video as a preparation of a scenario to distort what is actually happening in Cambodia, which is peaceful under the shadow of peace.
"Recently, Sihanoukville authorities cracked down on two foreigners who produced video content with the aim of inciting public opinion about security issues in the Kingdom of Cambodia. This is a scenario filmed with the pure intent of these two foreigners to distort what is actually the situation in the Kingdom of Cambodia, which is peaceful under the shadow of peace.
All these acts have seriously damaged the honor and image of the Kingdom of Cambodia that can not be tolerated. I hope this does not happen again.
I would like to support the Royal Government to take drastic measures to crack down on all these crimes as a warning message not to allow such crimes to be committed in the future, regardless of whether committed by foreigners from any country. At the same time, I would like to call on all my compatriots and friends to prevent the distribution and dissemination of content that distorts the truth and incites misunderstandings on our society.
Sihanoukville Provincial Court has sentenced two Taiwanese nationals to two years in prison and fined 4 million riel each for making fake videos of incarceration and torture. Incitement to cause serious disturbance to social security committed in Village 6, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville under Articles 494 and 495 of the Penal Code.
