Malaysia's economy grows slower than expected
"Growth has slowed amid a competitive external environment," the central bank said in a statement. "This is due to slower global trade, declining global technology cycles, tighter geopolitical and monetary policy."
The slowdown in economic growth in China, Malaysia's largest trading partner, has weighed on Malaysia's exports and economy. Other Southeast Asian countries also suffered. Singapore failed to meet its GDP target for 2023, while Indonesia and the Philippines also saw slower growth last year.
Once Asia's fastest-growing economy, Malaysia has been facing declining exports since March. The decline affected the manufacturing sector, which grew just 0.7 percent last year from 8.1 percent in 2022. According to Bloomberg News.
