According to Mondulkiri provincial authorities, during 2006 Khim Sam Ath, alias Ta Barang, traveled to Mondulkiri province and asked Thou Kling, also known as Ta Kamlous, to buy a plantation of 274 hectares of land. , 950 square meters located in Trapeang 3, Putong Village, Chong Plas Commune, Keo Seima District, Mondulkiri Province, with a land use application dated June 30, 2006 issued by Mr. Lat Limkun, Chief of Chong Plas Commune.
In early November 2023, Thou Kling, alias Ta Kamlous, a resident of Pu Tong village, Chong Plas commune, Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province, stole a large portion of 15 hectares of land belonging to Khim Sam Ath, alias Ta Barang, and sold it to Pang Borin and Song Irun's name is Van Chheng Oung, the first deputy head of the commune's commune. No.
