(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on the afternoon of February 16, 2024, chaired a meeting to disseminate the criteria for identifying model villages and data collection procedures in villages in rural areas of Cambodia.
The event was attended by the Permanent Secretary of State, the Secretary of State, the Undersecretary of State, the Director General, the Deputy Director General, the Director General of the Department, as well as a total of 108 leaders and professional officers. Separately, the director, deputy director of the department and civil servants of the 25 provincial departments of rural development participated in the virtual system (Zoom Meeting).
According to Mr. Oeun Thearith, Director of the Community Development Department, the Model Village Development Working Group has developed the model village criteria according to five main criteria, including: (1) Economy, (2) Social Affairs, (3) Health and Environment. Live (4) infrastructure and (5) good governance, which in each of the main points have clear detailed criteria.
In order for this work to be carried out effectively, the Minister recommended the following:
1. 30 model villages in 3 provinces that have been implemented in the past and existing achievements shall be evaluated according to the form of established criteria.
2. Officials from the 25 specialized departments and rural development departments of the capital and provinces must cooperate well and participate in the implementation of this work to be highly effective.
3. Prepare a summary report on the results of the model village evaluation and a meeting to discuss, experiment and improve the criteria to assess the level of development of all villages throughout the country.
4. Select villages that are favorable and have potential in key areas such as culture, tourism, nature, economy and agriculture to develop as model villages.
Egypt prepares Gaza border for Palestinian shelter
Egypt is preparing an area on the border with Gaza that could accommodate Palestinians in the event of an Israeli attack on Rafah, leading to mass evacuations across the border, four sources said on Friday. In what they described as an emergency measure by Cairo. This is according to a report released by the AFP news agency on February 16, 2024.
Egypt, which has rejected such arrangements, has repeatedly warned of the possibility that a deadly Israeli attack on Gaza could lead to the evacuation of Palestinians to Sinai, something that Cairo says is not the case. Absolutely acceptable.
A source said that Egypt was optimistic that talks aimed at reaching a ceasefire could avoid such a scenario, but that the country was taking precautionary measures by setting up temporary camps along the border.
Three other security sources said that Egypt had begun to equip the desert with some basic materials that could be used to provide shelter to the Palestinian people, stressing that this was an urgent task.
