Speaking at the FRESH BUSINESS program, Ly Sodeth, the World Bank's senior economist in Cambodia, said that the World Bank had forecast for Cambodia's economic growth in November that global growth in 2024 would be only slightly better than 2023. The growth rate is around 5.8 percent, while in 2023 the economic growth will be 5.4 percent.
Mr Ly Sodeth said that economic growth is a measure of GDP between the old and new years, so to predict the economic sector, four sectors are needed: real sector, foreign sector, fiscal sector. And the monetary sector, which reflects the economy as a whole.
Mr. Ly Sodeth made the remarks during a panel discussion on "The Situation of Cambodia's Economic Development in 2024".
"Obviously, during the 19 crisis of Kovid, a small number of countries have maintained good economic growth because they have a way of exporting or producing high value-added products," he said. "Such as the production of televisions, cameras or cars, which are high value-added and competitive products."
