On that occasion, the Minister led a team to inspect the progress of the canal to send water to save dry rice of farmers in Prey Kabbas and Samrong districts with a total length of about 5 km and had a face-to-face meeting with them. Farmers who grow dry rice in the above area.
Please be informed that about 1,200 hectares of dry paddy land in Kampeng commune, Prey Kabas district and in Trea commune, Cheung Koun commune, Samrong district, Takeo province are facing shortage of irrigation water.
According to the Minister, as of today, the progress of the construction of the canal, which started on February 12, 2024, reached 3,500 meters and the construction of 87 canals to facilitate the waterway from the Angkor Borei River has reached 100%. As a result, the intervention team rescued about 580 hectares of dry season rice farmers in Prey Kabas district and about 620 hectares in Samrong district.
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin said on Thursday that Russian families should have at least two children to sustain the country's ethnic identity and possibly three or more. Better yet. This is according to the release by Reuters on Friday, February 16, 2024.
Russia has paid large numbers of troops, but no figures have been released since the nearly two-year war of aggression in Ukraine, and hundreds of thousands of people have fled the country for fear of being targeted by the government. Speaking to employees of a factory in the Urals, Putin said a family with two children was appropriate for Russia to maintain its identity.
"If we want to survive as one ethnic group or as a multi-ethnic group living in the same Russia, we must have at least two children," Putin said. "But if each family has one child, the population will decrease, and for growth and development, the Russian population must have at least three children."
