Banteay Meanchey Military sends eight suspects to drug court
(Banteay Meanchey): At 23:30 on February 14, 2024, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Base Force led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, Municipal Gendarmerie Local Commander, conducted an operation to crack down on drug distribution and use cases. Detaining eight suspects.
The eight suspects include:
Colonel Nuon Ninaro, Poipet City Gendarmerie Base Commander, said that before arresting the suspects, on the night of February 14, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie patrolled the city to maintain security and order in the city. Until 23:30, the force patrolled to the above point and found eight suspects were drinking on the street in front of a rented room, leading to insecurity on the street.
Immediately, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie stopped the interrogation and tested for drugs in the urine with a positive result (+). After that, the local police force of the Municipal Gendarmerie arrested the 8 suspects and brought them to the Municipal Gendarmerie base for processing.
After the authorities arrested and interrogated the eight suspects, they confessed that they actually used drugs. Based on the confession, the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of anti-drug work, said that the crackdown was authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated the procedure. Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
The suspect has now been sent to the Provincial Court by the Anti-Drug Office of the Provincial Gendarmerie on Friday morning, February 16, 2024 to follow the procedure.
Kampong Chhnang Provincial Authority Dismantled Branches and Barriers at Boeung Thom Lake in Choul Kiri District
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Pich Keo Mony, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, this morning, February 16, 2014, received an order from Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Provincial Governor, to lead a joint team to inspect and dismantle large-scale fishing offenses. One is at Boeung Thom in Kampong Basrov village, Chulsa commune, Chulkiri district.
After actually inspecting the use of illegal fishing gear, the perpetrators cut down the flooded forest trees and put them in a net and surrounded the three-hectare nets and mosquito nets next to the conservation lot. At the above point, the Deputy Governor also ordered the professional officers of the Fisheries Administration and the fishing community to dismantle the poles and remove them and burn them there.
Representatives of the Prek Chtor community, who led the force to dismantle the barrier and remove the branches from the water and burn them on the mainland at Boeung Thom in Kampong Basrov village, Chulsa commune, Chulkiri district, said that all these Only 10 people like today took at least 3 days to complete, because some branches also have thorns that are difficult to pull and lift on another boat to push ashore to drop the pile to burn.
In particular, on the morning of February 16, 2024, he also visited the above crime scene with Mr. Pich Keo Mony, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, and the Deputy Governor also ordered professional officers and fishing communities. Completely dismantled, the twigs are brought ashore to be burned, and some of the twigs next to the conservation lot are transported to the dump to be used as a fish sanctuary.
Please note that for the offense of cutting down the flooded forest branches, use it as a snare and use a net to surround the snare to catch fish that are up to several hectares in size and are placed next to the fish species conservation lot. Boeung Thom point in Kampong Basrov village, Chulsa commune, Chulkiri district, Kampong Chhnang province was demolished by the Fisheries Administration on February 12, 2024.
