(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Puthivuth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, on February 16, 2024, confirmed that the Digital Government Committee is urging ministries and institutions to have a digital revolution team to help accelerate digital government policy.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Sok Puthivuth, Chairman of the Organizing Committee of the Digital Government Forum 2024 and the Digital Government and Digital Technology Exhibition, presiding over the press conference on the Digital Government Forum this morning, February 16, 2024.
Mr. Sok Puthivuth stated that "Currently, through the Digital Government Committee, we are urging each ministry-institution to have a digital revolution team to help accelerate the development of digital government policies quickly and effectively."
In addition, Mr. Sok Puthivuth stated that the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has set out the Digital Government of Cambodia Policy for 2022-2035, which has 4 goals, 10 strategies and 83 priority action plans.
According to Mr. Sok Puthivuth, under the leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathipadei Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, the President has set out the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, setting out five key points: * Human capital development * Economic Diversification and Competitiveness * Private Sector Development and Employment * Sustainable Development and Environment * Digital Economic and Social Development.
Mr. Sok Puthivuth highlighted that the first phase of the Pentagon strategy to support the vision in 2050, which makes Cambodia a high-income country.
At the same time, Mr. Sok Puthivuth said that in order for Cambodia to have a high income, we must promote a digital society in Cambodia. A digital society that can use the latest technology to drive the country's development to its full potential.
Mr. Sok Puthivuth added that in order to have a digital society, we must promote a digital economy to strengthen the competitiveness of the Cambodian economy, and to have a digital economy, we must promote a digital government as a nursery to promote. And support the development of the digital revolution in Cambodia.
Gangsters fight and use tricks to enter people's houses, steal a motorbike, decided in Svay Teap district, the authorities have already targeted
This case happened at 9:10 pm on February 14, 2024 on National Road 1 in Leap village, Kandieng Reay commune, Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province.
According to reports from residents, before the incident, a group of gangsters, about 7 to 8 people came to stop the motorcycle for dessert, but after a while, another group of teenagers were close. Ten people on a motorbike arrived at the scene and rang the motorbike.
While the children were eating dessert, they picked up stones in their hands to protect themselves, some even dragged motorbikes into the houses of the locals. Meanwhile, a group of children on a motorcycle arrived and started arguing and threw stones at the gangsters.
Later, the owner of the motorcycle that the gang stole disappeared, checked the security camera in the house and saw the gang member stealing the motorcycle and went to complain to the authorities to intervene.
He said that now the authorities have identified all the targets, but because the media leaked too quickly, the gang escaped, however, the authorities are working to build a case to the police to cooperate to arrest all the gangsters. Legal punishment is inevitable. Official Outcome of the Meeting between Samdech Hun Manet and the Ambassador of the Republic of the Philippines to Cambodia
