The Ministry of Environment has been closely monitoring the air quality in Cambodia, while the air quality situation is improving.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khvay Atiya, the spokesman of the Ministry of Environment, said this morning, February 16, 2024, the Ministry of Environment has been closely monitoring the air quality using equipment and quality control stations. 51 wind locations across the country.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said that in general, air quality in Cambodia was in good condition. Good because there are some necessary factors such as:
1: The working group monitored the air quality in the towns regularly, which was published on the Ministry's social media and some media outlets, which now covers the air quality monitors in all major towns, cities and in Phnom Penh.
2: The expert team regularly inspects and inspects air pollution sources according to the situation and necessity of each pollution source.
3. Strengthening legal documents and strategic plans to support air quality protection, such as: Sub-Decree on the Management of Air Pollution and Noise, Circular No. 01 on Measures to Prevent and Reduce Public Air Pollution, Cambodia Clean Air Plan, Strategic Plan Environment 2023-2028
4. Cambodia is in a favorable condition with the size and amount of pollution sources are still small and the air flow in cities and towns is good.
At the same time, the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries also issued a notification on measures to prevent and prevent wildfires to all competent institutions, sub-national administration, government officials, armed forces, communities, students, monks and all citizens. To clearly understand the duty to prevent and fight wildfires in close cooperation with specialized units under the auspices of the two ministries.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment stressed that the Ministry of Environment was promoting clean energy such as solar energy, wind power and hydropower, preventing pollution from factories, and promoting the use of Euro 5 energy for next year's transportation.
