(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, said that participating in blood donation is a very meritorious donation because it contributes to helping people.
He said this on the occasion of Dr. presiding over the voluntary blood donation program organized by the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia (ACC) in collaboration with the National Blood Transfusion Center on February 15, 2024.
The Voluntary Blood Donation Program is in line with the high recommendation of the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on the promotion of voluntary blood donation, as well as the call for the National Blood Transfusion Center to save your life. Diseases in hospitals that need blood.
The event was attended by the leadership and staff of the National Blood Transfusion Center, as well as a total of 94 voluntary blood donors, including customs and excise officials at all levels, staff and private sector representatives.
Dr. Heng Sok Chamroeun, Vice President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, emphasized that blood donation is very important to save the lives of patients because so far there is no medical technology that can produce blood. At the same time, the benefactors themselves also receive health benefits from donating blood.
She thanked all the benefactors of the General Department of Customs and Excise for their generous and especially facilitated and participated in today's event.
In addition, Customs and Excise officials and staff of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia also volunteered to donate blood within the framework of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and directly organized at the General Department of Customs and Excise for the first time. On February 7, 2023. Participating in blood donation is a very meritorious donation because it is a contribution to save people's lives.
At the same time, the Minister accompanied the Prime Minister also encouraged Customs and Excise officials, staff and representatives of the private sector to continue to do good deeds with love and save lives by donating blood in the future.
The Prime Minister also thanked the leadership, customs and excise officials, staff, representatives of the private sector, as well as teachers, doctors and staff of the National Blood Transfusion Center for participating in the voluntary blood donation program at the General Department of Customs and Excise. Cambodian Excise today.
