Will the US Congress approve $ 60 billion in aid to Ukraine to continue the war against Russia?
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The US Senate, which controls a majority of Democrats, has approved a $ 95.34 billion bailout package for Ukraine, Israel and Taiwan. The budget proposal will be submitted to the Senate for further approval. Will the proposed budget package, which includes $ 60 billion in aid to Ukraine, be available?
The budget will be sent to the House of Representatives, which is controlled by a Republican majority, for final approval. But hopes were low because House Speaker Mike Johnson had previously vowed not to support the bill, even after it was passed by the Senate.
Why did some Republican senators change their minds?
Several days ago, Democrats in both houses of parliament were said to have opposed the proposed military aid package to Ukraine, but the change of heart was blamed on Donald Trump's campaign rhetoric. An election campaign in South Carolina last weekend.
The $ 95.34 billion package includes $ 61 billion for Ukraine, $ 14 billion for Israel in the war against Hamas and $ 4.83 billion for assistance to US partners in the Indo-Pacific region. There is also Taiwan and China's threat prevention.
US President Joe Biden has been pushing for the US House of Representatives to approve a package of aid to Ukraine, but for months the proposal has been blocked. Republican opposition, especially in this House of Representatives. The Biden administration's pledges to continue providing aid to Ukraine have been stalled since late 2023.
