The following is the full text of the announcement: Gross insurance premiums in Cambodia continue to increase to more than $ 342 million by 2023, while insurance premiums increase by approximately 32%
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Bou Chanphiro, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, emphasized that the Cambodian insurance sector has grown remarkably fast and is playing an important role in supporting the social security and national economy by the insurance market in Cambodia. Cambodia has an average annual growth rate of about 20%, while in 2023 gross premiums will continue to increase to more than 342 million US dollars.
Mr. Bou Chanpirou emphasized this at the ISJ Overseas Workshop on "Mission of the General Insurance Sector for the Welfare of All" co-organized by the Cambodian Insurance Regulator, the Japan General Insurance Association, the Japan General Insurance Institute and the Cambodian Insurance Association to share. Experience and knowledge in the field of insurance, raise awareness and strengthen the capacity of insurance skills that can contribute to the development of the insurance market.
The workshop was held at the Phnom Penh Hotel for two days from 15 to 16 February 2024, with the participation of the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, Mr. Bou Chanpirou, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, Mr. Huy Va. Tharo, president of the Insurance Association of Cambodia, represented a large number of insurance companies and higher education institutions.
Mr. Bou Chanpirou, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, highlighted that with the political stability and economic growth that Cambodia has maintained over the last two decades, the Cambodian insurance sector has grown remarkably fast and is moving. The role is an important component in supporting the social security and national economy.
"Obviously, the market is growing at an average annual rate of about 20%, with gross premiums continuing to reach more than $ 342 million in 2023," he said. There are 41 insurers operating in Cambodia with assets of more than $ 1 billion, including 18 general insurers, 15 life insurers, seven micro insurers and one reinsurance company.
