(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan, through the Embassy of Cambodia, has signed a total grant of US $ 828,546 to three recipients under the Grants for Small-Scale Human Security Project (Kusanoni Grant).
The grant agreement was signed on February 15, 2024 by Mr. Ou Inu Assushi, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia, and Mr. Heng Ratana, Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center, Mr. Yi Songki, President Battambang Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Soy Sona, Director of Ratanakkiri Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
For this help to implement the following projects:
* First: Demining projects in three provinces in the northwest of Cambodia (US $ 515,060) Recipient: Cambodian Mine Action Center
* Second: Project to build a school building at Ping Pong Primary School, Bavel District, Battambang Province (US $ 88,900) Recipient: Department of Education, Youth and Sports, Battambang Province
* Third: Project to improve the post-harvest operation of cashew nuts in Ratanakkiri Province (US $ 15,060) Recipient: Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Rattanakiri Province
Japan's Kusanoni Grant began in Cambodia in 1991 to support Cambodia's efforts to develop and rebuild the country at the grassroots level.
The grant aims to protect vulnerable people from a number of factors, such as poverty and / or misfortune, that could directly threaten their lives, livelihoods and dignity, as well as promote their self-reliance. Communities. Since 1991, the Government of Japan has provided more than $ 69 million to local authorities and NGOs to implement 691 Kusanoni projects throughout Cambodia.
