The ceremony was attended by His Excellency the President of the National Assembly, Dr. Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and other senior leaders of the Ministry of National Institutions of Cambodia.
"Although today is the occasion for this celebration, I would like to remind you that as a Japanese person, 2024 has started with two tragic events: the earthquake In the Noto Peninsula and the plane crash at Haneda Airport. The emperor and empress are deeply concerned about this catastrophe and danger.
On behalf of the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, I would like to take this opportunity to express my gratitude to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Royal Family of Cambodia, Royal Government and the people of Cambodia. Express sincere sympathy with all your heart.
In these difficult times, he was encouraged by friendship and compassion, and many Japanese people were overjoyed at the generosity of the Cambodian people. In response to Cambodia's encouragement, the Japanese government will do its utmost to rehabilitate and rehabilitate earthquake-affected areas on the Noto Peninsula.
"Cambodia-Japan has once again celebrated the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries, an important event in the history of the two countries' diplomatic relations," he said. To mark the occasion, the two countries' bilateral relations have been upgraded to a "comprehensive strategic partnership."
Many great events were held throughout the year, and the program, which was held on December 8 to celebrate the close of the 70th anniversary, was a resounding success, with the high presence of four Deputy Prime Ministers and Many other Cambodian dignitaries, the most important guests of Japan in the 64th birthday of the Emperor of Japan at this time.
This year, he hopes to embrace the movement established in 2023 to further strengthen Japan-Cambodia relations. This year is the year of the factory, which is believed to bring about real change. With this belief, this year aims to achieve a lot of practical development in Japan-Cambodia relations, which has already been strengthened by trust and friendship.
To achieve this, he intends to monitor the outcome of last year's summit and work to ensure that our relationship is mutually beneficial. He wants the two sides to work together to pay attention to the "first phase technical strategy" put forward by the new cabinet to achieve a digital society, strengthen connectivity and improve the investment climate.
Moreover, as the international situation becomes more complex and we face many global challenges, it is important that Japan and Cambodia work together as partners to uphold international law and maintain international order based on the rule of law. .
