(Phnom Penh): Mr. Justin Kevin White, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia, expressed his interest in the "Funan-Techo Canal" project, a project to connect waterways between rivers and seas in Cambodia.
The Australian Ambassador's interest in the Cambodian canal project was expressed during a meeting with Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia on the morning of 14 February 2024. This.
During the meeting, in addition to expressing interest in the first major canal project in Cambodia, the Ambassador also praised Cambodia's mission to attract investors from other countries and pay attention to better infrastructure development.
During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol briefed the Australian Ambassador on the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to attract investors. In 2023, Cambodia received 268 investment projects with an investment capital of nearly 5 billion US dollars, a high increase compared to 2022, which received nearly 4 billion US dollars.
For January 2024, Cambodia received 32 investment projects. Compared to January 2023, there are more than twice. The Deputy Prime Minister expressed the expectation that investment projects will increase further despite the current global situation.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol also emphasized that in order to reduce the cost of transportation, the Royal Government has launched a comprehensive master plan on the Cambodian transport and logistics system 2023-2033. In addition, to increase competitiveness, Cambodia aims to use clean energy to 70% of total energy by 2030.
