(Gaza): Negotiations to end Israel's war with Hamas and the release of the remaining hostages entered a second day in Cairo as of Wednesday as Gaza residents prepare for an Israeli attack. On their last shelter in Rafah. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on February 14, 2024.
A Hamas source told AFP that a delegation had traveled to the Egyptian capital to meet with Egyptian and Qatari mediators after Israeli negotiators held talks with them on Tuesday.
The mediators are working to end the fighting ahead of the full Israeli invasion of Rafah, the last stronghold of more than 1.4 million Palestinians.
The alarming possibility of civilian casualties has prompted an urgent call for Israel to stop sending troops to this last major population center, even from its close allies. The United States, a key ally, has said it would not support any ground operation in Rafah without a "credible plan" to protect civilians.
Israel has led a series of airstrikes on Rafah and rescued two hostages in a special commando mission. According to the United Nations, the humanitarian crisis that could result from the Israeli invasion of Rafah could be catastrophic and lead to massacres.
The raid on Rafah could also cause problems for Egypt, including concerns that Hamas fighters may disguise themselves as Palestinian refugees entering Egyptian territory.
