Last Saturday, Myanmar's military regime announced a law on military service that would apply to men between the ages of 18 and 35 and women from 18 to 27 for up to two years. According to Myanmar media reports on Tuesday, based on a government government spokesman, military service will begin in April, after the Thingyan New Year.
Veterans who have retired in the last five years will also be called back to the army, the source said. Myanmar has enacted a law requiring military service since 2010, but it has not been implemented so far. Under the law, those who evade military service could face up to five years in prison.
