Russia claims 3 dead, 13 wounded in Russian airstrikes in eastern Ukraine
Ukrainian authorities claim that three civilians, including a child, were killed and 13 others were injured. About 100 patients were evacuated to nearby hospitals after part of a hospital in Selydove was damaged by Russian airstrikes.
Both Russia and Ukraine have denied targeting civilians in their airstrikes. Both sides claimed that the attacks, most of which were aimed away from the front lines, were to destroy military power and transport infrastructure.
Conservationists find 20 rare reptile eggs, 206 nests in Koh Kong province
(Koh Kong): From early January 2024 to the present, the Royal Turtle Conservation Team or Fibers of the Fisheries Administration and Wildlife Conservation Society (WCS) has found 20 nests of turtle eggs with a total of 206 eggs on An artificial beach near a breeding pond in the Koh Kong Provincial Reptile Conservation Center.
According to images taken by automatic cameras taken by the team on the beach, several turtles emerged from the breeding pond to lay their eggs between 8pm and 1pm. 4 in the morning. This is the fourth year that the royal tortoise has laid eggs in the center in Cambodia.
Conservationists expect to find more turtle eggs at the center during the 2025 spawning season, which runs from January to March.
Please note that the Koh Kong Reptile Conservation Center has played an important role in restoring the number of royal turtles. For example, 268 royal turtles are under care, including 118 newly hatched turtles in 2023. Center turtle breeding is a conservation goal of the WCS and the Fisheries Administration aimed at restoring the number of turtles in the wild.
The Royal Turtle is one of the 25 endangered species of freshwater turtles in the world and is listed on the IUCN Red List as the most endangered and representative species. To Cambodia since 2005.
