(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, February 14, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Hun Manet presided over the closing ceremony of the 2023 annual review meeting. Of the implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, Phase 4.
The 2023 Annual Review Meeting of the Implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform Program Phase 4 was held on 13 February 2024 under the chairmanship of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance; Chairman of the Steering Committee for Public Financial Management Reform.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has initiated the implementation of a "Public Financial Management Reform Program" that is comprehensive and covers all aspects of the national public financial system. The "Public Financial Management Reform Program" was officially launched on December 5, 2004 under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo as the then Prime Minister.
The vision of this reform program is to transform Cambodia's public financial management system from an input-centric and centralized system to one that focuses on results or achievements and is decentralized in line with international standards and excellence.
This reform program focuses on strengthening the efficiency and effectiveness of revenue and expenditure management of the state budget in order to support the implementation of sectoral policies of the Royal Government.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth also highlighted that after more than 20 years of implementation until the fourth phase of "Accountability Achievement", the Public Financial Management Reform Program has made great progress and is proud of its role. Important as a lever for the economic and social development of Cambodia. Based on the 2023 progress of the implementation of the fourth phase of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, the Royal Government can assess that:
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth highly appreciated and provided valuable comments to the colleagues of the Royal Government, the leaders of ministries and institutions, all relevant units under the Ministry of Economy and Finance, who have worked hard to promote the implementation of activities under the reform program. Manage public finances until good results should be proud.
