(Phnom Penh): At least 51 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on February 13, 2024 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on February 14, 2024.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 51 suspects, 44 were arrested in 20 drug offenses and seven were arrested in seven criminal offenses.
More than 820,000 polling stations across Indonesia opened at 7 a.m. and closed at 1pm (local time) on Wednesday for nearly 205 million Indonesian registered voters. Elect the president, vice president, and members of parliament at the national, provincial, regional, and city levels.
Each presidential candidate needs more than 50 percent of the vote to claim victory without having to go through a second round of voting. However, if no candidate receives more than 50% of the vote, the two leading candidates will continue to run in the second round, the final round on June 26.
Indonesia's new president will be sworn in in October 2024. Photo by Reuters In the case of the robbery of foreigners in Sen Sok district, the Criminal Police Department led a crackdown on seven suspects.
(Phnom Penh): Seven suspects involved in the robbery of foreigners in Sen Sok district were arrested by the Criminal Police Department on February 12, 2024.
The robbery happened on February 10, 2024 at 4:00 AM, when the suspect used a knife to stab a Korean man in the left cheek to rob the property.
Pursuant to the orders of General Sar Thet, National Police Commissioner and Deputy Commissioner for Planning, and Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department.
On February 12, 2024, at 15:30, the forces of the Criminal Police Department, led by Brigadier General Hun Moniroth and Lt. Col. Hem Bona, Deputy Director of the Department, in cooperation with the Sen Sok District Police Inspectorate, arrested a number of suspects. 7 people at the point of concrete road, Khmuonh village, Sangkat Khmuonh, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
After questioning, all seven suspects were involved in a robbery in Phnom Penh. Of the seven suspects, one was involved in the robbery of a Korean man on February 10, 2024, along with other accomplices.
Currently, the department has handed over to the Sen Sok District Police Inspectorate for further processing.
Reuters reported, citing complaints, that EU tariff measures were not in line with WTO rules. Essential fatty acids are used in consumer products such as cosmetics and pharmaceuticals and industrial lubricants.
The European Union (EU) said in January 2023 that it would impose tariffs of between 15.2 percent and 46.4 percent on Asian fatty oil imports from Indonesia, which it said was hurting its industry.
"The tariff will help ensure fair competition between fatty acids imported from Indonesia and locally produced fatty acids," the EU said.
Indonesia's lawsuit, officially called a "request for consultation", is the first step in a dispute with the WTO. The measure gives both sides about 60 days to resolve their differences before a formal WTO panel is set up to resolve the dispute in the event of a non-settlement. According to Reuters.
