(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Tuesday, February 13, 2024, Mr. Chea Somethy, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, and Ms. Chea Phalkun, his wife, joined hands to give love by preparing food, gifts, food and supplies. For people with mental health problems who are living and being treated at the Disability Care and Rehabilitation Center in Bakou Village, Bakou Commune, Kandal Steung District, Kandal Province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, leaders of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Major General Chhoeun Sochet, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, as well as government officials and the Armed Forces in Kandal Province.
The Mental Illness Care and Rehabilitation Center was officially inaugurated on September 4, 2019. The center has the role of providing care for people with dementia to receive accommodation, food, treatment, care, counseling and rehabilitation to integrate into the community.
Mr. Ratanak Udom also said that the center provides rehabilitation programs for the mentally ill, such as: teaching literacy, painting, making towels, making soap, farming, sewing bags, cosmetics and mental health education counseling programs with the mentally ill. . Dementia accommodation is organized according to gender and severity of illness (severe or mild) based on a diagnosis by a team of specialists.
New cases of dementia or severe illness are kept in a separate room for easy monitoring and care. The psychiatric ward, both male and female, is equipped with bells in each room for those with mental health problems at night who can ring the bell to notify caregivers.
The director of the center said that for people with dementia, there are three meals a day, plus dessert twice a week.
Minister Chea Somethy expressed his condolences to the mentally ill and also expressed his condolences to the families of the mentally ill. However, the Minister encouraged families with mentally ill members not to abandon them, but to take care of them. In case of lack of access to care, Mr. Chea Somethy encourages to contact the center to bring members to the center to help care for and treat them.
Mr. Chea Somethy mentioned the social protection policy of the Royal Government since the old legislature led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the new legislature led by Samdech President Hun Manet is to give high consideration to the lives of the people without abandoning any citizen. No. That is why the Royal Government has introduced a social protection policy, which is a policy to help all people with problems in daily life.
At the same time, Mr. Chea Somethy praised the President of the Center as well as the staff in all centers who have made great efforts to take care of people with mental illness, despite the difficulties. The Minister encouraged the director of the center as well as all staff in the center to continue to take care of people with mental illness in the center better with a high sense of responsibility.
Mr. Chea Somethy also thanked the benefactors who jointly donated personal resources such as budget, food and supplies to support the center. The Minister also called on philanthropists to continue to contribute to humanitarian activities with the center, which is full of high value human activities at the center.
After the meeting, Mr. Chea Somethy and his wife, as well as the Governor of Kandal Province, government officials personally inspected the accommodation of people in distress and prepared food for them.
Despite the mental illness, some psychopaths received a warm feeling of love for the minister and his wife's visit and food preparation. They smiled happily as the minister and his wife handed out food to them.
