Svay Rieng Provincial Authority Resolves Rice Irrigation System for People in Chantrea and Kampong Ror Districts
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Sor Sodany, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, on behalf of Mr. Peng Pursa, Provincial Governor, on the morning of February 13, 2024, led a professional officer of the local authority and his colleagues to inspect the cultivation and water condition of the irrigation system in Chantrea district.
Mr. Sor Sodany said that today, on behalf of the provincial authorities, he led a professional officer to inspect the dry season rice cultivation work at Daun Toay irrigation system and to continue to inspect the shortage of dry rice irrigation water in Kork Tek village, Chantrea commune, Chantrea district.
He said that according to the inspection, it was found that the main canal carrying water from the Vietnamese canal was blocked off at some points without installing a drainage system. After inspecting such situation, he assigned the Chantrea District Administration and the Chantrea Commune Administration to resolve the excavation from the Kork Tek canal in order to have a waterway for farmers to irrigate 150 hectares of dry paddy rice in a timely manner.
It should be noted that this land canal has the capacity to irrigate 550 hectares and was restored during 2019 by the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology.
After inspecting the above location, the Deputy Governor and his colleagues continued to check the progress of the restoration of Boeung Chek Bek Chan and Prek Kampong Ror to be prepared as a reservoir as well as irrigation system to ensure irrigation of rice to the people. To the future as well.
