250 Commune Agriculture Officers Receive Training to Prepare for Duties and Provide Agricultural Support Services to Farmers
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nuth Chan Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, representing Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, on the morning of February 13, 2024, presided over the opening ceremony of the first orientation training course for agricultural officials in Krab commune. Khan 2023, 250 students at the Royal University of Agriculture.
Dr. Yang Saing Koma, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, considered the opening ceremony as a formal welcome to all 250 commune agriculture officials and the start of the first four-day orientation training course to prepare new officials. It fulfills its role and provides agricultural support services to farmers well and effectively.
He added that there are three types of training: 1: Orientation training, 2: In-depth training on key topics based on the needs of each commune, and 3: Learning from the practical implementation that will take place. Every 2-3 months.
Mr. Nuth Chan Sokha congratulated and welcomed the young commune agriculture officials who passed the final exam on December 17, 2023 under the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and under the supervision of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Fishing.
In addition, he provided advice and recommendations for the children of the 250 commune agricultural officials to pay attention to learning, respect time, use knowledge and skills to serve the people effectively, maintain honor, dignity and good cooperation. In performing the work. The trainers must pay attention to provide knowledge and experience to the 250 new officials and open the opportunity to participate in opinions and ideas for the progress of all.
Please be informed that the recruitment of commune agricultural extension officers is a total of 1,600 people, which is divided into 3 stages: in 2023, 250 people have been selected and are receiving training in 2024, 800 people and in 2025, 550 people.
