Announcing the Recognition of the President of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Ratanakkiri Province, Colonel Muy Sophat, replacing Major General Kham Suk, who has been transferred to a new position
(Rattanakiri): On the morning of February 13, 2024, Honorary General Dr. Kun Kim, Senior Minister, Vice President of the Cambodian Veterans Association and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, announced the transfer of duties of the Chairman of the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Ratanakkiri Province.
The announcement ceremony was held at Ratanakkiri Provincial Hall with the participation of the President-Deputy Director of several departments around the province.
According to the decision of the Cambodian Veterans Association, Colonel Muy Sophat was recognized as the Chairman of the Committee and the Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Ratanakkiri Province, replacing Major General Kham Suk, who was transferred to a new position.
He said, "The sacrifice of fresh flesh and blood of veterans is invaluable to the Cambodian people in the cause of seeking peace for the motherland." At the same time, we must continue to increase our activities to support our veterans and their veterans' families, especially when there are needs and problems that need to be addressed, and care must be taken to respond in a timely manner.
At the same time, the Honorary General Dr. Kun Kim would like to encourage all stakeholders to continue to support and cooperate for the Veterans Association at all levels in the province to perform their work better to contribute to the promotion of the role of the former. Warriors deserve the merits of veterans for the cause of the nation.
