(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) presented the results of the meeting to review and decide on the content of banners for voter education, educational video spots related to the 5th legislative election and the content. Summarize the book about the election process in Cambodia from 1993 to the present.
This meeting was held on the morning of February 13, 2024 in the presence of Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC.
After reviewing and discussing the documents on the agenda in detail one by one, the NEC meeting edited some of the contents and words on those documents and decided as follows:
* First, agree to establish voter education centers in three provinces, including Takeo, Kampong Thom and Kampong Cham, with educational banners published there for public research and understanding of the election. The Voter Education Centers in the three provinces operate under the technical and technical support of the NEC experts from the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia.
* Second: Agree on the content and images of 2 educational videos:
* An educational short story entitled The 5th Legislative Senate Election 2024. * An educational and training story on election procedures and vote counting for the 5th Legislative Senate Election 2024.
* Third: Agree in principle on the summary of the book on the election process in the Kingdom of Cambodia from 1993 to the present.
Mr. Prach Chan instructed Mr. Tep Nytha, Secretary General of the NEC, to clearly explain to the polling station officials the delivery, receipt and storage of important election materials before the day of the Senate election. 5.
