Minister of Rural Development Inspects Roads and Bridges in Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum and Prey Veng Provinces
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on 13 February 2024, led an official to inspect the condition of some roads and bridges in Kampong Cham and Prey Veng and Prey Veng provinces, where a number of roads were damaged. Measures to repair and build new roads for people to travel as well.
During the mission, the Minister inspected a 4,320-meter-long concrete road connecting Tuol Kor village, Tonle Bit commune, Tbong Khmum district to Tuol Khleang village, Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province, which was damaged by a 120-meter-long river bank collapse. . To protect the safety of people traveling on the damaged road, the Ministry of Rural Development has decided to build a new 1,500-meter bypass to replace the damaged road.
The construction of these three bridges began on March 15, 2023 and is scheduled to be opened to the public before the upcoming Khmer New Year. This construction project is within the framework of the Ministry of Rural Development's Phase 2 Disaster Management Project in Cambodia and Southeast Asia.
The Minister continued to inspect the road construction site of the weather-resistant rural infrastructure development project in Prey Veng province with the participation of Mr. Suon Somalin, Governor of Prey Veng Province.
