Information Minister Presides Over the First Meeting of the Anti-Fake Information Commission to Control Information Order and Information Security
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, chaired the first meeting of the Anti-Fake Information Commission to manage information order and information security.
The first meeting of the Anti-False Information Commission to manage information order and information security was held on the afternoon of February 12, 2024 at Chaktomuk Mongkul Hall, chaired by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information.
The Anti-Fraud Commission, an internal mechanism of the Ministry of Information, was established on November 24, 2023, chaired by the Minister of Information, to oversee information order and information security.
The Commission also has the duty to take legal action against any false information that is socially polluting, which could be detrimental to national security, political stability, harmonization, social order and prestige of Cambodia.
(Stung Treng): On the afternoon of February 12, 2024, the Immigration Police Station at Trapeang Kriel International Border Crossing, Stung Treng Province, held a ceremony to announce the appointment and transfer of duties of the new Trapeang Kriel International Border Police Chief.
