According to a statement issued by the Ministry of Interior on February 6, 2024, Colonel Ouch Mean has been appointed as the new Immigration Police Chief at the Trapeang Kriel International Border Crossing, replacing Colonel Nhem Borim, who has been transferred.
Lt. Gen. Sok Veasna stated that all immigration police officers must understand their roles, duties and rights within the framework of immigration police officers who have completed their missions at international border checkpoints, such as:
* Checking the documents of cross-border travelers * Efforts to find out other relevant legal documents * Liaise with institutions stationed at international border gates as well as neighboring countries to Facilitate people, national and international guests to cross the border and trade with each other.
The lieutenant colonel urged all immigration police forces to pay attention to the control of cross-border crime and crime, as well as to strengthen security work for the people along the border as strictly as possible.
