Information Minister Offers 9 Recommendations for Additional Inputs to Radio Operators in Cambodia on the Occasion of World Radio Day 2024
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Information, Mr. Net Pheaktra, on February 13, 2024, sent a congratulatory message to the owners of radio stations, producers, presenters, technicians and journalists of radio institutions in Cambodia and around the world on the occasion of Radio Day. The 13th World on February 13, 2024.
World Radio Day was established with the aim of raising public awareness of the importance of radio in daily life and as an opportunity to enhance cooperation and exchange of experiences between operators of radio institutions to develop and Modernize radio stations to meet the needs of the public and the social evolution of digital technology.
He added that in the period of social, economic and technological development, and especially the development of digital technology, Radio Cambodia is focusing on increasing its operations by adapting through the integration of a new generation of diverse media, including images. And sound, as well as more widely disseminated, both traditional and modern, by creating a variety of topics to participate in educating and raising the knowledge of the Cambodian people.
With the remarkable achievements and achievements of the Ministry of Information, the Minister would like to take this opportunity to provide recommendations for additional input to the operators of radio institutions in Cambodia, paying attention to:
1: Pay attention to build and develop leadership and executive capacity to contribute to the transformation of information institutions into proactive and interactive public relations institutions effectively and efficiently.
2: Continue to improve and build the capacity to produce quality and innovative program content to improve the efficiency and quality of work through the approach of "new, real, fast and comprehensive, reliable and professional to connect all circles."
3: Continue to work together to protect the order of the media and information security in order to maintain peace and stability in Cambodia by disseminating quality information, adhering to the ethics and professionalism of the press.
4: Continue to strengthen cooperation and exchange experiences with each other to participate in the development of this media to grow under the principles of trust, equality, progress and interests.
5: Promote the integration of traditional media with modern media, paying particular attention to the digital transformation into its operations
6: Strive to strengthen the basic capacity of presenters and presenters and create more understanding of literature, culture, national traditions, etc. to avoid mistakes that may occur during the broadcast.
7: Continue to promote anti-trafficking, drug trafficking, traffic accidents and alcohol
8: Continue to promote the dissemination of safe village-commune policy in all forms to maintain social order
