Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Oddar Meanchey Provides Interest-Free Loans to 20 Poor Families in Banteay Ampil District
(Oddar Meanchey): Twenty poor families from some communes of Banteay Ampil district received interest-free loans from the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Oddar Meanchey province. The Cambodian Red Cross represents Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province and Chairman of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, with the participation of many other working groups on 12 February 2024.
On that occasion, Mr. Khin Nhean sent a message of greetings from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and Mr. Pen Kosal, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee in Oddar Meanchey Province, who always pays attention. For the well-being and livelihood of our people, especially the poor, widows, the disabled, the elderly, the helpless, the orphans, as well as the people affected by various natural disasters.
Mr. Khin Nhean said that, in fact, today, the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Oddar Meanchey province provided loans, which are the budget of the Cambodian Red Cross, as a small loan to 20 disabled families, widows, and poor families, in one case they can get a loan. 1 million riels without interest.
Mr. Khin Nhean stated that the loans provided to the poor people now are for various businesses and this money is not a gift, you can borrow up to 1 year without The money will be repaid every 6 months with 1 million Riel, will be repaid twice, the first time for 6 months, 500,000 Riel and the second time for another 6 months, 500,000 Another riel for the Cambodian Red Cross to give back to the poor.
