Ministry of Culture: Unethical composition, the Ministry will summon writers and performers for educational guidance
(Phnom Penh): Officials of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts on February 12, 2024 stated that in the case of unethical composition, the Ministry will summon writers and performers for education and guidance.
The statement from the Ministry of Culture came after a comedian recently sang and produced a music video to promote online gaming.
Pok Borak, director of the film department at the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, stated: "In this case, I would like to inform you that the ministry does not have a policy to control the composition of the song, this is a principle of respect for freedom of expression. "In the case of unethical composition, the ministry will summon writers and performers for education."
With this, Mr. Pok Borak continued that he also checked that the music video has been deleted from the media and the artist who performed it has also released an apology video.
At the same time, regarding the issue of artists, the Khmer Artists Association issued a statement declaring that it does not support any artist who uses his name as an artist and commits inappropriate acts.
The statement stated, "In order to protect the face, honor and dignity of artists in general, especially to participate in protecting the invaluable values of our nation's fine arts and culture, the Association strongly does not support you. "Any artist or individual uses the name of an artist and goes to do inappropriate things."
At the same time, Dr. Kin Phea, a social observer, said that Neay Kroeun's new song was a warning sign for social morality.
Please be informed that due to strong reactions from experts and the public, the director released a video apologizing publicly and decided to delete the song from the online game from social media on the evening of February 12, 2024.
