(Phnom Penh): Our Earth is about 4,600 million years old, going through its history through many eras, such as the Pre-Brian Age, the Paleozoic, the Mesozoic, the Xenophonic, and so on. In terms of earth history, what era are we living in?
The time we humans are living in is not yet out of the ice age. Geologists have defined the "ice age" as an age in the history of the earth where the polar regions are covered by ice. The current Ice Age begins 10,000 years ago, during the Fourth Ice Age.
People think that this warm period will end at some point, and the current widespread view is that the warm period during the Ice Age will last from 12,000 to 50,000 years (not From various effects by human works).
No one understands why these figures change over the tens of thousands of years, but other possible factors are the location of the continents, the atmosphere, the changes in the Earth's orbit around the sun, and even the orbit. Of the sun around the galaxy as well.
