In December 2022, the G7, the European Union and Australia banned the use of Western maritime services, such as insurance, flag hoisting and the transport of Russian oil tankers, valued at $ 60 or more. Per barrel. This is part of Western sanctions aimed at reducing Russia's potential for war in Ukraine while trying to maintain a good oil supply market.
Since October 2023, the United States has sanctioned about 27 Russian tankers for transporting more than $ 60 worth of Russian oil while using Western maritime services.
