The fruitful results summarized by Samdech Hun Sen are as follows:
* First, politics, diplomacy, security: The two sides discussed a lot, focusing on the continuation of cooperation in all fields and raising the level of bilateral relations from "a strong partnership for peace and prosperity in 2017" to " "Strategic partnership", the highest point in the history of diplomatic relations between the two countries.
Through raising the level of this relationship, it will expand the scope of relations in all fields, and that relationship is not only the Royal Government, but the people in the private sector, education, culture and agriculture are opening the way to strengthen relations between the two countries.
* Second: Economy: The Royal Government of Cambodia has set out a number of initiatives, and the Royal Government of Thailand has agreed and continued discussions to strengthen mechanisms to strengthen trade relations. He also met with the Thai private sector by organizing a Cambodian-Thai business forum to attract investment to Cambodia.
The main goal of the Royal Government of Cambodia is to promote economic development and job creation for the people, and therefore the prince strives to attract investors from Europe and Asia. On that occasion, the Royal Government of Cambodia signed five Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs), including an agreement between the Cambodian and Thai customs to facilitate this work.
Cambodia and the Thai government have agreed to extract oil from overlapping areas after a 20-year stalemate. The agreement with the Thai side to take oil in the overlapping area is in the national interest, not an act of treason as the unscrupulous claim.
* Third: Labor: The Royal Government of Cambodia has a constitutional responsibility to protect the Cambodian people wherever they are, so in Thailand both sides have agreed to establish a Consulate General in Songkhla to provide Ease of protection for people working in southern Thailand, reducing visa fees by 2027, mobilizing the social security system between the two countries and including seniority.
