Third. I would like to encourage you to implement the 10 key recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister and the 10 recommendations that I set out on August 29, 2023 to be highly effective.
Fifth. The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training must continue to increase the training of master's degree technical skills to fulfill the role of middle level manager in the production chain of enterprises and establishments, and this training program must be organized for internships, practical work in Establishments for 4 to 6 months to ensure high quality, capacity, skills, productivity and competitiveness.
9th. In order to continue to improve the health and well-being of workers, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, in collaboration with relevant ministries and institutions, must continue to improve the implementation of occupational safety and health (OSH) in the workplace to reduce Maximize occupational hazards and risks.
10th. The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training shall cooperate with the relevant ministries and institutions to organize education campaigns and disseminate widely throughout the country in order to promote and raise awareness among workers, competent authorities at all levels and the public about educational measures, Prevent, and prevent fires in enterprises and businesses in the manufacturing and tourism industries.
And 13th. I would like to take this opportunity to encourage all ministries and institutions to continue to participate in the proactive spirit in the implementation of public administration reform, decentralization and deconcentration and capacity development of civil servants to improve work efficiency, public financial management reform program and Relevant policies, and digital revolution to optimize public services in response to requests from the private sector.
At the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results and further direction of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, Samdech Hun Sen stated that the agreement with the Thai side to take oil in the overlapping area is for the national interest, not an act of treason. A nation like the ungodly mentioned.
According to the Prime Minister, the reason why Cambodia and Thailand are talking to take advantage of this is because they see energy security as a long-term strategy between Cambodia and Thailand. Without energy, things could not work, not even human beings could do anything without energy.
In addition to oil, there is also natural gas in the overlapping area, if Cambodia receives oil and gas, it will be sold to raise money for the state, while oil will be refined into gasoline or diesel to supply, he said. Local as well as job creation in more oil exploration areas.
Regarding the overlapping area, in addition to oil interests, Samdech Hun Sen also highlighted the water border work with the Thai side, with careful negotiations to ensure national sovereignty.
Negotiations to resolve the dispute over the overlapping claim area have been postponed for 20 years after the two countries failed to negotiate in 2001. The overlapping claim area covers an area of more than 26,000 square kilometers. The square is estimated to contain millions of barrels of oil and gas at the seabed.
