Banlung businessmen are busy selling ornaments and flowers to bring good luck during the Chinese-Vietnamese New Year.
(Ratanakkiri): As the traditional Chinese-Vietnamese New Year is approaching tomorrow, it is observed that vendors selling gifts and home decor during the Chinese-Vietnamese New Year seem to be very busy in Their sales.
In fact, on the morning of February 8, 2024, in the market in Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province, people, both men and women, rushed to buy goods to prepare for the celebration of the Chinese-Vietnamese New Year on the 9th. February 2024, tomorrow.
Li Leng, a Chinese jewelery seller in Banlung Market, pointed out that sales of Chinese jewelery and home decor during the Chinese New Year at her place this year seemed to be slightly lower than last year. Is down slightly from last year as some buyers cut back on purchases due to poor economic conditions.
Ms. Meng Hak, a fruit and flower seller, also said that sales this year seemed to be better than last year, although prices this year have risen slightly. Chinese nationals and Chinese connoisseurs flocked to buy fruits, flowers, and home furnishings. This makes her expect that her fruits and flowers will be sold out by this time.
Vendors in Banlung market also said that for pork, chicken, duck, these days, normal sales are not very good, but hope that people will be able to come and buy tonight because most of the meat. Do not buy much until the day when customers buy, and the price is normal every year, as long as the Chinese New Year or other festivals increase the price a little.
In a meeting to disseminate the sub-decree on the management of civil aviation security of Cambodia on the morning of February 8, 2024, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun affirmed that all inactive shortcomings that occur at all international airports must be corrected immediately. Completely abolished in accordance with the will of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun said, "Security must continue to be guaranteed from now on, not planned and guaranteed, so please ask the head of the institution, the head of the unit at the airport to visit and help. Plan with strength and material in mind. This is the responsibility of our committee to the Royal Government and the people is the biggest thing.
In this regard, the Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Committee for Civil Aviation Security of Cambodia instructed all heads of relevant units and institutions to reorganize their action plans to ensure security and order at all international airports. In particular, effectively implement the Sub-Decree on the Management of Civil Aviation Security of Cambodia.
Separately, for technical work and coordination with the capital, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun assigned Mr. Mao Havannal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, to be responsible for implementation. The long-term strategic plan will be handed over to Om Yentieng, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions and Deputy Secretary of the Secretariat of the National Counter-Terrorism Committee.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun stressed that all units must develop action plans, set SOP standards and promote services quickly to raise the profile of the Royal Government of Cambodia, because he sees the location of the International Airport as the first place to receive. Investors and tourists.
Please be informed that on January 12, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, issued a sub-decree on the management of civil aviation security of Cambodia. This sub-decree has 12 chapters and 25 articles.
This sub-decree defines the management of civil aviation security in Cambodia in order to enhance the effectiveness of civil aviation, protect the security and safety of passengers, pilots, ground staff, general public, airports, international airports, local airports and airports, as well as against Territorial violations related to civil aviation activities and while flying.
The National Committee for Civil Aviation Security of Cambodia is chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun, accompanied by a Permanent Vice-Chairman, 11 Vice-Chairmen and several other members. This National Committee shall act as a staff for the Royal Government to lead and manage the work of civil aviation security in Cambodia.
