He stressed that during this process, political parties must turn off their loudspeakers and suspend all their election campaign activities. The relevant Capital and Provincial Election Commission shall request the cooperation and coordination with other relevant authorities to take measures to protect security, order and order during the election campaign. All campaign activities must stop 24 hours before election day.
Cambodia-Thailand Business Forum, Duke Kith Meng stated that Hun Manet has always supported the private sector and adhered to the principles of multilateralism and international agreements.
(Thailand): Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council for Cambodia, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, under the leadership of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has always supported the private sector and adhered to Adhere to multilateral principles and international agreements.
This statement was made by Duke Kith Meng at the Cambodia-Thailand Business Forum co-organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the Thai Chamber of Commerce and the Thai Chamber of Commerce under the chairmanship of Samdech Manet on the afternoon of February 7, 2024. .
Duke Kith Meng stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out a pentagonal strategy, a long-term plan aimed at achieving Cambodia to become a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050.
At the same time, Duke Kith Meng also delivered a speech and noted the achievements made by the two countries' economic partnerships, especially the regular exchanges of leaders of the two countries, which really helped boost trade. And bilateral investment.
"Thai investors are among the most successful and prominent foreign investors in Cambodia, reflecting the deep ties between the two countries, and the main areas in which Thai companies are investing in Cambodia include agriculture, tourism," he said. And the retail sector. ”
He added that the key factors that make Thai companies suitable for Cambodia in Cambodia include: rapid economic growth at an average rate of 7%, low labor costs, free trade agreements, government incentives, geographical proximity and cultural ties. Between the two nations, which makes it easier to do business and understand each other.
Duke Kith Meng also encouraged the business community of the two countries to create and seize opportunities by using existing mechanisms such as the Greater Mekong Subregion, the Mekong Cooperation Framework (ACCMECS), which are conducive to trade facilitation. Services and business links in which Thai investors can set up production facilities in Cambodia and export finished products to ASEAN, ASEAN, China, Korea and the United Arab Emirates.
The Cambodia-Thailand Business Forum was held successfully and exchanged views on the investment climate and potential of business opportunities in Cambodia and Thailand, as well as the actual experience of Thai companies present and operating in Cambodia. This afternoon, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet closed the meeting to review the work of the old year and raise the work direction of the new year of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
