Looking back at the history of Cambodia under the Democratic Kampuchea regime, politicians divided into factions, divided into regions, caused serious destruction to the Cambodian people due to divisions, lack of unity, selfishness, selfishness. Thus, the achievements of a divisive political character can make it clear to the people that they are incapable of being real politicians.
The Peace Students for Democracy Association calls on voters of the Candlelight Party to consider how to vote for a party that has split into three parties. Therefore, not going to the polls is a good option for members of the constituency of the Candlelight Party, because if you go to vote, you do not know which one to vote for.
