In modern times, the image of the dragon is commonly used by the Chinese, that is, it is no longer the "exclusive property" of anyone. Chinese people believe that dragons can bring happiness and good luck, so in everyday life and in important ceremonies, the presence of dragons on various materials.
In Chinese literature, the word "dragon" is used in combination with many words to form expressions that compare different stories, especially representing strength, stamina, power and courage, which are the main elements of literature. Which is widely used by Chinese people and learners of Chinese characters.
According to the Chinese Lunar Calendar, the traditional Chinese New Year this year is the Year of the Dragon, so the Chinese people, who have a rich dragon culture and a special passion for dragons, believe that in this new year, the nation will be even more prosperous. Prosperous, peaceful, people live and earn a living.
