Sudan's 10-month war between its national army and paramilitary forces has devastated the country's infrastructure, triggering famine warnings and displaced millions at home and abroad.
Half of Sudan's population of about 25 million is in urgent need of humanitarian assistance and protection, while more than 1.5 million people have fled to the Central African Republic, Chad, Egypt, Ethiopia and South Sudan, according to the United Nations. Nation.
The United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) and the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) have launched a joint call for $ 2.7 billion to provide humanitarian assistance to 14 people. 7 million people.
(Bangkok, Thailand): At around 8 pm on Wednesday, February 7, 2024, His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and HE Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, His Excellency, led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Returns to Cambodia after a one-day official visit to Bangkok, Thailand.
At 8 o'clock this morning, Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Bandith led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to pay an official visit to Thailand at the invitation of Thai Prime Minister Setha Thavisin. The visit lasted only one day, but was highly valued for the cooperative relations between Cambodia and Thailand, which continued to bear fruit for the benefit of both nations.
Prime Minister Hun Manet became the first friendly country leader to pay an official visit to Thailand after the country formed a new government in September 2023. His Excellency Hun Manet's visit has received the warmest and most hospitable welcome since the groundbreaking of the Thai airport.
At the Royal Government of Thailand, the official welcoming ceremony was held with great pomp and ceremony by Mr. Setha Thavisin. The red carpet, the honor guard and the army were organized to welcome the visit of the Prime Minister.
Within the framework of strengthening political and diplomatic ties, the two heads of government agreed to upgrade the level of bilateral relations from "Strengthening Partnership for Peace and Prosperity" to "Strategic Partnership" for mutual benefit. Come for the nation and the people of both countries.
The two heads of government also discussed regional and global affairs, expressing appreciation for mutual support in international forums and promoting cooperation in the fight against transnational crime and fraud. Online system and building the border between the two countries into a border of peace and prosperity.
After the bilateral meeting, the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Thailand co-chaired the signing ceremony of the five Memorandum of Understanding and also issued a joint statement on relations and cooperation between the two countries.
During today's visit, Samdech's President Hun Manet, who is gaining popularity, also paid a courtesy call and discussed with Mr. Van Mohamad Namtha, President of the National Assembly of Thailand, and Prof. Phorn Phat Vichit Chhol Chhay, President of the Thai Senate.
The President of the National Assembly and the Senate highly appreciated the visit of Prime Minister Hun Manet to Thailand. The President of the National Assembly and the Senate expressed strong belief that under the leadership of the President, the relationship between Cambodia and Thailand will be better and stronger.
In the evening before his retirement, Hun Manet also presided over the Cambodia-Thailand Business Forum organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Thai Chamber of Commerce, as well as the Cambodia-Thailand Friendship Association. The forum was attended by 300 investors and businessmen from both countries from a total of 166 companies.
Through the Cambodia-Thailand Business Forum, this will be a new opportunity in the field of bilateral trade and investment between the two countries, as well as further strengthen the Cambodian-Thai friendship.
Cambodia and Thailand have set a goal of achieving a bilateral trade volume of 15 billion US dollars by 2025.
