(Phnom Penh): Although it is the private sector, all private security agencies must receive the necessary skills training from the General Commission of the National Police through the Department of Private Security Management to strengthen their capacity. This was stated by Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police on the afternoon of February 7, 2024.
On the occasion of presiding over the representative of General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, at the Closing Ceremony of the 57th Private Security Agency Training Course, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi affirmed that this training course is aimed at professional private security agencies. And clear skills in accordance with Sub-Decree No. 289 of the Royal Government of Cambodia and Instruction No. 033 of the Ministry of Interior.
In this regard, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi, on behalf of the General Commissioner of the National Police, encouraged and advised the Department of Private Security Management to continue to pay attention and encourage further training courses for private security agencies while the security agencies. The private sector is seen as an important support force for the local authorities.
After undergoing specialized training, the Deputy Commissioner-General requested that the private security agencies have the right attitude to participate in the work, adhere to what is right and must respect the qualifications of the private security agents with discipline. Ethics, use of private security uniforms and adequate equipment.
