Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha Asks Legal Study to Issue Clear Guidelines Allowing Vehicles to Turn Right at Red Lights Without Fines
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Aphisandit Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee, requested to study the legal aspects and issue clear instructions to allow all means to turn right at the red light. Not illegal and no fines.
The introduction of Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha was made this morning, February 7, 2024, during a meeting to review the results of road safety work in 2023 and raise the direction after he saw that the decision to fine or not fine. The way to turn right when the traffic light is red is still unclear.
In this work, Dr. Sar Sokha instructed Mr. Hem Yan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, to co-study with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to review and prepare a clear instruction on this case.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha, allowing all means to turn right at the red light is one way to alleviate current traffic congestion. However, when turning right at a red light, all drivers must give priority to those driving at the same blue traffic light, meaning they can turn when there is no other way to pass.
