The President of the Thai National Assembly welcomed the President's official visit and congratulated him on his election as Prime Minister of Cambodia. The President of the Thai National Assembly praised the official visit as the Prime Minister was the first friendly country to pay an official visit to Thailand after Setha Thavisin took office.
The Thai National Assembly President expressed his satisfaction with the good relations and cooperation in all fields between the two countries. He also expressed strong hope that relations between the two countries would be further strengthened and expanded after the official visit.
His Excellency Hun Manet thanked the President of the National Assembly of Thailand for his warm welcome. The President informed about the results of the working meeting with Mr. Setha Thavisin, especially the upgrading of the relationship between the two countries from "Partnership for Peace and Prosperity" to "Strategic Partnership".
He stressed that with the increase in relations, the two countries are committed to boosting cooperation in many important areas, including diplomacy, security, defense, trade and investment, people-to-people contacts and tourism.
