(Phnom Penh): The National Authority for Combating Drugs has confirmed that in the four years from 2020 to 2023, the authorities cracked down on and confiscated nearly 600 tons of drugs and chemicals and arrested more than 70,000 suspects. People.
In 2021, the police cracked down on more than 6,000 cases, including 9 cases of processing and arrested more than 13,000 suspects and seized more than 4 tons of 600 kilograms of drugs and nearly 85 tons of chemicals. .
In 2022, the police cracked down on more than 6,000 cases, including 10 cases of processing and arrested 15,000 suspects and seized nearly 15 tons of drugs and more than 504 tons of chemicals. By 2023, more than 8,000 cases have been cracked, including 14 cases of processing, and more than 20,000 suspects have been arrested, and nearly 3 tons of drugs and 469 kilograms of chemical compounds have been seized.
He pointed out that in recent years, the drug situation, both internationally and regionally, remains a challenge, both in the current situation and for the long term.
Due to the ongoing armed conflict in many places around the world and in the region, drug criminals are taking the opportunity to increase the production and cultivation of both synthetic drugs and addictive plants.
At the same time, Cambodia continues to be threatened, especially by the effects of drugs from the Golden Triangle. In particular, the transit of drugs by land, by post and by air, such as the transport and trafficking of drugs across the Cambodia-Laos border, the storage of hundreds of kilograms of drugs in geographical locations, capitals and provinces along the border and adjacent. Sea for export by land and sea.
In response to the drug situation, Senior Minister Prum Sokha, Deputy Permanent Secretary of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, requested all relevant ministries, institutions / professionals to increase border controls, focusing on transit traffic. Boundaries, especially chemical goods, are still lacking.
He also requested the exchange of information related to the transportation of drugs and chemical compounds between the units in the border area and the territorial authority of the capital and province, where companies, factories and enterprises are not yet fully used and regular.
