(Preah Vihear): Mr. Yos Phanita, Member of the Central Committee and Vice Chairman of the 8th Senate Candidate Group, said, "In order to support the candidacy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the President of the Senate for the 5th term, all constituencies throughout Preah Vihear Province must be prepared." Qualifications to prepare relevant documents, especially to take good care of health in order to participate in the election of the 5th legislature of the Senate on February 25, 2024.
Mr. YOS Phanitta expressed his great pleasure for the current meeting between the deputies and the Commune / Sangkat Council, which is the same senator election. He said that the election of senators has two types of constituencies: the incumbent MPs and commune councils.
Mr. Yos Panita pointed out that in Cambodia, there are two types of elections: general elections and non-general elections. The general election consists of parliamentary elections and commune council elections. In particular, non-universal elections include the election of senators and the election of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Councils.
He stated that in Cambodia, since 1999, there have been four non-universal elections for senators with a six-year term, and the fifth legislative election will be held on February 25. The coming year 2024. He also told voters about the election campaign from the 10th to the 23rd, the 24th is a white day and the 25th of February is an election day.
Mr. YOS Phanitta also instructed all voters in Preah Vihear province to take good care of their health and prepare official documents for the election day, which the Commune / Sangkat Councils and their deputies will go to the polls on. On February 25, 2024, for Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, to be the President of the Senate.
It should be noted that for the commune councilors throughout Preah Vihear city, there are 15 constituencies and for the commune councilors throughout Tbeng Meanchey district, there are 17 constituencies.
Minister of Water Resources presents the progress of water resources to the 7th National Assembly
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of February 7, 2024, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology presented the progress of water resources to the 7th National Assembly.
