The working meeting between the Third Committee of the National Assembly and the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology was held at the Bayon Conference Hall of the National Assembly with the participation of representatives of the 10 specialized committees of the National Assembly.
Dr. Loy Sophat said that the meeting was held to study and understand the field of work, which is the responsibility of the Third Committee of the National Assembly, the cooperation between the legislature and the executive to promote the implementation of the program. The policy and the pentagon strategy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly to be effective.
With the results achieved by the Ministry, the Minister also mentioned some challenges that need to be addressed, especially in the context that the world is facing climate change and global warming has led to changes in water regime. Rainfall, along with rapid changes in land cover, has affected the flow of water in the upper reaches of rivers or streams, as well as causing frequent floods and droughts that Cambodia has been experiencing.
