Samdech Thep Dey and Lok Chumteav Bandit Arrive in Thailand Safely
(Phnom Penh): After traveling for about an hour at almost 10 am on Wednesday, 13 Roch Khe Boss, the year of Panchasak, BE 2567, which is on February 7, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister Cambodia and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pich Chanmony Hun Manet have led a delegation to Thailand safely.
The visit to the airport in Bangkok, Samdech Thepdey and Lok Chumteav Bandith was warmly welcomed by senior officials of the Royal Government of Thailand, as well as the Cambodian Ambassador to Thailand and many other embassy officials.
At around 8 this morning, Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Bandith led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to pay an official visit to Thailand. The one-day visit comes at the invitation of Thai Prime Minister Setha Thavisin.
Accompanying the President and Lok Chumteav Bandit are Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Senior Minister, Minister and key officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia. As well as private sector leaders of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the official visit, the President and Lok Chumteav Bandit will pay homage to King Maha Vajiralongkorn, King Vejirak Klaus, King Yuhua, King of Thailand at the Royal Palace.
Samdech Hun Sen will also pay a separate courtesy call on the leaders of the legislature, including Prof. Phorn Petch Vichhit Chhol Chhay, President of the Senate, and Mr. Van Mohamad Namtha, President of the National Assembly.
For the meeting between Samdech President Hun Manet and Mr. Setha Thavisin will discuss work on bilateral and multilateral cooperation that provides mutual benefits. The two prime ministers will also preside over the signing ceremony of a number of documents on bilateral cooperation.
During his visit to Thailand, President Hun Manet will also deliver an opening speech at the Cambodia-Thailand Business Forum.
The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs emphasized that the current official visit of the President to Thailand will further strengthen the long-standing relations and traditional ties between the two countries in the spirit of "strengthening the partnership to Peace and Prosperity "for the mutual benefit of the people of the two countries as well as for peace, stability and prosperity in the ASEAN and international community.
It should be noted that Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Setha Thavisin, Prime Minister of Thailand, were elected by the National Assembly to be the Prime Minister on the same day, August 22, 2023. After receiving parliamentary support, the two leaders immediately called each other to congratulate and wish each other well.
Less than a month after becoming prime minister, on September 28, 2023, Setha Thavisin chose Cambodia, a neighboring country, to pay an official visit. The visit is also his first overseas trip as Thai Prime Minister.
Please note that Cambodia and Thailand established official diplomatic relations on December 19, 1950. The relationship was severed in 1962 and reunited in 1991.
