A young man from a poor family is learning technical skills because he wants to be a hero to help his family according to the instructions of the Minister of Labor
(Phnom Penh): A young man living in a poor family has expressed his ambition to become a hero to help his family get out of hardship and debt, as instructed by Minister Heng Sour Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
The minister once said: "Born as a child of the poor, do not be upset, but we must learn good skills and techniques to have a clear profession in the future, we will be a hero to save the family. Get out of poverty. ”
From a poor family in Phnom Penh, Ra Sopheap, who dropped out of 8th grade, decided to study home air conditioning skills at the Institute of Industrial Technology through a 1.5 million vocational and technical training program of the Royal Government.
Ra Sopheap, a mother who sells food in a wheelchair, stated that she decided to study this air conditioning skill to get a clear skill, easy to earn money to become a hero, a family pillar, to help solve poverty and to Get rid of debt as well.
In addition, Ms. Yong Sophea, the mother of young Ra Sopheap, expressed her happiness that her son went to study a specific skill to be a capital to find a job and earn money to support the family. At the same time, she also thanked Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, who always considered young people from poor families to attend this vocational and technical course.
