The whole world joins the Chinese New Year celebration night! "Central Chinese New Year Celebration Night" hosted by China Central Radio and Television "in Laos"
BEIJING, Feb. 1 (Xinhua) - A number of activities on "Chinese New Year Celebration Night" by the Central Radio and Television of China were held in Laos on February 1.
Lao Prime Minister Sonexay Siphandone praised a number of activities organized in Laos by China Central Radio and Television, adding that these activities have added color and fun to the cities of Laos, which has made tourism a success. It is growing and becoming more vibrant. Such cultural exchanges also give Laotians a better understanding of Chinese culture and art.
His Excellency Hun Manet will pay an official visit to Thailand on February 7, 2024 at the invitation of the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand Setha Thavisin. Ahead of the Cambodian head of government's official visit to Thailand, it was reported that Thai authorities had arrested a number of Cambodians living and working illegally in Thailand.
Prior to the visit in Thailand, many Cambodian monks, businessmen, traders and workers, including Thais, released a video welcoming the visit of President Hun Manet and expected that the cooperative relations of The two countries are growing, especially the mutual benefit between the Cambodian and Thai people.
In an interview published by the Thai newspaper Mithichun, the Thai Minister of Defense stated that the authorities were monitoring the activities of the Cambodian opposition in Thailand. "Thai police and information police are investigating the case and Thailand will not allow any foreigner to take Thai territory to carry out political movements against other countries, which is strictly against the laws of the Kingdom of Thailand," he said.
According to a press release from the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the official visit, the President and his wife will pay a courtesy call on His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej at the Royal Palace. The President will pay a courtesy call on the leaders of the legislature, including Professor Phorn Ket Vichit Thul Chhay, President of the Senate, and Mr. Van Mohamad Namtha, President of the National Assembly.
Samdech Hun Sen and Mr. Setha Thavisin will meet to discuss bilateral and multilateral cooperation that provides mutual benefits. The two prime ministers will also preside over the signing ceremony of a number of documents on bilateral cooperation. In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet will also deliver an opening speech at the Cambodia-Thailand Business Forum.
The upcoming official visit to Thailand by the President will further strengthen the long-standing relations and traditional ties between the two countries in the spirit of "Strengthening the Partnership for Peace and Prosperity". Reciprocal for the people of the two countries, as well as for peace, stability and prosperity in the ASEAN and international community.
