Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Set 10 Principles to Maintain Security for the 5th Mandate Senate Election
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Chairman of the Permanent Security Command for Provincial Elections, introduced the Permanent Security Command for Provincial Elections and set out 10 principles to strengthen and increase the effectiveness of election protection. Appoint a senator for the fifth term in 2024 to run smoothly, freely, correctly and fairly.
The 10 points were raised by the provincial governor on the morning of February 6, 2024 at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall during the meeting of the Permanent Security Command for the 5th legislative election for the 2024 Senate.
* First, to lead, monitor, organize, manage and use the relevant competent forces to ensure that the 5th Senate election in 2024 is conducted in a secure, orderly, and safe manner, without fear, without intimidation, without intimidation. And no violence
* Second: Consult and manage cooperation in security, public order and social security, as well as other areas of work at the request of the Provincial Election Committee.
* Third: Disseminate the principles, activities and results of the implementation of the duties and responsibilities of the CJP, as well as the content related to ensuring the security of the pre-election process and the election to the national and international public to understand and understand.
* Fourth: Gather information about incidents or events related to the security situation of the election process and information from all sources that affect the security environment of the election process in order to explain, clarify the reaction, neutralize the influence, avoid confusion from National and international public opinion in severe cases must cooperate with the competent authorities to implement legal measures
* Fifth: Manage, manage and use human resources, materials, technical equipment and all kinds of relevant departments and units in order to promote the success of the 5th Senate election in accordance with the NEC's calendar.
* Sixth, to disseminate relevant legal principles and legal documents in order to enhance the capacity of stakeholders to cooperate in ensuring better security, public order and security for the election to be better and more responsible.
Seventh: The Provincial Administrative Unity Command shall control, lead, command and monitor the implementation of the election security agencies with the police force, the military police and / or the Kampong Cham sub-military operation area, as well as the existing People's Defense Forces.
* Eighth: During the election campaign of the political party, the force to protect the hurricane or the march by foot or by all kinds of vehicles and around the premises of the meeting or public campaign, maintaining a neutral political environment.
* 9th: Continue to disseminate the plan No. 001/24 PK dated 3 January 2024 of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command on the protection of security, safety and public order for the process of the 5th legislative senator election. 2024 to the forces of the Provincial and Municipal Administrative Unity Command
10th: The commune / sangkat administrative post police must keep the residence of the voters as they came out to Kampong Cham city to wait for the election at the polling station in Kampong Cham city. CPP in Stung Treng Province Holds a Meeting to Review Work Progress and Work Directions for Implementation and Joint Planning for the Senate Election
