This morning, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet closed the meeting to review the work of 2023 and raise the work direction for 2024 of the Ministry of Social Affairs
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, February 6, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of 2023 and Raise the work direction for 2024 of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation established by Royal Kram No. NS / RKOT / 0105/001 dated 17 January 2005. The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation fulfills its mission as a staff to the Royal Government on the leadership and management of the social sector, veterans and youth rehabilitation.
As an effective management and leadership mechanism, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation regularly organizes annual work meetings and raises its work direction for the new year. On February 5, 2024, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation held a meeting to review the work in 2023 and set the direction for work in 2024.
After the opening ceremony, Mr. Chea Somethy continued to lead the conference on the 5th of February. The meeting allowed the leaders of the specialized units to intervene as well as provide various opinions from the leaders of the Ministry to improve the shortcomings as well as provide additional good ideas to promote better work.
At the opening ceremony, Mr. Chea Somethy praised the achievements of the Ministry in 2023. Mr. Chea Somethy thanked Mr. Vong Soth, former Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, for his dedicated efforts to lead the Ministry to achieve many achievements.
The Minister also commended the leaders and officials of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation for their joint efforts to work responsibly in 2023.
The Minister also thanked the relevant ministries, institutions, relevant authorities, the private sector, national and international organizations and development partners at both the national and sub-national levels for their past cooperation in implementing the Ministry's strategic plan to promote the social sector, especially Provide social services closer to the people in accordance with the actual needs and policies of the Royal Government that have been implemented.
Minister Chea Somethy also highlighted some new achievements that the Ministry has achieved in 2023. The Ministry has adjusted the structure of the Ministry to be in line with the evolving situation of the social sector, has prepared and officially launched:
The Ministry has hosted the 5th Asia-Pacific Conference on Persons with Disabilities from 15-17 March 2023 and decided to issue the "Phnom Penh Declaration", which has been jointly adopted. Important documents for countries in the Asia-Pacific region to implement to achieve the social and economic empowerment of people with disabilities during and after the Kovid-19 pandemic.
In addition, on December 5, 2023, His Majesty the King Hun Manet recently announced the implementation of the "National Social Assistance Program in the Family Package" and the "Social Protection Program in Response to Emergencies".
The National Social Assistance Program in the Family Package will benefit about 700,000 equitable families, equivalent to 2.8 million people, with a budget of 674.5 billion riels ($ 165 million) in 2024.
The National Social Assistance Program in the Family Package is a compilation of the National Social Assistance Program, a synthesis of existing programs combined with additional new programs to sustain people's livelihoods by adhering to the principles of environment and equity, as well as avoiding drastic declines. Accumulation of income for all equitable families, as well as for family members living with HIV / AIDS.
The National Social Assistance Program in the Family Package will benefit about 700,000 equitable families, equivalent to 2.8 million people, with a budget of 674.5 billion riels ($ 165 million) in 2024.
