Mr. Sun Chanthol considers the large investment projects for January to show the trust of investors in the leadership of Samdech Manet
(Phnom Penh): The report of the Council for the Development of Cambodia shows that in January 2024, Cambodia received up to 32 additional investment projects. Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, considered these investment projects to show the confidence of investors in the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen Net, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
According to the report of the Council for the Development of Cambodia on February 1, 2024, as of January 2024, up to 32 investment projects have been approved. According to the report, the 32 projects have a total investment of more than 187 million US dollars and can create nearly 29,000 jobs.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol told Fresh News that the profitability and sustainability of the production chain is the most important condition for every business. Therefore, before investing in any country, investors must study in detail the possibility of profitability, especially the factors of peace and social stability in the target country to ensure the sustainability of investment.
For the above brief reasons, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol affirmed that the decision to invest in Cambodia now shows the confidence of investors in the leadership of Samdech Manet in ensuring peace and stability. Stabilize Cambodian society to make their factory production chains run smoothly and seamlessly.
In addition, investors have confidence in the leadership of Hun Manet in making their investments fruitful through flexible, highly motivated and favorable investment policies. This is the emphasis of Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also considered these investment projects as the result of the policies, diplomacy, economy and the efforts of President Hun Manet over the past five months.
The Deputy Prime Minister reminded that as the Head of the Royal Government and the Chairman of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, Samdech Hun Sen has made great efforts to mobilize and persuade foreign investors to invest in Cambodia. In that, every trip abroad, Samdech Thipdey never misses business programs and meetings with investors.
