Mr. Lang Senghong confirmed this on the evening of February 5, 2024, on the occasion of the knife market signed an agreement with the odorless pig farm to bring organic pork to supply the market in Phnom Penh. Location: Kon Kambit Market, Borey Peng Huoth Branch, Boeung Snor, Phnom Penh.
According to Mr. Wei Vannak, the owner of the Chrak Kes Dam farm in Dang Tong district, Kampot province, who is a supplier of odorless or organic pigs, said that odorless pigs are pigs that are raised naturally and do not cause bad odors around the farm and Provides pure natural food. This pork is lean, lean, pink in color and tastes different from factory-fed pork.
Mr. Wei Vannak said that raising odorless pigs takes longer than feeding pigs from factories that provide nutrients to promote the growth of pigs, that is, up to more than 6 months, pigs can reach 100 kg weight compared to pigs. Factory feed that takes only 4 to 4 and a half months.
