(Battambang): After receiving a report from the local authority on the case of people injured by unexploded ordnance (Mine 69) in Samlot district on the afternoon of February 5, 2024, the Cambodian Red Cross branch with Mr. Sok Lou, Chairman of the Branch Committee, assigned a branch representative led by Mr. Pheng Sethy, Deputy Governor and a member of the Branch Committee, and his colleagues immediately visited and provided humanitarian donations to the victims.
It should be noted that Mr. Sim Sopheap, 55 years old, living in Phnom Rey village, Tatork commune, Samlot district, Battambang province, was injured by a landmine (69) left over from the war while he was traveling to the plantation to clear and sell to support his family in At around 9:00 am on February 4, 2024, he broke his left leg and injured his right calf and left forearm. He is currently being treated at Battambang Provincial Referral Hospital.
On that occasion, Mr. Pheng Sethy brought the condolences of Mr. Sok Lou, especially Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always cares for the families of the victims, regardless of caste, color, religion. Or any political trend, say, "Where there are difficulties, there is the Cambodian Red Cross" and share the grief over the incident that happened to the victims.
He also instructed the family to take good care of the injured, follow the doctor's instructions and wish a speedy recovery.
