(Kampong Chhnang): Dr. Sopheachar Ouk Rabun, Chairman of Kampong Chhnang Provincial National Team, accompanied by Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, on the morning of February 5, 2024, led the provincial, district, commune and relevant departments to visit. Farmers will inspect and rescue 230 hectares of dry rice fields in Svay Chrum commune, Rolea Bier district, which are in need of water for irrigation.
Mr. Dok Bunthon, Director of the Provincial Water Resources Department and Mr. Ngin Hun, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, inspected the pumping of water to dryland rice in the above area, said that the dry season rice crop in this area has not been severely damaged. No, we can pump water from the 20 May dam to the main canal and continue pumping to save time. Therefore, pumping water into the main canal above more than 10 days can save all the dry fields at this point.
Separately, Mr. Dok Bunthon said that in the dry season of 2023 and 2024, dry rice fields that lack water in Rolea Bier and Boribo and Kampong Leng districts have more than 1,000 hectares. So far, the provincial, district and relevant authorities have rescued a total of 1,000 hectares, and a small amount is still being rescued.
He added that today, the Provincial Department of Water Resources provided 300 liters of diesel to Svay Chrum commune authorities and 100 liters of fuel to the provincial Department of Agriculture. The governor of Kampong Chhnang province will also provide 400 liters of oil to be used to pump water from the 20 May dam to save 230 hectares of dry rice fields that are in need of irrigation water for another month.
(Banteay Meanchey): A group of veterinary officers cracked down on the transportation of more than 60,000 chicken eggs, equivalent to 200 pieces, hidden by bus from Kampong Speu to distribute in Banteay Meanchey. The bus was stopped at 1 pm on February 4, 2024 on National Road 5 in front of Prek Ropov Primary School, Prek Ropov Village, Russey Krok Commune, Mongkul Borei District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
An official from the Production and Veterinary Office of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries said that at around 1 pm, officials from the Production and Veterinary Office arrived at the above point and stopped a yellow-blue bus with a license plate. Phnom Penh 3D-9090.
After inspecting the garage below, officers found 200 chicken eggs, equivalent to 60,000 eggs. Veterinary officials said that the truck stole chicken eggs, while the driver said that he was hired to transport chicken eggs from Udong district, Kampong Speu province to Moey for distribution in Banteay Meanchey only. He denied knowing the owner of the chicken eggs, only contacting the caller.
After inspecting the garden, the officers brought the evidence of the offense and the above-mentioned means to the Provincial Production and Veterinary Office to proceed with the procedure, because all the eggs are not properly documented and there is no source to transport them from anywhere. Come.
