(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, led a delegation of the Ministry of Information to meet and discuss with the Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation and Information led by Mr. Sous Yara, Chairman of the Fifth Committee of the National Assembly. Comments on the implementation of the political program and strategy of the first phase of the Royal Government of the 7th mandate related to the field of information and audio-visual.
Mr. Sous Yara clarified the purpose of the discussion and consultation on the implementation of the political program and strategy of the first phase of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate related to the information sector to help orient the Royal Government's policies and responsibilities. Right for the people.
With this, the President also mentioned the strengthening of cooperation between the legislature and the Ministry of Information as a strategic future in order to make the information strategy effective for the nation.
The Chairman of the Fifth Commission emphasized that the discussion on this occasion to hear the progress report of the Ministry of Information in the 7th mandate of the National Assembly to strengthen the quality of information towards the dream of Cambodia is a high-income country by 2050.
As a strategic direction on institutional management and institutional reform, the Ministry of Information must be deepened and must be a public relations institution of the Royal Government that is proactive, effective, efficient and effective in order to contribute to maintaining peace, political stability and Development.
To achieve this vision, the Ministry of Information has laid out a number of work sites to continue in-depth reforms, focusing on modern institutional and administrative modernization, strengthening institutional efficiency and quality of work, human resource development in the field of information and audio-visual, law enforcement. Cooperation with partners and protection of officials, adhering to the principles of compassion and ability to provide encouragement.
At the same time, the Ministry of Information has been working to maintain order in the field of information and audio-visual and to strengthen information security, which aims to ensure the right of citizens to access information, the quality of information and information security to prevent and combat false information and strengthen ethics. Biology As modern media has been acting as an important source of information for the public.
Both public and private media play an important role as a mirror of social reality and as part of ensuring the public's right to information and knowledge and engaging with the authorities in resolving issues in a timely manner to serve the interests of the nation and the people of Cambodia. .
In addition, the Minister outlined the White Paper for the development of the Ministry of Information in the next 25 years, including: the transition from analog to digital media, media development, professional training in journalism, the fight against fake news and Build legal bases and strengthen law enforcement.
The Minister of Information also presented the short, medium and long term plans to strengthen the Ministry of Information and the information sector.
During the meeting, the Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation and Information, as well as members of other committees of the National Assembly, praised the achievements of the Ministry of Information in the past five months for the caretaker government. Seventh, set out the direction to strengthen the work of information and audio-visual in Cambodia even better.
