The Cambodian Mine Action Authority requests Laos to join the 165th State Party of the Ottawa Convention as Cambodia chairs and hosts the 5th Review Meeting of the Convention
During the meeting, as chair of the Fifth Review Meeting of the Convention on the Prohibition of Anti-Personnel Mines (Ottawa Convention), Dr. Ly Thuch asked Laos to consider joining the 165th State Party of the Ottawa Convention while Cambodia will chair and host the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on a Mine-Free World of the 2024 Ottawa Convention in November.
The President of the Ottawa Convention 2024 also stated that the Lao side, as the President of Cambodia, will strive to mobilize resources and seek cooperation and assistance from development partners and donors to support Laos' demining activities in the event that Laos is a party to the Convention.
Cambodia is committed to supporting the Lao side to the best of its ability to clear mines and comply with the standards of the Ottawa Convention. At the same time, Dr. Ly Thuch also praised Laos' achievements in clearing cluster munitions.
The Lao Ambassador to Cambodia noted that November 2024 is a major international event that Cambodia will host and people from around the world will visit Siem Reap to attend the International Conference of the Ottawa Convention to Promote A world without mines. Laos is ready to attend the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit of the Ottawa Convention to be held in Siem Reap in November 2024.
