(Banteay Meanchey): A man who was good at chasing villagers in Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province, was arrested by the local police force of Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province and sent to court in connection with a case of intentional aggravated violence.
The suspect is Soy Sary, 33 years old, currently living in South Banteay Chhmar Village, Banteay Chhmar Commune, Thmor Puok District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
On February 3, 2024, Brigadier General Ouk Sophon, District Commander of the District Gendarmerie, led a force to detain a suspect based on a complaint by Ho Srey Phot, a female perpetrator of violence against the plaintiff. February 2, 2024 at Thmor Dek Ke village, Banteay Chhmar commune, Thmor Puok district.
Police confiscated a 63-cm-long wooden knife and a 29-cm-long black plastic knife.
After his arrest and interrogation, the suspect confessed that he had used a machete and a sharp knife to cut and stab the victim. Walking on his way, he always chases after people and shouts threats. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the district police force has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
The suspect has now been sent to the Provincial Court by the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Bureau on the morning of February 4, 2024 to follow the procedure.
Chinese New Year in Phnom Penh makes Chinese people miss their homeland very much
(Phnom Penh): Chinese people who are present in Cambodia expressed their nostalgia for their homeland while attending the traditional Chinese New Year celebration in Phnom Penh on February 2. Reminiscent of when the show was staged with pictures showing the Chinese New Year scene in their hometown.
Ms. Cai Vinping, a volunteer Chinese language teacher at the Confucius Institute at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, who participated in the exhibition of books and other materials that reflect the traditional Chinese identity of the program, told Cambodia-China Friendship Radio that the event It really means a lot to her because she misses her family in China so much.
Since 2024 is a year of people and people change, Ms. Cai Vinping invites more Chinese tourists to visit Cambodia because Cambodia is a country with a long history in the region like China, so she believes that Chinese people Really want to explore Cambodia, especially the "Great Angkor Wat" attracts visitors from China.
Ella, who is the Chinese host on the show, said she was "very excited" to attend the event because she missed her hometown so much. "I left my hometown about 4 years ago, so while attending this event, I miss my hometown, but in Cambodia as well as in Phnom Penh, I am happy because the Cambodian people are friendly and the colleagues are really nice. Regards.
On the occasion of the Chinese New Year, she wished her homeland and China more prosperity and prosperity, and the Chinese people will be happy, beautiful and lucky in life. She also hopes that this event will make Cambodians more aware of Chinese culture and traditions by inviting them to enjoy delicious traditional Chinese food. She believes that this arrangement will contribute to strengthening and expanding relations between China and Cambodia.
Such a celebration of "Traditional Chinese New Year" 2024 is also being held at the Olympia Shopping Mall in Phnom Penh on February 3.
