Farmers in Sangkat O'Kanthor, Stung Sen City smile as the price of rice sold per kilogram ranges from 1,150 Riel to 1,160 Riel
(Kampong Thom): Currently, dry season rice cultivation has made farmers busy harvesting to meet the needs of daily life, especially to increase household economic income and reduce imports.
Farmers in Sangkat O'Kanthor, Stung Sen City, Kampong Thom Province, smile happily as rice cultivation has increased and the price of rice is higher than this year, especially the price of rice sold per kilogram from 1,150 to 1 riel. , 160 Riels.
Mr. Chiv Kim Un, Chief of O'Kanthor Commune, said that in O'Kanthor Sangkat, 80% of the total population is 1,151 families, and farmers cultivate dryland rice twice a year. The land area in O'Kanthor commune is 4,436 hectares, but more than 1,400 hectares are farmers from outside the administration.
"Now we see that his farmers are very prosperous and he always praises the government, praises our authorities because the price of his rice has gone up," he said.
At the same time, Mr. Pen Vanrith, Director of Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that under the leadership of the Royal Government, efforts have been made to help farmers in the province continue to grow many secondary crops and fruits and vegetables. More to supply both livelihoods and markets to meet the needs of the total cultivated area of nearly 600,000 hectares, while the area for dry rice is 85,000 hectares.
This is an increase of 140% of the plan, an increase of more than 20,000 hectares due to the good price of rice, farmers have worked hard to grow crops and in the name of expertise to monitor farmers' yields. He said that after cutting off the feed, we have more than 640,000 tons of food left. Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha urges municipal, district and Khan administrations to be highly responsible in implementing the functions of the education sector that the Royal Government has transferred
The Royal Government has been piloting and learning from the transfer of education, youth and sports functions to the 14 municipal administrations in Battambang province since 2020.
Based on an assessment conducted by the inter-ministerial working group in 2023, the implementation of this mechanism has achieved remarkable positive results. Based on the results of this pilot implementation, the Royal Government has decided to expand this transfer to municipalities, districts and Khans throughout the country from 2024 onwards.
