(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Khin Nhean, Permanent Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee, Oddar Meanchey Province, on February 2, 2024, led a working group to provide loans, which are the budget of the Cambodian Red Cross to provide for poor families, families with disabilities and women. 50 widows in Chongkal district.
On that occasion, Mr. Khin Nhean sent a message from Mr. Pen Kosal, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee, Oddar Meanchey Province, who always pays attention to the well-being and living conditions of the people, especially the poor, widows. The disabled, the elderly, the homeless, the orphans, as well as the people affected by various natural disasters.
Mr. Khin Nhean said that the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Oddar Meanchey province has provided loans, which are the budget of the Cambodian Red Cross, as small loans to 50 families with disabilities, widows and poor families, in one case can get 1 loan. Million Riels without interest.
Mr. Khin Nhean confirmed that the loans provided to the poor people for various occupations at this time are not gifts and you can borrow up to one year without interest and have to repay. Every 6 months with 1 million Riel to be repaid twice, the first time for 6 months, 500,000 Riels and the second time for 6 months, another 500,000 Riels for the Cambodian Red Cross. Give it back to the poor for further loans.
He also called on our people, after receiving this loan, to work hard to expand their businesses such as agriculture and animal husbandry to improve family life.
