(Phnom Penh): Currently, the sex service business is considered an illegal business for most countries in the world, including Cambodia, but there are still some countries that allow people to run a legal business. . Are there any countries that still allow the operation of legal sex services?
Countries that still allow this service include:
New Zealand In 2003, the New Zealand government allowed people to run legal sex businesses. This business owner can get legal business rights under the Public Health Law and the Labor Law, which means that this business owner can get the same benefits and get the same rights as the employees in the labor sector. Other.
* Australia In this federal state, the operation of sex work depends on the state, with some states allowing legal business and others not.
Austria In Central Europe, sex work is legal throughout the country. Sex workers must be properly registered in advance, especially for health checks, taxes, and must be 19 years of age or older.
* In Bangladesh, in Asia, the government has made it legal for women to have sex, and all forms of sex work are legal, but for men, the government does not allow it.
In addition to these four countries, there are a number of countries that have easy access to sex work, even without a valid permit, including Japan, Thailand, Singapore, South Korea, China, Vietnam, Belgium, Brazil, Canada, Colombia, Ecuador, France, Germany, Greece, Indonesia. The Netherlands and so on.
