(Phnom Penh): Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has recommended a review of alcohol advertisements, especially billboards in public places. This instruction was made on February 2, 2024 in the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers.
Samdech Manet's recommendation comes after the recent tragedy of traffic accidents seems to increase alarmingly, in which most cases of accidents caused by drivers under the influence of alcohol. In each accident, there are always many deaths and injuries.
A press release on the outcome of the cabinet meeting stated, "The President has instructed the relevant authorities to review alcohol advertisements, especially billboards in public places, with appropriate restrictions. To contribute to reducing traffic accidents caused by driving under the influence of alcohol.
