The 10th World Cashew Conference 2024 was held for three days from 1-3 February 2024 in Siem Reap with the participation of senior government officials, the Ambassador of the European Union to Cambodia, and the Svay Sith delegation. Cashew World represents development partners and many national and international dignitaries.
Uon Siloth, President of the Cambodian Cashew Association, told Fresh News on February 2, 2024 that the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations, which ranked Cambodia third in cashew crops, was based on the amount of cashew production. Cambodia raw.
He said that in 2023, Cambodia produced more than 650,000 tons of cashew nuts, which shows that Cambodia's cashew production is the third largest in the world. The first country is Ivory Coast and the second is India.
Although Cambodia produces a lot of cashew nuts, Cambodia is not a processing country. The largest producers of cashew nuts are Vietnam, followed by India and Brazil.
He expects that Cambodia's cashew processing will be more than now, as the Cambodian Cashew Association is currently working to cooperate with stakeholders, attracting a number of investors to invest in cashew processing in Cambodia, including companies. Singapore's CSNC, Japan's Nirat and Cambodia's Cambodian Agrile Wood are in the process of running production lines.
According to the president of the Cashew Association, in 2021, Cambodia was ranked as the largest producer of raw cashew nuts in the world with a production of 1,180,000 tons. In 2022, it ranked second with 690,000 production.
