Minister of Environment unveils plans to save Tonle Sap Lake from rubbish and plastic bags as partners study feasibility
(Battambang): Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, highlighted the project to clean the surface of the Tonle Sap Lake from garbage and plastic bags, while a German organization is also helping to clean the plastic of the Tonle Sap Lake. Separately, an organization is also studying the feasibility and has agreed to study what the Tonle Sap Lake will be in 25 years and what preventive measures should be taken to preserve the Tonle Sap for generations to come.
This statement was made by Dr. Eang Sophalleth at a press conference following the visit of the EU Delegation to Cambodia, the German Ambassador to Cambodia and Member States for the first ForOurPlanet Campaign in 2024 at the Tonle Sap Biosphere Reserve. (TSBR)! Siem Reap and Battambang provinces on the afternoon of January 31, 2024.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth said: "I considered last week to clean the water. There are two types of water: 1: clean the plastic bags on the surface of the water, and the top priority is the Tonle Sap, because the fish world. "The Tonle Sap serves about 6 million of our people. If we lose fish due to pollution by plastic bags, we will lose a lot."
The Minister of Environment said that when the amount of plastic increases, the fish will become plastic and people who eat fish that contain microplastics will suffer from diseases caused by microplastics.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth said he had discussions with the German ambassador to Cambodia, including a German company helping to clean up plastics along the Tonle Sap Lake. The Minister of Environment said that if there is a plan to prevent the import of garbage and plastic bags in the 14 canals, the work to save the river from garbage and plastic bags will be more.
In addition, Dr. Eang Sophalleth also asked an organization to study the possibility of cleaning the river. "What will Sap become and what preventative measures are needed to preserve the Tonle Sap for generations as the world, as well as Cambodia, is facing climate change?"
The minister added that officials are also studying how many factories in Cambodia drain water into the Boeung Boeung River after a detailed study, and the ministry will set up a monitoring system for all factories to make sure. Water from the factory into the lake is good water does not pollute the environment because the quality of this water is very important for people.
The Tonle Sap Lake has played an important role in maintaining climate balance in the region, preventing and reducing floods, as a habitat for spawning fish, a rice barn area rich in biodiversity and rich natural resources. Each year, the Tonle Sap Lake absorbs about 20 percent of the flood water from the Mekong River.
Responding to the enormous importance of the Tonle Sap Lake to the entire Cambodian nation, the lake has been designated a nature reserve, categorized into multiple use areas. Institutions involved in the management of the Tonle Sap Lake include the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Interior, the Tonle Sap Authority and sub-national authorities around the Tonle Sap Lake.
With the above warning, Samdech Manipur Hun Manet instructed the working group led by Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction to clearly define the Tonle Sap Lake Conservation Land. The designation of Tonle Sap Lake conservation land must ensure accuracy, sustainability and efficiency.
Hun Manet stated that the Tonle Sap Lake Conservation Area must be protected in order to protect the reputation of the Tonle Sap Lake as the largest and richest lake. Provincial and district authorities around the Tonle Sap Lake play a central role in protecting the Tonle Sap Lake. Minister of Information calls on all ministries, institutions, private companies and the media to continue to support the development of Khmer boxing
