General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 72 suspects, 56 were arrested in 25 drug cases and 16 were arrested in 14 criminal cases.
US strikes Houthi group, firing on two targets in one day in the Red Sea
The United States has launched airstrikes on Houthi militants in Yemen, but the attack was not seen as a response to a retaliatory attack that killed three US soldiers and wounded more than 40 others. On a Tower22 basis. The Houthis on Jan. 30 fired missiles at two targets on the same day: a U.S. warship and a cargo ship.
The Yemeni Houthis have vowed to launch more attacks on US and British warships. The pledge was made in a statement on Wednesday, stating that US and British warships involved in the offensive against Yemen were the target of attacks.
The United States and Britain have repeatedly attacked Houthi targets in Yemen, setting up a multi-ethnic naval patrol to secure Red Sea waters. The Houthis continue to attack their targets in the Arabian Sea.
On Tuesday, January 30, the Houthis fired several missiles at the USS Gravely as US Central Command said U.S. forces fired a cruise missile. The Houthi attack is the 38th since November 19, 2023.
Yahya Sarea said the Yemeni Armed Forces had fired on a US cargo ship, the KoL, en route to Israeli ports. The same military spokesman confirmed the missile launch on the ship. The Houthis say there have been several explosions on the US merchant ship.
