(Phnom Penh): The spokesperson of the Cabinet of Prime Minister Hun Manet on the afternoon of February 1, 2024, issued a press release on the results of the meeting between Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Mr. Yoshihisa Suzuki, Chairman of the Business Cooperation Committee. Mekong-Japan of Japan Chamber of Commerce and Industry.
During the meeting, HE Hun Manet welcomed Mr. Yoshihisa Suzuki and the visiting delegation to Cambodia and expressed his pleasure at the current working meeting to strengthen the relationship between the Japanese Chamber of Commerce and Industry and the Kingdom. Cambodia, which has shown its contribution to the strengthening of Cambodia-Japan economic relations and the close people-to-people relations of the two countries.
On the occasion of the meeting, Mr. Yoshihisa Suzuki expressed his deep gratitude to the President for taking the time to allow him and the delegation to pay a courtesy call and express their gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia. Always pay attention to supporting Japanese companies' investment in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Chairman of the Committee informed the President about the activities of the Japan Chamber of Commerce and Industry, the largest economic and commercial institution in Japan, which currently has 515 offices and a total of more than 1.25 million members. Major in textiles, machinery and metals, energy, chemicals, food, housing, information technology and finance.
In addition, the Chairman of the Committee informed the President about the existing investment activities in Cambodia in the textile, gas supply and agriculture sectors, which focus on sesame and the purpose of his visit to find out. Develop the economy and opportunities for investment in Cambodia, especially the expansion of investment in the textile sector in the form of OEMs on textile materials that show the products made in Cambodia (Made In Cambodia).
The Chairman of the Committee also informed the President about the activities of the Mekong-Japan Business Cooperation Committee, an international committee of the Japan Chamber of Commerce and Industry, which is responsible for collecting information, conducting surveys and research studies. About the investment and business environment in Mekong countries, including Cambodia.
At the same time, the President also welcomed the interest of companies of the Japanese Chamber of Commerce and Industry who wish to further expand their investment activities. He also highlighted the attractiveness of the Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the incentive policy for investors and business people, which ensures a realistic, favorable and flexible investment environment.
Before concluding, the President sincerely hopes that the visit of Mr. Yoshihisa Suzuki and his delegation on this occasion will further increase the possibilities and expand the potential of further investment in Cambodia with confidence and realism. The Royal Government is always ready to coordinate and cooperate with Japanese investors in order to turn Cambodia into a major investment destination and a regional hub.
