(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda and the Governor of Prey Veng Province, Mr. Suon Somalin, on the morning of February 1, 2024, led a team of relevant officials to inspect the Vaiko River Station in Mohaleap Commune, Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province.
Mr. Un Chanda said that the Waiko River Pumping Station is a source of water pumped from a small river in Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province.
At present, due to Prey Veng province, there are 3 districts, 13 communes need water to save the dry rice of farmers located near the Waiko River Station, about 10,000 hectares.
Therefore, after the inspection by the two provincial authorities, it was decided to pump water from the small river through the Waiko River pumping station to supply to Prey Veng province, which needs about 20 million cubic meters of water and takes 16 days to pump water because the system This irrigation can take 3 days for the water to flow to Mesang district, Prey Veng province.
Mr. Un Chanda added that the pumping process will start on February 1, and the cost of pumping water will be borne by the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration. Courtesy and job discussion
