Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron Announces Implementation of Standard Learning Standards in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): In response to the spirit of the first meeting of the Council of Ministers of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, which set out four key measures to improve the quality of public schools from kindergarten to secondary school, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister On the morning of February 1, 2024, the Minister of Education, Youth and Sports presided over the announcement of the implementation of the model learning standard in Phnom Penh.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron added that the model school will focus on student achievement, with the school focusing on and determining student achievement using top-down and bottom-up mechanisms. On.
* The mechanism below is the Department of Education, Youth and Sports or the educational institution has the right to request a model school for the National Commission for evaluation. Provinces with more model schools will also be recognized as the director of the model department.
He added that during the 2023-2024 school year, the Ministry will select sample schools, which are about 500 to 1,000 potential schools, to receive support and evaluation, expected to meet school standards. Learn from the example of the next two years. In the near future, the Ministry will evaluate the selection of about 50 schools for the announcement at the education conference, which is scheduled to be held in early April 2024.
The Ministry has been developing mechanisms to promote the implementation of model schools and school support mechanisms through: Good Principals, Good Teachers, Specialists such as Curriculum, Assessment, Finance, and General Management, Resource Development Programs Lead schools and teacher development programs, first-grade math instruction and first-grade reading in primary school, and new teaching methods in secondary school.
Minister Hang Chuon Naron also stated that the implementation of the model school standard is a comprehensive school-level education reform, focusing on public educational institutions from kindergarten to high school in order to strengthen students' knowledge and morals. Better to get to higher education.
