(Phnom Penh): The Credit Guarantee Corporation of Cambodia (CGCC) has announced its continued support for small and medium enterprises in Cambodia by launching three individual credit guarantee schemes and six package credit schemes. Credit guarantee projects on bond issuance and capacity building programs for small and medium enterprises.
The decision to continue to support small and medium enterprises is the primary mission of providing credit guarantees to all targets to improve the financial environment and develop small and medium enterprises in the start-up and expansion of the enterprise. Small and medium as well.
He added that CGCC has launched three individual loan guarantee projects, six package loan guarantee projects, bond issuance credit projects and capacity building programs for small and medium enterprises.
Ros Silva, Secretary of State at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said that while the global economic model is changing, the CGCC has an important role to play in supporting small and medium-sized enterprises to have access to adequate financing to seize investment opportunities, increase employment and improve employment. Revenue aims to boost economic growth and achieve Cambodia's vision in 2030 and 2050.
He added that the CGCC must also be ready to support the development of the Cambodian securities market through the diversification of credit guarantees to the issuance of bonds to help increase the credit level of local bond issuers to be able to raise capital through Bond issuance on the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
At the same time, the CGCC also plays a role in developing credit guarantee mechanisms that lead to the development of financing mechanisms and financial products that can contribute to economic diversification and increasing competitiveness in line with the Pentagon strategy for growth, employment, and development. Equity, efficiency and sustainability.
As of December 31, 2023, after three years of operation, the CGCC has approved $ 164.72 million in loan guarantees for nearly 2,000 businesses nationwide, providing them with job opportunities. To more than 52,000 workers. The National Assembly will nominate two senators, and those who wish to run for office shall apply at the General Secretariat of the National Assembly.
