Russia's Defense Ministry says each side has rescued 195 soldiers and will fly to Moscow for medical and psychological treatment.
The RIA news agency reported that the United Arab Emirates played a key role in mediating the agreement.
"As a result of the January 31 talks, 195 Russian soldiers who were in danger of being taken prisoner of war have been repatriated from the occupied territories," the Russian Defense Ministry said in a statement. "Kiev regime in exchange for 195 prisoners of the Ukrainian Armed Forces were exchanged."
The two countries have been carrying out regular prisoner exchanges through intermediaries since the war began nearly two years ago, although no peace talks have been held between them since the first months of the conflict. The last and biggest change was on January 3, when a total of 478 prisoners were transferred after mediation by the United Arab Emirates.
