In 5 months, the campaign to reduce the use of plastic in Cambodia received the participation of more than 4.6 million people
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khvay Atiya, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that until Tuesday, January 30, participants will directly implement the campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use No plastic bags ”nationwide increased by more than 4,616,968 units / person.
The spokesman added that on January 30, 2024, a total of 66,846 people participated in the "Today I do not use plastic bags" campaign in 18 provinces: Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Speu, Kampong Thom. Kampot, Kandal, Kratie, Mondulkiri, Phnom Penh, Prey Veng, Pursat, Ratanakkiri, Preah Sihanouk, Svay Rieng, Takeo and Tbong Khmum provinces.
It should be noted that the campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags" began on September 1, 2023, with active participation in 44 schools, including a total of students. More than 1,800 people in Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province.
In addition, the campaign "Today I do not use plastic bags" has also started to participate in schools in other districts and provinces and reduce the use of plastic bags one day a week. Stop using it every day for beauty, start from school, lead a clean community and lead a clean Cambodia for the next generation.
The spokesman of the Ministry of Environment thanked on behalf of the Ministry of Environment to all ministries, institutions, Phnom Penh and all provincial administrations, including sub-national authorities, a number of development partners who have cooperated with the Ministry of Environment and paid attention to participate and promote. The campaign to reduce the use of plastics vigorously and successfully is a matter of pride.
Mr. Khvay Atiya once again called for more efforts to promote the priorities of environmental chakra strategies, including: clean, green and sustainable, with a particular focus on the "Today I do not use plastic bags" campaign to cultivate the mindset of Cleanness from the heart, from thoughts and attitudes, helps Cambodia, which is our home, all clean in the future and clean in the long run.
Mr. Khvay Athiya further called on all citizens to stop littering in public places and turn to proper care, especially the implementation of the 4Rs (denial of reduction, reuse and recycling) and participation. Stop using disposable plastic bags and completely eliminate them.
At the same time, the Ministry of Environment plans to proceed to the next step for the campaign under the theme "Today I do not use plastic", which received half of the country's people to participate in the practice of not using plastic bags. The second step of the campaign is to distribute bins to all schools and pagodas that can separate garbage, landfills, solid waste, plastic, garbage for processing, fertilizer and so on.
The next step is environmental clean-up, which focuses on cleaning plastic waste on the ground and in water and cleaning the air. In particular, the third step is to put in place to promote environmental protection, the beauty of Cambodia without pollution and lead to the gradual elimination of plastic waste from Cambodia in the future. Throughout 2023: The National Employment Agency (NEA) of the Ministry of Labor receives nearly 40,000 registered job seekers
